ryteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T02:12:05-07:00","id":924362,"title":"","content":"Nice! I love the crossover elements with Werewolf. I think I'll keep to the doctor archetype, but maybe change the background to better fit it to the setting. Probably keep the Path too, unless you consider that having restricted access to Spirit would slow the group down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T04:04:55-07:00","id":924385,"title":"","content":"Spirit is not the only Arcana that matters. Spirits that are materialized in the Fallen world can be interacted with using any physical or magical means, barring Numina. And a Thyrsus Mage can allow you to affect spirits in the Shadow. <br /> <br /> Spirits won't be the only antagonists, obviously. There are always Sleepers, Mages, and all sorts of goodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T06:00:27-07:00","id":924411,"title":"","content":"Cool! Keeping de Moros doctor in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T07:09:56-07:00","id":924431,"title":"","content":"I would like to play the author acanthus guy please. I will write up a much better backstory later today. I will also write up his family and friends and other parts of the backstory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","user":"wtaylorjr2001","date":". 07-01-2016, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T10:29:07-07:00","id":924523,"title":"","content":"The way it is looking now I will have that background and everything done tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T17:50:43-07:00","id":924693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wtaylorjr2001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=924523#post924523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way it is looking now I will have that background and everything done tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok! Hey, no immediate time pressure. I need everyone to post character concepts and make character sheets, too, before we could start. That might not happen as quickly because I know some people may want to change from their original submission. <br /> <br /> And as I said in the other thread, I'm out of town on vacation until July 10, so I may have less time to post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T23:41:20-07:00","id":924790,"title":"","content":"Reposting Sara with some background changes for the new location. Can I ask ohers to repost their characters, even if they're using the same concepts from before? (Makes it easier for me to check references for suggesting character ties.)<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Character concept/archetype: </b><br /> <br /> Sara Tath - 'Security Consultant' (Read, legalized hacker)<br /> <br /> Sara is something of a scandal in her home town. That might have something to do with the fact that she managed to plunge half the county into darkness when she was twelve and hacked into the electrical grid, marrying technical know how with being too young to really grasp the consequences of her actions. The FBI and NSA both took a certain interest at that point and she went through a lot of questioning to ensure she didn't have ties to untrustworthy elements.<br /> <br /> She also got a lot of warnings and restrictions, but at the same time, her skills received more positive attention and her education was watched and shaped by those who had found her and wanted to ensure she was kept under control and motivated to use them in more desired ways. Her childhood and youth was therefore an awkward time, people both angry at her, and envious at what she could do, and the tale of the 'Blackout' circulated for a number of years.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Awakening:</b><br /> <br /> Path: Obrimos<br /> <br /> Her Awakening came about after several weeks of toying with code and the most complex program she'd ever worked on, one that kept filing on her for reasons she couldn't grasp. It was designed to write it own code, to solve simple problems she put to it and to be adapt to find correct solutions. She lost herself in the shining, ever more complex code as it grew tangled and ensnared her like a web, systems flickering to life and dying around her as she felt more and more, like she was in a living creature.<br /> <br /> When she realized that everything she felt and sensed around her in the web as the living energy of both the physical and the digital world, her eyes finally opened.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Preferred game/player style:</b> I'd be very keen on exploring mysteries and seeking answers, as well as dealing with tough choices and philosophical quandaries.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T06:08:23-07:00","id":924858,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://orig03.deviantart.net/8d94/f/2008/335/c/a/ca7da8184c45ef4c45cb66ed052a037a.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Player: wtaylorjr2001</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Chronicle: </b>Mountains of Shadow</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Shadow Name: LUCKY DOG</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Sympathetic Name: Michael Korn</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Path: Acanthus<br /> Order: Mysterium<br /> Cabal:<br /> Legacy:<br /> <br /> Virtue: Generous<br /> Vice: Hasty<br /> Concept: Author<br /> <br /> Attributes<br /> Intelligence: 2<br /> Wits: 2<br /> Resolve: 2<br /> <br /> Strength: 2<br /> Dexterity: 3<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Presence: 3<br /> Manipulation: 2<br /> Composure: 4<br /> <br /> [5/3/4 distribution with extra dot put into Composure]<br /> <br /> Skills<br /> Academics:<br /> Computer:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Investigation: 2 (Interviewing) Order Skill<br /> Medicine:<br /> Occult: Arcadia 3 (First Dot Free) Order Skill<br /> Politics:<br /> Science:<br /> <br /> Athletics: 3 (Swimming)<br /> Brawl: 2<br /> Drive: 0<br /> Firearms: 1<br /> Larceny: 0<br /> Stealth: 0<br /> Survival: 0 Order Skill<br /> Weaponry: 1<br /> <br /> Animal Ken: 0<br /> Empathy: 0<br /> Expression: 3 (writing)<br /> Intimidation: 0<br /> Persuasion: 2<br /> Socialize: 3<br /> Streetwise: 0<br /> Subterfuge: 3<br /> <br /> <br /> Advantages<br /> Health: 7<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> Defense: 5<br /> Initiative: 7<br /> Speed: 10<br /> Size: 5<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 2<br /> Wisdom: 7<br /> Max Mana/Per Turn: 11/2<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> <br /> Hallow 2<br /> Safe Place 2<br /> Sanctum 2<br /> Shadow Name 3<br /> Resources 2<br /> Mysterium 1<br /> High Speech 1<br /> <br /> Arcana:<br /> <br /> Fate 3<br /> Time 3<br /> Space 1<br /> <br /> Praxes:<br /> Divination<br /> Exceptional Luck<br /> <br /> Rotes<br /> Postcognition<br /> Fools Rush In<br /> Choose the Thread<br /> <br /> <br /> Dedicated Tool<br /> Silver capped walking stick.<br /> <br /> Nimbus<br /> A somewhat Fae quality hits the air around him.<br /> <br /> Long-term:<br /> Strange Luck occurs such as someone rolling lucky seven seven times etc.<br /> <br /> Immediate:<br /> Time seems to run slower<br /> <br /> Signature:<br /> Peoples sense of time is off. One minute seems like an hour, etc<br /> <br /> Tilt:<br /> +1 composure, -1 Wits when around Doctor Luck's spellcasting<br /> <br /> Aspirations<br /> Scrutinize werewolves under magesight Short Term<br /> Compare Fate Interconnections of werewolves vs Human beings. Short Term<br /> Find out who is stalking him and what they want and deal with them Long Term<br /> <br /> <br /> Obsession<br /> Research paranormal activities and creatures such as werewolves, find out how they live day to day, what they eat, everythingabout them, and Write an Urban Fantasy Novel<br /> <br /> <br /> Equipment<br /> Old car<br /> android phone without sim card but with skype<br /> Idea notebook<br /> <br /> Experience<br /> Spirit 1 4pts<br /> Sanctum 1 1pt<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 1. Character concept and pre-Awakening life: Who are you? What defines your personality? Who are the important people from your Sleeper life?<br /> <br /> Michael Korn is a struggling author who has one book out. That book is a new york times bestseller. He spends most of his money learning new things to write about, so he is most often broke. He researches his books thoroughly. He became proficient at shooting firearms, swimming, rock climbing and more in order to write about the experience in detail. He is slowly building up an experience library of sorts that he can draw upon at need. He grew up on the streets so he can protect himself to a degree, but he is no bruce lee. His understanding of magic, on a deep and fundamental level was extraordinary. He could draw energy exceptionally well to the point where he could out do some disciples in power. Perhaps it was his unique creativity that forged a more pronounced link between him and Arcadia that allows him to draw more power, but whatever the reason, he is strong in the force.<br /> <br /> He is a quiet introverted man who almost lives in his books. He tries to fight against his introversion by putting himself in situations that force him to be extroverted. He can hide his introversion well. The most important people in his life is his family. He has a younger sister and mother and father. Whenever he gets a little ahead financially, his little sister would show up and do him in. Emily Blake is his first reader. She reads his work and tells him if it put her to sleep, or kept her up all night. Those are the only things he wants from her. She helps him perfect his craft.<br /> <br /> Michael is a world class athlete. He has learned so many new sports and such over the years, and excelled at them to write about them, he found himself one day swimming across currents that others would surf. He is almost an encyclopedia of occult knowledge. He has always been fascinated by the fae, fairies and elves. He was also fascinated by the world that they came from.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 2. Awakening: Please indicate what Path you want to belong to, and then a brief narrative description of your Awakening experience.<br /> I want to play an Acanthus mage.<br /> <br /> Michael loves to write, but sometimes his muse is absent and he cannot think of anything to write, he gets writer's block. One such time caught Michael and he decided to take a break from writing for a while and went to a local bar. He drank light, a light beer, and he drank slowly. There was a girl at the bar staring at him. He noded to her and she came over asking if the seat next to him was taken. He motioned for her to take a seat. He talked to her and learned that she is from out of town, but close, about a five hour drive. The evening drew on and he continued to drink with the girl he had just met. She said she recognized him from the back of one of his books. She took him, intending to go to her house with him. They got into her car and drove for hours. Somewhere along the drive, he passed out.<br /> <br /> He woke in a ditch, his clothes missing, and covered in dirt. A pile of dirt then splashed on his face and when he looked up he saw a man shoveling dirt on him. They were burying him alive. He didn't see the girl, the hole was at least ten feet deep and he was at the bottom. He stood up. He heard them say that he was awake and that was unfortunate. They shot him in the stomach.<br /> <br /> He realized that he was about to die in an unmarked grave this very night. He fell back from the force of the bullet and a tear came down his cheek, he didn't notice he was crying. This was all so unreal. This was wrong. His next thought was that everything was wrong. A lie. He heard them say that was it, they had shot him so they didn't need to finish the grave, no one would find him here.<br /> <br /> They left and the vines came. They did not grow as much as crawled down into the grave. Breathing heavy he hoisted himself up the vines and out of the ditch. Everywhere he looked there were thick clawing hedges that shred his clothes and his skin. The bullet hurt and the scratches from the hedges were getting deep. He was bleeding a lot. He felt a pull. He looked and saw in the distance, barely saw more like it, a tower. It was an Ivory Tower that called to him, that pulled him. He began to walk. There was a point where he could not go on and he fell into the razor sharp hedge cutting himself deep. That woke him and he stood up and walked.<br /> <br /> He didn't know how long the walk took, but he made it to the tower. He walked inside. He looked around and found no door to enter the tower, only this open waiting room. The walls were covered in names. He couphed and blood came out. He closed his eyes and sat down. Here is where he would die. He wasn't dead yet. He saw a spot that was empty on the wall and for some odd reason decided to add his name to the names on the wall. When his name showed up, he was back in the ditch. He clawed his way up. He didn't know how long he was in the grave but he was weak.<br /> <br /> He knew he needed to be found fast before he bled to death. He remembered shows where the cowboy was shot and he pressed against the wound to slow the bloodflow. He was bleeding from a bullet and gashes from the hedge. He needed help and immediate help. In his mind he focused on finding help, or help finding him. He formed a clear picture in his mind of him running into a hunter in these woods. It was a slim possibility that he focused on with all his might. And he walked, to try to get closer to the hunter. He didn't know how long he walked before he passed out.<br /> <br /> He woke in a hospital. He remembered everything and wondered at how lucky he was to be alive. When he asked the doctors told him some hunters found him bleeding to death in the middle of the forest.<br /> <br /> He spent a few weeks in the hospital before they released him. He went home and wrote furiously. As he wrote he found a change in himself. This world was a lie, and the truth could alter the lie. He formed a clear mental image of finding a lottery ticket on the ground. It was an odd experiment and he went out looking for a lottery ticket. He found nothing. He figured it was just his imagination, thinking he could do magic. Hours later, when he had forgotten about the experiment, he went to a convenience store for milk. Outside on the ground he found an unused lottery ticket. Was that his magic or just plain luck. He needed help to understand what was going on. He formed the mental image of a teacher and he meeting up. Where could he go.<br /> <br /> He went to a map, got a pencil, closed his eyes and stabbed the map with the pencil. Just outside of Denver Colorado was where he was going. He packed up things for a stay of about a month, and went to an area just outside of Denver to find a mentor to teach him about this thing of his.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 3. Preferred game/player style: What are you interested in accomplishing in this game, either for yourself or for your character? What would make this game the most fun for you?<br /> <br /> As I said before I like creating things. I like also creating situations, thinking on my feet as it were. I like the idea of fortune and its control. I like freedom within a span of possibility. I like the awakening story I wrote so please tell me if it is OK.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","user":"wtaylorjr2001","date":". 11-02-2017, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T00:00:29-07:00","id":925243,"title":"","content":"Have you heard from Chaos and Tambov?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","val