"content":"I get the feeling it's just the three of us at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T06:53:03-07:00","id":932492,"title":"","content":"I think you mean 4? ChaosArchon is the only one whom I haven't seen respond here. But that might change once I get more info up.<br /> <br /> My wife is out of town today and I have some miscellaneous errands to spend, but my goal is to get info up so we can get the game started this weekend. When I only have pockets of time, it's been easier to work on the other Mage game, so I want to take advantage of that down time today to get this one going!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T09:39:43-07:00","id":932541,"title":"","content":"I'm fine.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I make a quick mock up of Ain Soph update:<br /> Skills: Academics, Investigation, Occult, Science, Expression<br /> <br /> Yantras: TBD<br /> <br /> Attainments: (Supernal Vision, Wards and Signs, Supernal Dispellation; Exorcist's Eye, Ephemeral Shield, Craft Fetish)<br /> <br /> 1st: Word of Command (Instant)<br /> Know Spirit (Instant)<br /> <br /> 2nd: Supernal Vision (Instant, Non-Supernal)<br /> Exorcist's Eye (Instant, Gaunlet) (???)(stronger than Spirit Eyes)<br /> <br /> 3rd: Cleanse the Pattern (Instant)<br /> Ephemeral Shields (Instant, Spells/Gifts) (???)(Stronger than Spirit Armor)<br /> <br /> 4th: Wards and Signs (Instant, Advanced Duration, Potency Primary)<br /> Ephemeral Shield (Instant, Spells/Gifts, Physical Attacks) (???)(different from Honorary Rank)<br /> <br /> 5th: Supernal Dispellation (Lasting)<br /> Craft Fetish (Lasting)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T19:53:15-07:00","id":932745,"title":"","content":"Ok, I finally got a bunch of info up with extra notes about the setting, including larger Mysteries in Denver, Awakened politics, and some recent events.<br /> <br /> I would request at this time that no one begin as an initiate in a Legacy yet. This is partially because I don't think it makes sense for very recently Awakened mages, but also because I want to allow myself some time to wrap my head around Legacy rules before I introduce that aspect in-game. I didn't really explore Legacies at all in 1E, so I'm a bit behind in understanding all of the things they do.<br /> <br /> Please review the setting info and let me know if you have any questions/concerns. I'm now going to review each of your character backgrounds and stats, and I'll ask questions or make changes as needed to help you finalize your character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T20:22:10-07:00","id":932760,"title":"","content":"Here are some thoughts about the submissions so far.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2650\" data-vbnamecard=\"2650\">Retias</a><br /> I'm really digging the character concept still, and I think the Free Council is a great fit for my vision of how they'll fit into Denver politics. I agree that a regular familiar, rather than a Goetia as you initially discussed, is a great fit for both the character and the campaign. When you have time, try to put together a draft of the familiar's stats, numina, and bane, and add it to your character sheet.<br /> <br /> For my ease of tracking math, can you indicate which skills are Rote Skill specialties for your Order? You can just write (Rote Skill) or something like that next to each one. Also, you can add the free Order Status and High Speech merits to your list.<br /> <br /> In regards to your nimbus, I like the descriptions. Just a reminder, the nimbus tilt is something that will affect <i>other</i> people around Spider, not herself. The idea is that if they're studying her with Mage Sight and she casts a spell, or tries to intentionally flare her nimbus, it may apply that tilt to someone else temporarily. Giving someone else 8-again on computers is thematic, but may not be as relevant? What about something like giving someone else -1 Wits because they're confused by the obscure Supernal symbols floating around you?<br /> <br /> When you have time, please also add Aspirations (and indicate which are short vs. long term), Obsession, and any other Path/Order tools she might have already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T20:55:15-07:00","id":932774,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> <br /> By and large, I really like the narrative part of the new backstory you came up with. It seems more realistic to me, and adds some interesting room for plot hooks and questions about these mysterious people -- Why did he pass out? Why did they shoot him? Do they know he's not dead? Should be interesting to explore those questions.<br /> <br /> As for the stats themselves, though, I'm going to have to ask you to make some significant changes.<br /> <br /> Your overall character concept and story don't seem to be reflected in your choices for your stats. Having Dex 4, but only Int 2 and Presence 2 -- the attributes I would expect to be higher for a writer -- seems odd to me. Your choices for skills also have me confused. Your back story doesn't reference anything related to Crafts, but per the description of what each level of dots means, your character is &quot;outstanding&quot; - just shy of &quot;absolute mastery&quot; - at repairing or building things with his hands. Occult 4 is similarly too high for a newly Awakened character who otherwise has had no contact with supernatural creatures or true occult knowledge. Same issues with Athletics 4, which combined with your Dex/Wits gives your bestselling author a whopping Defense 7, and Subterfuge 4.<br /> <br /> It's not that you can't have these skills for your character; it's just that most of them really don't fit at all with the character you described in your backstory. With those stats and attributes, you seem on paper more like a spy or assassin who specializes in hand-to-hand combat. If you want to stick with the writer, I'd say prioritize mental and social skills, especially Investigation, Expression, Empathy, Socialize, and probably Occult (if you stick with the sci-fi/fantasy author idea you mentioned before).<br /> <br /> I am hesitant to let you have Gnosis 3 out the door. The main issue is that you have no merits to spend on things that would make most sense for your character concept. Without dots in Allies, Library, Resources, Contacts, or Professional Training, your best-selling author comes across as a &quot;one-hit wonder&quot; who got lucky on his novel, has little excess income (maybe sitting on loans or bills that take up all of his spare income?), and few important people in his life that he could turn to for help in a pinch. I would be fine with a lot more of these missing merits if your character concept was more of a washed-up author, or a fledgling author struggling to make his name known. So, I would personally suggest going Gnosis 1-2 and taking dots in other merits that make more sense for your concept, or keeping Gnosis 3 and updating your character concept description. If you drop Gnosis, make sure to drop 1-2 praxes as necessary.<br /> <br /> When you have a chance, you'll need to add your nimbus descriptions and create a nimbus tilt (p. 88-90). For Aspirations, I think those are usually more non-magical in nature, but you should at least pick 2 that could happen in a course of a single chapter (so over the course of a few days in game time) and 1 long-term aspiration. I would prefer Aspirations and Obsessions be based on <b>actions</b>, not outcomes for where to spend experience; otherwise you just get rewarded for spending experience, and that seems off to me. So for example, consider making &quot;Study Supernatural creatures&quot; closer to something like &quot;Scrutinize a werewolf using Mage Sight&quot; or &quot;Interact with a spirit materialized in the material world.&quot; For your long-term Aspiration and Obsession, similarly try to pick an action your character wants to pursue or a Mystery he wants to explore/solve.<br /> <br /> Let me know if you have any questions/concerns about my feedback, or if I can help you make the changes in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T21:05:48-07:00","id":932777,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> <br /> I think you should have 1 more Social skill dot, if you get one for free from Professional Training. Does that mean you picked Persuasion as your third Asset Skill, per Professional Training 3? Because you can only put the free dot from Professional Training 4 in one of your Asset Skills.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of your white coat as your Dedicated Tool! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You might want to include some kind of scalpel or other medical device in your equipment as a Path or Order tool, yeah?<br /> <br /> For your Aspirations, remember that 2 should be short-term (able to accomplish in a few days in game time at most) and 1 should be long-term. I'm not sure which of yours are short or long; could you review them and update if needed, and maybe indicate those? Also, can you make your Obsession more specific?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T21:28:28-07:00","id":932782,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a> <br /> Props to making me need to Google &quot;cryptozoology&quot; to know what that meant. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You'll probably still need to remind me when you think that applies to your Occult rolls.<br /> <br /> For Stealth, I'm on the fence but feel like you might need to pick a different or more specific skill specialty. I'm having a hard time thinking of situations where that one <i>wouldn't</i> apply. If you disagree, let me know.<br /> <br /> For the Hobbyist Clique merit, just update your character sheet with the final decision when you settle on one. Since we already are starting with everyone in an Order, you'll need to replace that Aspiration.<br /> <br /> For the ATV, I have no idea. I'll say you can have one at Resources 2, as that strikes me as something a person with a &quot;comfortable, middle class wage&quot; could afford.<br /> <br /> You still need make the nimbus descriptions and nimbus tilt, and pick 6 dots' worth of rotes. Otherwise, just try to flesh out a little bit more of your character's background when you have time. Maybe come up with some names of the drinking buddies or other interesting things I could use as plot hooks, to help me better understand who Phil is as a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T21:42:02-07:00","id":932784,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to say that there's a Simurgh in my home game too, and seeing it as a shadow name again after I just encountered the word for the first time is low key freaking me out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T03:59:51-07:00","id":932861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=932777#post932777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a><br /> I think you should have 1 more Social skill dot, if you get one for free from Professional Training. Does that mean you picked Persuasion as your third Asset Skill, per Professional Training 3? Because you can only put the free dot from Professional Training 4 in one of your Asset Skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the Asset Skills are Science and Medicine, but with the third dot of Professional Training I took Persuassion as athird Asset Skill. But you are right, I missed 1 dot. I've put it in Expression, so he is more articulate and can write better papers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really like the idea of your white coat as your Dedicated Tool! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You might want to include some kind of scalpel or other medical device in your equipment as a Path or Order tool, yeah? </div> </div> </div>Ha, yeah! An scalpel was my idea for a Path (weapon) Tool. It's sort of a knife, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For your Aspirations, remember that 2 should be short-term (able to accomplish in a few days in game time at most) and 1 should be long-term. I'm not sure which of yours are short or long; could you review them and update if needed, and maybe indicate those? Also, can you make your Obsession more specific? </div> </div> </div>Updated and changed, I left one Aspiration slot free for posible plot objectives that may appear, because I can't think of any short term Aspiration right now.<br /> <br /> By the way, take another look at my char, I changed the folowing:<br /> <br /> Shadow Name: Ouroboros Ophis<br /> <br /> Backstory and Daily life: He now teaches medicine at the university, while his wife works at Denver's Children hospital.<br /> <br /> Arcana: Life 3 Death 2 Matter 1 (unless you prefer that I refrain from making an out of path Arcanum my best)<br /> <br /> I'm still lacking Rotes, I'll work on that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T06:20:52-07:00","id":932877,"title":"","content":"Ok. For my convenience with double-checking math, can you indicate on your sheet which skills are asset skills and your Order rote skill specialties? So maybe behind them, put (Rote Skill) or (Asset Skill), or use *, +, etc. next to the name and a key for which symbols mean what.<br /> <br /> Scalpel is totally fine as a weapon Path tool! And you can use it as a literal weapon, just like a knife, in a pinch.<br /> <br /> Some ideas for other short-term Aspirations (remember, these can be things you want for your character, even if <i>he</i> wouldn't wish it on himself): Interact with a werewolf, study a dead body, witness a killing, study an object in Twilight, etc.<br /> <br /> I was about to say that the rules won't let you start with the 3rd dot in a non-Ruling arcanum. Turns out I was wrong! As long as you only have 3 dots in one arcanum, and 3-5 are spent in Ruling arcana, you're good. Now, remember that any improvised casting from Life spells will cost you 1 additional mana, so many people prefer to put them into Ruling arcana simply because it's more efficient and makes sense. But you're welcome to distribute them however you like as the rules allow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T06:25:33-07:00","id":932880,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I will add the Rotes and note the Asset and Rote Skills.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> <br /> <i>Rote Skills are in cursive</i><br /> <br /> <u>Asset Skills ar underlined</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 07-17-2016, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T06:47:21-07:00","id":932883,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks! As far as I can see, everything with Ouroboros Ophis (try saying that ten times fast, hah) is ready to go. I think I can introduce some NPCs through your healing in the Awakened community -- probably some mages who've gotten into &quot;scuffles&quot; with werewolves or spirits and need some patching up. If you have any ideas for some specific NPCs that you'd like to add, pitch the ideas here. Some of them could fall under your Contacts merit from Professional Training, although I would expect most of those to include patients at the University of Colorado-Denver medical school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T07:12:56-07:00","id":932890,"title":"","content":"Well, I wouldn't mind the ocasional wolf-blooded or regular human from a pack to be a patient too (Werewolves kinda don't need doctors :P Well, until I get Life 4 and can heal Aggravated damage, now that's a bargaining chip). He takes his Hypocratic Oath very seriously and will help anyone in need.<br /> <br /> As for Contacts, yeah, I was thinking regular folk for patients. Supernatural creatures, I think, defeat the purpose of the Merit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T09:50:15-07:00","id":932943,"title":"","content":"I am not on the Internet now, I will put up the corrections Monday, Tuesday at absolute latest. I am sorry about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T10:59:29-07:00","id":932973,"title":"","content":"All changes added in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T11:48:27-07:00","id":932983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wtaylorjr2001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=932943#post932943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not on the Internet now, I will put up the corrections Monday, Tuesday at absolute latest. I am sorry about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally fine! Real life trumps gaming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Any questions about my comments, or are those fair points?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T03:58:50-07:00","id":933352,"title":"","content":"Added the Aspiration: Learn about alternative medicine (Tai Chi, Acupuncture, etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T13:31:46-07:00","id":933559,"title":"","content":"First thanks for working with me, and sorry it is taking so long. Next I could use some help on creating nimbus tilts, obsessions and aspirations. Sorry for getting to you so late. Next I went over the character and I agree with you. I was trying to make the previous character fit here. He was a world class athlete. This character is also an athlete, but hopefully more inline with a struggling artist concept. He is struggling because all the money he makes goes into experience training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T15:26:49-07:00","id":933609,"title":"","content":"If your Nimbus is somewhat Fae-like, maybe the Tilt could be a -1 to Wits as people become distracted by the magic, for example. The specifics of the Long Term, Inmediate and Signature are more complicated. What exactly is a Fae air? When I hear those words the first thing that crosses my mid is glamour (hence the proposed tilt), but maybe you meant something else entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T03:57:21-07:00","id":933797,"title":"","content":"I added Rotes and free Merits. Will decide on HC randomly.<br /> <br /> One of his buddies should be Persian or Kurdish.<br /> <br /> I also volonteer to handle legacy crunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T06:47:48-07:00","id":933846,"title":"","content":"Reviewing characters again to see how things are coming.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2650\" data-vbnamecard=\"2650\">Retias</a><br /> Looks like you're just about done here! Thanks for making the changes. The only thing that I see is I'd like to make a few tweaks to the familiar. I made some comments about this in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=925384#post925384\">the other OOC thread</a>, but for a rank 2 familiar, I'd like to start with 11 attribute dots and 4 numina. I will grant additional dots to the familiar as you gain experience, which you can use to help develop the familiar.<br /> <br /> So, to make the changes, I'd like you to add 1 more numina and drop 3 of the attribute points (you're at 14 total currently). Per RAW, you can also stick at 3 numina and add 1 more dot to an Influence domain.<br /> <br /> In terms of ban and bane (p. 255-256), since you're going with rank 2, let's make those more obscure and potentially serious. I'll make some suggestions, which you can either keep or pick something else along a similar vein.<br /> <br /> Ban: The machine spirit must corrupt a computer at least once per month, or lose all Willpower.<br /> Bane: Rainwater collected during a thunderstorm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> <br /> Looking much better. A few more suggestions/tweaks.<br /> <br /> You actually have 1 more attribute dot to put in somewhere. They should be a 3/4/5 split + 1 bonus for Resolve or Composure. I think when you went back and tweaked those, you forgot to add the bonus dot. For skills, you seem to be missing Skill Specialties now; pick 3 related to skills of your choosing. Please also indicate your Rote Skill Specialties for your Order (Investigation, Occult, Survival for Mysterium).<br /> <br /> I am ok with you having Gnosis 3. Your character is going to begin poor. You can't start with any equipment that would be higher than availability 1. You can have an apartment or home, but it's cramped and not great quality. You could have a beat-down vehicle if your character would have one. Because you have Gnosis 3, mark on your sheet that your max mana is 13 and your max mana/turn is 3. You also need to pick a second Obsession, as characters with Gnosis 3 start with 2 of those in play.<br /> <br /> For rotes/praxes, this is your call, but you might not want Exceptional Luck as both a praxis and a rote. You can't have both qualities on any given roll; either you use it as a rote, or you use it as a praxis. Because some of the benefits overlap, it's probably smarter to pick different options, but that's your call.<br /> <br /> For the nimbus, your tilt can have a total of +2 bonuses or penalties to attribute or dice rolls. Remember that these will apply to other characters who view you casting a spell, not to yourself. Check out p. 88-90 for details, with info about creating nimbus tilts on p. 90. For the &quot;fae quality&quot;, you could give something like -1 Composure, -1 Wits as onlookers find themselves befuddled by the aura of Arcadia around you. Just an idea.<br /> <br /> As I said before, please make your Obsessions and Aspirations more specific, and specify which Aspirations are short- vs. long-term.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> <br /> As far as I can tell, I think you're all set. Let me know if I missed something or if you have any questions!<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a> <br /> As I suggested before, I'm iffy on &quot;moving quietly&quot; as a skill specialty. Can you clarify, pick something different, or tell me why you think it's a specialty? It seems pretty broad in scope.<br /> <br /> Please create the familiar using the guidelines I suggested above for Retias, except for rank 1 (so 6 attribute dots, 2 numina). Ban and bane should be fairly common things.<br /> <br /> Still missing nimbus info and tilt. Let me know if you need help with this.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm waiting to hear from ChaosArchon still. If I haven't anything by the time the rest of you are wrapping up with character creation, we'll start without him. He can potentially join later, if he still chooses to. Otherwise it'll be a 4-player game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T08:50:15-07:00","id":933921,"title":"","content":"Almost done,I need another obsession, taking suggestions. I have research arcadia space and time, but I believe it is too broad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T14:28:32-07:00","id":934094,"title":"","content":"My familiar is now suitably tweaked. I wasn't sure of what other numina might fit, so I took another point in an Influence. (I'm happy to take suggestions though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T14:57:10-07:00","id":934117,"title":"","content":"I would like to have a picture to see how Spider is suposed to look. I changed mine a bit, being younger than originally intended (40 rather than 50).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T22:41:15-07:00","id":934304,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I added a picture in for her. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T23:33:18-07:00","id":934313,"title":"","content":"Nice! Thanks, Retias..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:43:15-07:00","id":934365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I suggested before, I'm iffy on &quot;moving quietly&quot; as a skill specialty. Can you clarify, pick something different, or tell me why you think it's a specialty? It seems pretty broad in scope. </div> </div> </div>Moving Quietly is actually a sample in the core D:<br /> <br /> I won't apply if Phil is being searched for by sight or scent.<br /> <br /> How about Moving in Woods?<br /> <br /> 6 Attributes, 2 Numina for Familiar, got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T05:36:35-07:00","id":934421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=934365#post934365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Moving Quietly is actually a sample in the core D:<br /> <br /> I won't apply if Phil is being searched for by sight or scent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, yeah, fair point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That one wasn't listed in the Mage 2E book, but I reviewed the CoD book and you're totally right. You can totally keep it. I guess I was making assumptions about what the whole purpose of stealth should be without thinking that it doesn't always entail moving quietly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T05:49:16-07:00","id":934428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Retias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=934094#post934094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My familiar is now suitably tweaked. I wasn't sure of what other numina might fit, so I took another point in an Influence. (I'm happy to take suggestions though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>You can always pick Numina that are generally useful, even if they don't necessarily reflect the familiar's type of spirit. For example, you could have a Blast that narratively consists of an electric shock or bolt of energy. That certainly would help in combat.<br /> <br /> I also think Computer Code is quite narrow for Influence. I think something like &quot;Technology&quot; or &quot;Electronic devices&quot; would be totally fine. If I were creating a machine spirit, I would probably have Influence over &quot;electronic devices&quot; and &quot;metal.&quot; You're welcome to use those if you think they fit what you're looking for. If you're going to invest 4 merit dots in the familiar, it should be pretty sweet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T06:40:59-07:00","id":934453,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> - I reviewed your character sheet and I think it looks a lot better! Thanks for continuing to work with me and making those changes.<br /> <br /> The nimbus stuff looks great. Thanks for adding those details. I like the Aspirations and Obsessions, and I don't think they're too broad. The only thing I can think of is that 2 of your Aspirations include werewolves, which overlaps with your first Obsession. I would probably just give you Beats (rather than Arcane Beats) for those actions.<br /> <br /> I think you're all set to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T13:33:02-07:00","id":934686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=934428#post934428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can always pick Numina that are generally useful, even if they don't necessarily reflect the familiar's type of spirit. For example, you could have a Blast that narratively consists of an electric shock or bolt of energy. That certainly would help in combat.<br /> <br /> I also think Computer Code is quite narrow for Influence. I think something like &quot;Technology&quot; or &quot;Electronic devices&quot; would be totally fine. If I were creating a machine spirit, I would probably have Influence over &quot;electronic devices&quot; and &quot;metal.&quot; You're welcome to use those if you think they fit what you're looking for. If you're going to invest 4 merit dots in the familiar, it should be pretty sweet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Adjustments made. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T15:24:44-07:00","id":934731,"title":"","content":"Thank you for working with me. I am inexperienced when it comes to playing mage. I only read the rules. But I like the system, it is open to creativity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T03:09:57-07:00","id":934976,"title":"","content":"I updated the Familiar; needs stats for the frog Fettered to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T03:48:39-07:00","id":934983,"title":"","content":"There are animal stats listed here, if those might help. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xMwKNrnxhEuCQjP1qStbxl-C4JIyRmT1D4FVgSqjmpo/edit#heading=h.x2uk4pvnusiq\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...h.x2uk4pvnusiq</a><br /> <br /> No frogs, but there is a toad. (Has no idea what the difference is between frogs and toads)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T12:52:38-07:00","id":935748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Retias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=934983#post934983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Has no idea what the difference is between frogs and toads)</div> </div> </div> </div>Frog: small, smooth, lives mostly in water.<br /> <br /> Toad: bigger, warty, sometimes poisonous, lives mostly on land (when adult).<br /> <br /> There're poisonous frogs too, but they live in the tropics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T13:06:11-07:00","id":935756,"title":"","content":"For purposes of game mechanics, you can use the Toad stats. Thanks for sharing, Retias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>