":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T06:55:38-07:00","id":943587,"title":"","content":"I edited my post for clarity, Two reaches of which one is for instant casting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">Spider</span><br /> <br /> It takes 3 hours for a ritual, you would be an hour late for the meeting if you cast a ritual spell. Instant spell casting is fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","user":"wtaylorjr2001","date":". 08-04-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:37:18-07:00","id":943828,"title":"","content":"FYI everyone, I'm swamped today and the next few days because I'm moving. I might be delayed in replying or making posts. Sorry in advance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T20:17:47-07:00","id":944094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wtaylorjr2001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=943587#post943587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I edited my post for clarity, Two reaches of which one is for instant casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the rules of spell stacking (p. 118), you can't cast Exceptional Luck multiple times and get boons from each. I'm going to ignore your second roll. <br /> <br /> The good news is that as an exceptional success, you get 1 WP back (moot point here as you're full) and can allocate the bonus to potency. You have Potency 4 for the boon, so you can take Charmed, Steadfast, and 2 mundane rolls with the 9-again property. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:red\">Spider</span><br /> It takes 3 hours for a ritual, you would be an hour late for the meeting if you cast a ritual spell. Instant spell casting is fine. </div> </div> </div>This is accurate. Spider could text the others and just show up late if she prefers.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2650\" data-vbnamecard=\"2650\">Retias</a> - As for the familiar, I asked around on the main Mage board to ask for clarification about familiar Manifestation Effects and most people suggested either Fetter + Unfetter (like I suggested) OR just use Possession. For generally manipulating technology, The Machine could just use its Influence effects. For finer details or nuanced manipulation, it could possess the technology outright. Unfetter only temporarily releases the fetter bond; if the spirit wanders away from its fetter for more than an hour, it goes dormant. In that sense, you can maintain more control over the familiar, but The Machine might resent you and require more convincing to help you. If you just use Possession and something else you like, The Machine will have more freedom and flexibility to roam, but that means less control and higher risk of harm to it. Kind of like using a shock collar on a dog versus letting the dog roam freely. Both have their benefits, but I need to know what you would prefer to have. If you take Possession and drop Fetter/Unfetter, you get a second Manifestation effect to pick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Typo 08-05-2016, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T23:58:12-07:00","id":944160,"title":"","content":"Ah, sorry, I thought I answered you. Possession would be fine, in that case. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And Spider may be a bit late, but she'll be at the meeting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:40:58-07:00","id":946275,"title":"","content":"Everything is perfect just one thing, it was Steadfast and Charmed, not Inspired and Charmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:04:57-07:00","id":946293,"title":"","content":"Yep, my bad. I'll edit my post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T00:04:59-07:00","id":947573,"title":"","content":"I'll post with Sara when her late arrival makes sense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:19:40-07:00","id":947686,"title":"","content":"Eh, the hour isn't so important in this case. Just go ahead posting that you're the last to arrive and that you show up late. This is more of a transition scene to give you all a chance to get together. I'd rather just keep the game moving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T08:27:42-07:00","id":947795,"title":"","content":"Slight mistake of omission. I have 3 potency so it will be Charmed, Steadfast and one nine again roll(mundane)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T09:59:58-07:00","id":947830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wtaylorjr2001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=947795#post947795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slight mistake of omission. I have 3 potency so it will be Charmed, Steadfast and one nine again roll(mundane)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you were right the first time - you have Potency 4.<br /> <br /> Potency is the primary spell factor. Upon successfully casting the spell, you may increase the Potency by 1 stage for each dot in the associated Arcanum, minus 1. The spell starts with Potency 1 by default, so basically you get a maximum free Potency equal to your dots in Fate (3 in this case).<br /> <br /> Then, you scored an exceptional success because you used your Praxis and scored at least 3 successes. With an exceptional success on the casting roll, you can pick one bonus from a list on p. 115 (also listed on p. 328). You chose the option to gain a free increase in the spell's primary spell factor, so that brings you up to Potency 4.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Luck states that you can mix and match boons equal to the spell's Potency, so 4. You picked Charmed, Steadfast, and 2 uses of 9-again rolls on mundane actions.<br /> <br /> I know these rules are complicated as we're learning them, but I'm pretty sure you'll be using this spell a lot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> so I'm sure we'll figure it out with practice.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, in regards to the spell you're trying to cast on the group. I think you're forgetting the rules on spell control, and on the scale factor.<br /> <br /> If you want to give each member of the cabal a blessing of Exceptional Luck, you can either cast it on each mage individually, or you can cast it one time and include everyone as a target. If you cast them individually (like you did in your post), then you need to refer to the rules on spell control on p. 118:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p. 118</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage can have as many active spells as she has dots in Gnosis. Each additional spell requires a Reach, plus another Reach per spell already over the limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You already have Exceptional Luck cast on yourself, so if you try to hold onto additional spells for each cabalmate, that last one is going to require a Reach because you'll be over your spell control limit (3, for your Gnosis 3), <b>and</b> you'll have to spend 2+ reach for every spell after that one for the rest of the duration of those spells. I don't recommend this.<br /> <br /> The better approach is to either take -4 and increase the standard scale factor to include 4 subjects, or to use 1 Reach for the Advanced Scale factor (which affects up to 5 subjects simultaneously). As discussed above, the spell will have Potency 3 by default unless you increase the Potency factor on the spell.<br /> <br /> If you wanted, you could release the Exceptional Luck spell that you currently have active on yourself, and just include yourself and the other cabalmates in the same spell. That way you each get the boon, but it only takes 1 active spell. It's your call.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 08-10-2016, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T12:51:08-07:00","id":947966,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't be it easier to just add Target Factors so it only &quot;fills&quot; one of Dr, Luck's spell slots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:02:39-07:00","id":947978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=947966#post947966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't be it easier to just add Target Factors so it only &quot;fills&quot; one of Dr, Luck's spell slots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. That's what I meant by this part:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=947830#post947830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The better approach is to either take -4 and increase the standard scale factor to include 4 subjects, or to use 1 Reach for the Advanced Scale factor (which affects up to 5 subjects simultaneously). As discussed above, the spell will have Potency 3 by default unless you increase the Potency factor on the spell.<br /> <br /> If you wanted, you could release the Exceptional Luck spell that you currently have active on yourself, and just include yourself and the other cabalmates in the same spell. That way you each get the boon, but it only takes 1 active spell. It's your call.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm misunderstanding your question (or the rules)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:12:32-07:00","id":948097,"title":"","content":"It seems I messed up this time. Well like you said I'm still learning. I keep omitting things. I was casting the spell as a rote because I wanted the extra dice. It was an experiment to get a feel for the probabilities. The rote allows me to use Occult 3 as a mudra. I totally forgot about the number of active spells rule. I will pay one willpower to release the spell I have and make a group spell like you said. I think it would be better to cast this as a praxis. I am amending the post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:54:02-07:00","id":948143,"title":"","content":"Hey man, no worries. FYI, you don't need to spend WP if you just want to end a spell you're in control of. You can do that as a reflexive action at no cost. The WP option is for making a spell remain in effect for the remainder of its duration, but outside of your active control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T11:13:18-07:00","id":948708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=948657#post948657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dr. Luck</b><br /> You can give yourself 1 mana back instead, per the rules on exceptional spellcasting rolls. (I believe that you don't get both points back because those were spent on mitigating Paradox, not technically the casting of the spell itself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaveB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cowl is short on Willpower (he has three points left) after a Mage Sight and a desperate Dispellation the night before (events which will be revealed in the fullness of time). <b><i>He has seven Mana remaining</i></b>, after he requisitioned time with a Hallow from the Guardians. Also pertinant to these spells, he has Gnosis 3 and Fate 4. And Wisdom 5, but that comes later.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> The next spell is<br /> <br /> <b>Shared Fate (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <i>Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Composure<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine, Persuasion, Politics<br /> Fate is an instrument of both justice and punishment. This spell braids the fates of two subjects together. Whatever befalls one subject affects the other.<br /> Whenever one subject suffers damage, a Tilt, or an unwanted Condition, any others suffer it as well. If the number of subjects spell factor is not increased when casting this spell the mage herself is treated as one.<br /> +1 Reach: The link instead only works one way for one of the subjects \u2014 such that the subject suffers harm inflicted on the others but not the reverse.<br /> +2 Reach: The subject is not linked to the mage or any other specific subject. Instead, she suffers any damage, Tilt, or unwanted Condition she inflicts, regardless of whom she harms.</i><br /> <br /> First, the good news. The spell is Withstood, but Cowl knows how weak Ivan's mind is after his last spell, and Jon knows that his Potency will be sufficient without taking dice penalties. <span style=\"color:blue\">Again with the playtest, Dave notes that the spell should probably do one instance of harm per Potency, but that won't matter here, as three - combined with the spell Cowl just cast - will be quite sufficient</span>. He will take the -4 dice to make it last a week, though.<br /> <br /> Now the downsides. This is going to <i>hurt</i>, Paradox-wise. One Reach for instant casting, one for sensory range, one for Advanced Duration, three to activate <i>both</i> of the spell's Reach clauses... That's a whopping eight Paradox dice (2 each for 4 Reach over the limit). Plus one for this being Cowl's second Paradox roll of the scene. <span style=\"color:blue\">Dave underlines the &quot;it isn't obvious *when cast*&quot; note in his playtest file</span>. Reduce that by 2 for using the coin again, and it's still seven dice. That could knock Cowl unconcious or leave him with a nasty Paradox Condition (or, if he chooses to not contain it, potentially summon a Gulmoth. Yeah, he doesn't even think about that).<br /> <br /> So he throws Mana at it. His Gnosis lets him spend three Mana a turn, his casting is going to take two turns anyway, so <i><b>he spends six Mana</b></i> to reduce the Paradox pool to a single die. Jon considers making it a chance die, but he wants to keep one last Mana in case there's a fight later and Cowl needs his Mage Armor.<br /> <br /> Dave rolls the Paradox die. It's a 10. (not making this up, I really did roll 2 tens on 2 seperate single-die rolls), but the reroll is a 4. Cowl attempts to contain it, succeeds with 4 successes, and Cowl takes another resistant bashing wound.<br /> <br /> Then the spell itself. Base dice pool of 7, -4 for advanced duration, +4 for all the yantras. Spend another Willpower to make it ten dice.<br /> <br /> Jon rolls six successes. An Exceptional Success! Dave can't be arsed to think of a Condition, so the group just get an Arcane Beat and Cowl gets a Willpower back, and then Jon consults the list of things he could do with the exceptional success. Make it Potency 4... Nah. Make it Advanced Potency... He doesn't think anyone's going to try to Dispel it. Inflict a Condition on Ivan on top of the spell... Maybe, but... <i><b>Refund all Mana spent on the spell plus one.</b></i> AHa!<br /> <br /> <b><i>Jon records that Cowl now has eight Mana left.</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:25:59-07:00","id":948743,"title":"","content":"Sure, works for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:41:12-07:00","id":949927,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the late post, work was eating at me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T07:54:17-07:00","id":950031,"title":"","content":"I decided to retroactively spend 1 extra Reach I forgot about, and Roll for 'dox. 1 B, dox contained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T08:44:03-07:00","id":950053,"title":"","content":"If someone else casts a spell on you, does it count against your active spells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T09:07:54-07:00","id":950069,"title":"","content":"Such as in sustaining a beneficial spell on you? It wouldn't, it only counts against their limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T10:40:27-07:00","id":951196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wtaylorjr2001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=950053#post950053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone else casts a spell on you, does it count against your active spells?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Retias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=950069#post950069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such as in sustaining a beneficial spell on you? It wouldn't, it only counts against their limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Retias has it right. This is a new rule compared to 1E. In the last edition, you could cast spells on someone else to get in the way of their spell control and cause penalties on their rolls. Now, spell control and limits are only for spells under <i>your </i>control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T05:33:57-07:00","id":952442,"title":"","content":"What Practice do I need to stabilize the wounded? Compelling, Ruling, Perfecting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:49:34-07:00","id":952511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=952442#post952442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Practice do I need to stabilize the wounded? Compelling, Ruling, Perfecting?</div> </div> </div> </div>My gut says that it would probably be Ruling, or maybe even Shielding (2-dot), at least for Life. There is a comparable Time 2 spell (Veil of Moments, p. 188) that would &quot;pause&quot; someone who is bleeding out, so I'd say 2 dots is plenty to do that. If you were actively healing someone, that would be Perfecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T09:56:59-07:00","id":952576,"title":"","content":"That spirit stuff sounds fine Rwknoll. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Spider will explain her findings en route, but I'll hold off on my next IC post until the others have had chance to respond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:07:43-07:00","id":952584,"title":"","content":"I think I'll wait until Luck's player posts, to not mess up chronology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:06:09-07:00","id":953221,"title":"","content":"I am excited about the game and I get carried away. I will get better I promise. I want to be a writer and I am using this as an excercise. I just get carried away. I will hold my posts to one action at a time. I was trying to do creative thaumaturgy, creating a new improvised spell.<br /> <br /> Can I use an improvised Fools Rush In to use the nonexistant for me medicine skill to keep her alive until Ouroboros gets there? I don't want to know too much because it will interfere with the spell. I won't diagnos her, I will just try to keep her alive using Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"dat