awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:06:10-07:00","id":964958,"title":"","content":"What do I roll to offer those spirits on the other side Essence for telling us what happened and leading us to Sally?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:42:12-07:00","id":965009,"title":"","content":"It can be a simple social roll. Manipulation + Persuassion, perhaps? You first need essence to bribe them though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:59:53-07:00","id":966260,"title":"","content":"Bugger I though Channel Essence was Weaving the entire time. D:<br /> <br /> So I spend 2 mana, cast Channel Essence, offer Essence, cast Channel Essence again, give Essence. Right?<br /> <br /> And the second casting is withstood by Gaunlet, which is, what, 2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":6508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","user":"Tambov","date":". 09-09-2016, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T17:14:40-07:00","id":968263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=962158#post962158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, would it be possible for us to purchase the first dot in the others' Order Status and later Egregore/Techne? RAW seems to allow it, but I'd rather run it by you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I don't think you should be able to purchase Egregore/Techne. From a roleplay perspective, I don't see why the Orders would divulge secrets or special Order practices to someone not initiated in their Order. I don't see any indication why you couldn't obtain at least 1 dot of Status for other Orders, but I have a hard time coming up with a rationale for why an Order/caucus leader would allow that kind of privilege to a non-member.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What do I roll to offer those spirits on the other side Essence for telling us what happened and leading us to Sally? </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree with the suggestion for Manipulation + Persuasion (instant action), contested by spirit's Finesse. Technically we could also use Social Maneuvering here, but that seems a little convoluted for what you're trying to do.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, you could also just use the brute-force method and command it to answer you (p. 181). However, the Spirit won't be able to see or interact with you while your Shadow Walk spell is active.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bugger I though Channel Essence was Weaving the entire time. D:<br /> <br /> So I spend 2 mana, cast Channel Essence, offer Essence, cast Channel Essence again, give Essence. Right?<br /> <br /> And the second casting is withstood by Gaunlet, which is, what, 2? </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I follow about the Weaving part? You can use Channel Essence here with Spirit 2 if that's what you're asking.<br /> <br /> I realized I had a confusing line in my IC post. The spirits are in Twilight, so they're actually here in the material world -- on your side of the Gauntlet -- they're just not manifested. I edited my post for clarification.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to double check in the book, but I thought you could just spend mana and have it count as Essence for the purpose of this spell...but I'm not seeing that now? So I'm not sure how that actually works. But assuming you had the Essence available, you only need one casting to give it to them, and it's not Withstood by the Gauntlet (which is actually strength 3 here) because they're in Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:09:43-07:00","id":970579,"title":"","content":"This seems to have slowed down a peak...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T05:29:52-07:00","id":970637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=970579#post970579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems to have slowed down a peak...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I noticed that too and was going to check in today.<br /> <br /> Unless I'm missing something, no one is waiting on me for a response before they can reply, right?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> - Waiting to see what you would like to do next. How would Dr. Luck try to help with the investigation? I see in your most recent post that you wanted to provide another blessing of luck on the investigation; did you want to try and roll for some spell to see if you can do that? It would need to be something other than Exceptional Luck or else it won't stack with your existing bonuses. You have Time, Fate, and Space magic, and I'm sure you could find some ways to make any of those useful here. You can also do a perception roll (Wits + Composure).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2650\" data-vbnamecard=\"2650\">Retias</a> - Still waiting on a Wits + Composure roll for perception to see what else you find, either using your regular vision or that heat-signature spell you were interested in trying. I'd need a spell roll to see the effects of the spell you want to create and attempt to cast. It would be a standard Unveiling spell if you used Forces to allow your eyes to pick up heat signatures, probably a modified version of Nightvision (p. 141).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> - What would Ophis like to do next?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a> - What do you want to do next? What might you do to interact with the spirits? As noted above, you can try bribing them with Essence, compel them to answer, or do something else. You'll need to make yourself visible to them in order to interact with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:36:32-07:00","id":976570,"title":"","content":"Anyone other than Thorbes have any input or responses? I'll wait a little longer to hear back, but otherwise I will assume there isn't enough interest to keep the game going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:31:55-07:00","id":977115,"title":"","content":"I'm in, I just going through hell right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:32:59-07:00","id":980823,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm calling it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It seems like there is insufficient interest to keep this game going. I would be glad to continue it when we can get enough interest, but for now I am going to be placing this game on hiatus. If there are specific reasons you're not finding it interesting or things you would like me to address, please comment here or send me a private message. If enough players become active again, we can pick things back up where they were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T05:12:37-08:00","id":1019722,"title":"","content":"I Was really busy with CtL playtest, is there a chance we could resurrect this or, failing that, add a 7th player to suburbia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T06:23:12-08:00","id":1020342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1019722#post1019722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Was really busy with CtL playtest, is there a chance we could resurrect this or, failing that, add a 7th player to suburbia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi Tambov! Unfortunately, there does not appear to be sufficient interest in this game currently. Without at least a few active players, I won't be able to run this game.<br /> <br /> The Supernal Suburbia game has the other problem -- it has a very active and large player group. I don't think there is room for another player currently. However, if someone were to drop out, I can contact you and see if you would be interested in joining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T03:47:55-07:00","id":1123821,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> - I don't think your character would pick a Shadow name explicitly copying the name of one of the Firstborn. Especially once you become a mage, I think that your &quot;pack&quot; would find it extremely foolish and presumptuous. And it would also earn you a lot of scorn among mages, especially your Order mentor, who would have strongly urged you to pick a different name.<br /> <br /> Could we compromise here and maybe have you pick a name that references it? Even &quot;Death Wolf&quot; would be less offensive to Uratha and other mages than &quot;Kamduis-Ur&quot; specifically.<br /> <br /> Everyone else: Please post here in the thread for your character sheet. I need you to specifically include it right on this thread using text and post formatting, rather than linking to Dropbox, because I can't access it easily from my phone or from the internet when at work. You can skim through other posts in this thread or my other game's thread to see examples of the formatting. For example: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=926755#post926755\">check this one out</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T04:13:29-07:00","id":1123827,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Sure, Compromise can always happen. Death Wolf could easily be put in if my character would have thought the exact name would have been more insulting than honoring. And if even Death Wolf would have been an insult rather than a honor to his former patron then a referential name would have been chosen. Might need help picking that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:39:08-07:00","id":1124040,"title":"","content":"Is it possible that Dr Luck can get back into this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:53:47-07:00","id":1124051,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><b>Bad Dawg: <span style=\"color:darkred\">Obrimos Guardian of the Vail</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 11/11 (2)</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </div> <hr /><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Shadow Name</b>: Bad Dawg<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name</b>: James Wilkerson<br /> <b>Order</b>: Guardians of the Veil<br /> <b>Path</b>: Obrimos<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Eleventh Question<br /> <br /> <b>Vice</b>: Arrogance<br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Tenacity<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>ATTRIBUTES:</b></span><ul><li><b>Mental</b>:<ul><li>Intelligence: 2</li> <li>Wits: 3</li> <li>Resolve: 3 (Free Dot)</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Physical</b>:<ul><li>Strength: 3</li> <li>Dexterity: 3</li> <li>Stamina: 2</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Social</b>:<ul><li>Presence: 2</li> <li>Manipulation: 1</li> <li>Composure: 3</li> </ul></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>SKILLS:</b></span><br /> * indicates Rote Skills<ul><li><b>Mental: </b>-3 Untrained<ul><li>Academics: 0</li> <li>Computer: 2</li> <li>Crafts: 0</li> <li><span style=\"color:#800080\">*Investigation: 3 (Asset Skill), Specialty (Crime Scenes)</span></li> <li>Medicine: 2</li> <li>Occult: 3 (One Free)</li> <li>Politics: 0</li> <li>Science: 2</li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><b>Physical: </b>-1 Untrained<ul><li>Athletics: 3 Specialty (Aimed Spells)</li> <li>Brawl: 0</li> <li>Drive: 1</li> <li><span style=\"color:#800080\">Firearms: 3 (Asset Skill), Specialty (Handguns)</span></li> <li>Larceny: 0</li> <li>*Stealth: 0</li> <li>Survival: 0</li> <li>Weaponry: 0</li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><b>Social: </b>-1 Untrained<ul><li>Animal Ken: 0</li> <li>Empathy: 0</li> <li>Expression: 0</li> <li>Intimidation: 0</li> <li>Persuasion: 0</li> <li>Socialize: 0</li> <li>Streetwise: 2</li> <li>*Subterfuge: 2</li> </ul></li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">ARCANA:</span> </b><ul><li><b>Prime:</b> 2 (Ruling)</li> <li><b>Forces:</b> 1 (Ruling)</li> <li><b>Matter:</b> 1 (Common)</li> <li><b>Time:</b> 2 (Ruling)</li> <li><b>Spirit:</b> 1 (4 Experience) (Common)</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>GNOSIS</b>:</span> 2 (Free)<ul><li><b>Highest Arcanum:</b> 3</li> <li><b>Other Arcanum:</b> 3</li> <li><b>Combined Spells:</b> 1</li> <li><b>Obsessions:</b> 1</li> <li><b>Mana/Turn:</b> 11/2</li> <li><b>Yantras:</b> 2</li> <li><b>Paradox:</b> 1</li> <li><b>Ritual Interval:</b> 3 hour</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>PRAXES:</b></span><ul><li>Postcognition</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>ROTES:</b></span><ul><li>Choose the Thread</li> <li>Craftsman\u2019s Eye</li> <li>Dispel Magic</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">MERITS:</span> </b>(1 Experience)<ul><li><b>Merit: </b>Guardian Status (1 Free)<ul><li>Status in the Guardians of the Veil.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Merit: </b>High Speech (1 Free)<ul><li>The ability to read and speak High Speech.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Merit: </b>Profession (2) Private Investigator/Bounty Hunter.<ul><li>Two Asset Skills: Firearms and Investigation.</li> <li>Networking: Gain two contacts within the field of Investigator (Police, Werewolves)</li> <li>When making a roll with her Asset Skills, she benefits from the 9-again quality</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Merit: </b>Resources (2)<ul><li>comfortable, middle class wage</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Merit: </b>Safe Place (1)<ul><li>His private investigators office.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Merit: </b>Trained Observer (1)<ul><li>9-Again on Perception</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Merit: </b>Artifact (5); This Artifact is the original Colt 45 prototype constructed in 1871. It was enchanted by an unknown Supernal Entity in the early 1900\u2019s. Through the use of the Time in a Bottle attainment all effects are cast as instant casting at the cost of 1 Mana per activation, it also bestows the Fast Spell Merit on the wielder as long as it is used as one of the spells Yantras. The first effect in this magnificent weapon can cause some truly terrible wounds. The weapon can fire a bullet that has been hexed. In addition to doing normal damage it can bestow a hex upon the target that it hits. This is considered an Aimed Spell and it is delivered by the bullet striking the target. The second effect can only be cast by gripping the handle in both hands and holding the weapon in a non-threatening manner.<ul><li>Effect: Time in a Bottle (Attainment), Exceptional Luck - Hex (Fate 2), Acceleration (Time 3).</li> <li>Gnosis: 3</li> <li>Mana: 10</li> <li>Base Dice Pool: Exceptional Luck (5), Acceleration (6).</li> </ul></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>ADVANTAGES:</b></span><ul><li><b>Size:</b> 5</li> <li><b>Speed:</b> 11</li> <li><b>Health:</b> 7</li> <li><b>Willpower:</b> 6</li> <li><b>Wisdom:</b> 7</li> <li><b>Initiative:</b> 6</li> <li><b>Defense:</b> 6</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>YANTRAS:</b></span><br /> <b>Dedicated Tool</b>: Colt 45 (Artifact)<br /> <br /> <b>Path Tools:</b> Steel, petrified wood, gold, perfected materials; Double-edged sword, spear, noble weapons<ul><li><b>Coins</b>: Authentic 1871, 20 Dollar Gold Coin.</li> <li><b>Cups</b>: Steel Whisky Flask</li> <li><b>Mirrors</b>: Polished Perfected Silver (Cell Phone sized) (Lunargent) \u2013 Reflects things in Twilight.</li> <li><b>Rods</b>: Petrified Wood Police Baton.</li> <li><b>Weapons</b>: Katana (Longsword), Wakizashi (Short Sword) and Tanto (Dagger).</li> </ul><b>Order Tools</b>: Items that Conceal ones Identity (Masks, Cloaks, Veils), Items used to see more clearly (Rose-tinted Glasses, Prisms, Magnifying Glasses),<ul><li><b>Mask</b>: Ski Mask.</li> <li><b>Cloak/Long Coat</b>: Leather Duster.</li> <li><b>Magnifying Glass</b>: Jewelers Loop.</li> <li><b>Rose-tinted Glasses:</b> Mirrored Rose-tinted Sunglasses.</li> <li><b>Prisms:</b> Crystal Prism.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>NIMBUS:</b></span><br /> <b>Long Term Nimbus:</b> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>'Energizer' </i></span>- The long term effects of being exposed to this Nimbus is a feeling of being wired, juiced, or pumped up. This energized feeling gives you a sense of endless energy and at first this is a very good feeling. Some would consider this a good thing, however prolonged exposure can break the body down as the hours, days and even weeks roll by and you find that a good solid rest is nearly impossible.<br /> <br /> <b>Immediate Nimbus</b>: <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>\u2018D\u00e9j\u00e0 Vu\u2019</i></span> - The best way to describe what you feel when you are subjected to this Nimbus is a feeling of D\u00e9j\u00e0 Vu, a feeling that you have done this before. It isn\u2019t so much that you have done this before as it is a feeling that you have experienced this Nimbus before.<br /> <br /> <b>Signature Nimbus</b>: <i>\u2018<span style=\"color:#B22222\">Looking Glass\u2019</span></i> - This Nimbus leaves a light sheen on everything that it touches. At first glance this sheen looks like oil resting upon water, but someone scrutinizing the substance quickly realizes that it is the substance of the supernal, Prime, as seen through the looking glass of Time. Time changes all things but Prime is eternal, the mixing of the two is spectacular.<br /> <br /> <b>Nimbus Tilt</b>: <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>\u2018Shards\u2019</i></span> - The Nimbus Tilt is like a grenade of Prime exploding, sending shards of needle sharp Prime outward. As the shards strike those that are looking they penetrate reducing the onlooker\u2019s composure by one. <b>Effect:</b> -1 Composure<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>ASPIRATIONS:</b></span><ul><li><b>Short Term: </b>Make an Ally</li> <li><b>Short Term: </b>Establish a Sanctum</li> <li><b>Long Term: </b>Regain the respect of the detectives that he once worked with.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>OBSESSIONS:</b></span><ul><li><b>Long Term:</b> ??????</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>CONDITIONS:</b></span><ul><li>No Persistent Conditions yet.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>ATTAINMENTS:</b></span><br /> <b>Prime: </b>Counterspell, Universal Counterspell, Mage Armor (Prime)<br /> <b>Forces: </b>Counterspell,<br /> <b>Matter: </b>Counterspell,<br /> <b>Time: </b>Counterspell, Temporal Sympathy, Mage Armor (Time)<br /> <b>Spirit: </b>Counterspell,<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>LEGACY: </b></span>The Eleventh Question<br /> The Undisturbed Scene: Specialized &quot;Perfect Timing&quot; and Optional: Activate Matter Mage Sight when entering a scene.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">EQUIPMENT:</span><br /> Colt 45: </b>Holstered on right hip, covered bu duster. This is an Artifact and does not have availability rating. (Damage +2, Range 30/70/140, Clip 6, Initiative -2, Strength 3, Size 1, Availability -)<br /> <b>Wakizashi: </b>Sheathed on his left hip, covered by duster. (Damage +3, Initiative -3, Strength 2, Size 2, Availability \u2022\u2022\u2022, Tags -, Effects +1 Durability)<br /> <b>Petrified Wood Police Baton:</b> On belt behind the Wakizashi. (Damage +1, Initiative -1, Strength 2, Size 2, Availability \u2022)<br /> <b>Duster:</b> Full length Leather Duster.<br /> <b>Tools:</b> These Items are carried in various internal pockets in the Duster. <span style=\"color:#800080\">Path</span> (1871, 20 Dollar Gold Coin, Steel Whisky Flask, Polished Perfected Silver (Cell Phone sized)), <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Order</b></span> (Ski Mask, Jewelers Loop, Mirrored Rose-tinted Sunglasses, Crystal Prism).<br /> <b>Smartphone: </b>Older Model (Samsung Note 4) T-Mobile service, acts as a Hot Spot. (Die Bonus +1, Durability 2, Size 1, Structure 1, Availability \u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Laptop: </b>HP ProBook 675 (Base Model) w/built-in badge reader, and fingerprint scanner. (Die Bonus +1 , Durability 2, Size 3, Structure 2, Availability \u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Lockpicking Kit: </b>Pocket size kit (Die Bonus +1, Durability 1, Size 1, Availability \u2022) Always requires a Dexterity + Larceny roll to use.<br /> <b>Flashlight:</b> Small but Bright penlight/laser pointer (Die Bonus +1, Durability 1, Size 0, Structure 0, Availability \u2022)<br /> <b>Car:</b> 2008 Hyundai Sonada (Full size car, Dice Modifier -3, Size 12, Durability 3, Structure 15, Speed 80)<br /> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Age/Birthday:</b> 38/September 4, 1979<br /> <b>Gender:</b> Male<br /> <b>Height:</b> 6' 3&quot;<br /> <b>Weight:</b> 270 lbs<br /> <b>Build:</b> Muscular<br /> <b>Occupation:</b> Private Detective<br /> <b>Ethnicity:</b> Scandinavian Mixed<br /> <b>Nationality:</b> American<br /> <b>Hair Color:</b> Sandy Blond<br /> <b>Eye Color:</b> Blue<br /> <b>Sexuality:</b> Heterosexual<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> He is an Ex-Police Undercover Detective turned Private Detective after he was accused of murder. His detective agency is in its infancy and not profitable yet. To make ends meet he is a registered Uber driver and will take Body Guard assignments. He is licensed to carry concealed.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> Bad Dawg<br /> Fashioning his shadow persona after the three headed dog Cerberus, the beast of all beasts. Knowing that his Shadow Name will carry with it all the deeds that he must do to reclaim his life. On the streets Bad Dawg\u2019s reputation/image is that of a large junkyard dog that you do not want to cross in a dark ally.<br /> <br /> <b>Pre Awakening:</b><br /> James\u2019s start in life was rocky, an Orphan at Denver Children\u2019s Home since the age or 3 he doesn\u2019t know or even remember his parents. He was up for adoption on several occasions but as he grew older less and less people even looked his way. After his best friend was adopted and he was overlooked yet again he decided to hit the streets and take his chances on his own. The streets were not kind to a 13 year old boy.<br /> <br /> That didn\u2019t go so well at first as he was constantly hungry, at least at the orphanage he had food. But he was determined that he could make it. He was forced to turn to petty shoplifting to eat and was eventually caught. His luck changed that night as the old police sergeant, Terry, which nabbed him turned out to be a true guardian in disguise. James resisted at first but eventually accepted Terry\u2019s help and that was the smartest thing he had done in his short like. Terry became a tutor, mentor and substitute father, he even tried to take James into his home but was met with strong resistance by James, independence and self-reliance was important to the young man.<br /> <br /> With his guardians help, in spite of himself, James became a better person. With his life heading in a new direction he was able to join the Police Academy, with help, while there he learned that there was a better life. And from that point on he poured himself into his new life. In a meteoric rise in the department, with unseen help, he became a homicide detective. There he seen the worst of mankind and just what they can do. But even in that environment he flourished. There he had friends, respect, authority, and even a lover, Judy from records.<br /> <br /> A decorated veteran of the police force his life was good, very good. He returned to Denver Children\u2019s Home as a symbol to those there that you can become someone even with a dismal start in life. He mentored youth throughout the city and tried to pay forward what he had received. Then it happened, that fateful night when his life would change again.<br /> <br /> <b>The Awakening:</b><br /> It was a restless night and James was out on a walk when he heard it. There as a scream coming from a dark ally, at least he remembers it as a scream. Grabbing his service revolver he darts down the alleyway. His only thoughts were that someone was in trouble and he needed to help, NO it was his duty to help.<br /> <br /> The screams were muffled as if someone was screaming while in a sound proof room, yet they reverberated off the wall in the alley making a muffled echo. As he entered the alley he was not prepared for what he saw. There was a dark figure standing in a cloud of darkness, the darkness seemed to have a life of its own and it swirled around the figures feet.<br /> <br /> He will never forget the darkness, the way it moved brought the alley to life. James fired his weapon twice maybe three timed, truthfully he can\u2019t remember. The report of the weapon also muffled, echoing as the scream did. Then what he saw can\u2019t be explained, the darkness reacted with lightning speed and then he saw the bullets momentarily suspend in midair almost as if they were trying to decide where they would go.<br /> <br /> Simultaneously he saw the bullets take three different paths, the first is that they fell to the ground robbed of all forward motion, the second path was straight forward disintegrating as they hit the darkness and the final path was altered by the darkness swerving to strike the screaming man.<br /> <br /> To his horror the bullets chose the third options as the darkness altered their trajectory straight into the screaming man\u2019s chest. With that he collapsed as the weight of the world came crashing down upon him. The last thing that he heard was a laughter as none other, then the dark stranger spoke a single sentence &quot;Welcome to your new life&quot; as consciousness gave way to the void.<br /> <br /> As his consciousness floated in the endless black void it suddenly snapped into place as his mind entered the Astral Realm of Pandemonium. Landing in the underground tunnels of this realm he began to wonder only to seemingly end up in the same place. The denizens of this place were horrid demons ripping at the souls of new arrivals, yet they did not bother him as he was a thought and not a departed soul. Still he was pulled, driven to move forward until finally he arrived in a cavernous space and there in the center was a Tower made of Iron. Flowing from the tower was a river of an impossibly dark thick liquid and there stood a man as bold as the tower and as hard as the iron. The man handed Terry a cup filled with the liquid. As he drank of the liquid his mind once again returned to his body, a body that was handcuffed to a stretcher in an ambulance.<br /> <br /> <b>Post Awakening:</b><br /> His awakening did change his life and not for the better, at least not so far. To start he was charged with the murder of the stranger in the alley. He was forced to defend his reputation and clear his good name. This wasn\u2019t easy but with his newly formed talents he was able to scrape enough evidence together to remove himself as a suspect. But unfortunately in doing so he had to cross the line and cut corners. This hurt his reputation and distanced him from his friends and colleges.<br /> <br /> He was angry and from that anger he said and did things that severed him from his old life, only he truest of friends stuck by him through the worst of it. James turned to the bottle, looking for redemption at the bottom of that bottle, but none was there. The street kid came back and he became cruel to those few that stuck around. He discovered that the tongue is the sharpest weapon and words can wound.<br /> <br /> In three months he undid what it took a life time to do. He was back to being that 13 year old on the street. His dreams filled with days now past and his thoughts are consumed with returning there some day. But first he must find the one that did this to him. The stranger from the alley, his \u201cOne Armed Man\u201d.<br /> <br /> <b>Important NPC:</b><br /> <b>The metaphorical \u201cOne armed man\u201d:</b> This \u201cMysterious Figure\u201d is the man that caused his awakening, framing him for a murder. Guardian<br /> <b>The older cop (retired sergeant):</b> Terry is the man that helped him become what he is today. James discovered that he is a mage with Life 3 or better.<br /> <b>Lieutenant in Homicides:</b> Charles is his former Lieutenant when he was in Homicide.<br /> <b>Records Clerk:</b> Judy is one of his friends, and sometimes his lover. She works in records.<br /> <b>Kent Jasper:</b> The father of the man that was killed in the Alley.<br /> <br /> <b>Personal Notes:</b><br /> James has withdrawn and spent his pension, savings, 401k, and every bit on money he can muster to find the \u201cMysterious Figure\u201d from the alleyway. His obsession with this man has caused him most of his friends, his job, and even his self-respect. Even those closest to him are starting to withdraw as he obsesses over this figure and quite frankly that are sick of hearing about it. If he doesn\u2019t recover soon he will lose what little he has left. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>EXPERIENCE:</b></span><br /> <b>Start:</b> 5 Any<br /> <b>Regular Experience:</b> 0, <b>Regular Beats: </b>0/5<br /> <b>Arcane Experience:</b> 0, <b>Arcane Beats:</b> 0/5<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Expenditure:</b><br /> Starting: 1 Merits, 4 Arcana<br /> <br /> <b>Beats Record</b><br /> <b>(A/M) \u2013 Date; Reason</b></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 09-12-2017, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T06:16:50-07:00","id":1124274,"title":"","content":"I hope the Colt 45 isn't overboard. I didn\u2019t have the points to make the companion artifact &quot;The Badge of Authority&quot; but he wants to find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:53:15-07:00","id":1124534,"title":"","content":"I think the Fast Spells Yantra bonus is not really supported by the rules, but I personally like it. Makes sense for the Artifacts own effects at least. Otherwise it's not very overwhelming in its effects to be honest. Your character is predisposed towards time anyway, making the acceleration effect redundant in the future. And the hex will have issues with withstand on many people. That said I'm just jaded by now, I think it's at least thematically nicely built, though I question why touching the handle makes you faster. Weird effect for a gun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T17:05:45-07:00","id":1124536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wtaylorjr2001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1124040#post1124040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible that Dr Luck can get back into this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, we are full now. Recruitment was open here on the boards for a while and I gave spots to the first few to express interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T17:51:54-07:00","id":1124548,"title":"","content":"A question : Are we going to start as a previously established cabal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T18:23:37-07:00","id":1124559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1124548#post1124548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question : Are we going to start as a previously established cabal?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my plan, yeah.<br /> <br /> I am torn on what Order I want my guy to be in. I feel like an Army Veteran might feel naturally drawn to the Arrow, but I also find it interesting to contemplate a Vet who pushes away a military-like organization to pursue membership in a different kind of group, like finding the Mysterium to be a breath of fresh air or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:43:31-07:00","id":1124590,"title":"","content":"Currently I'm playing with the idea of a Clavicularius mage from the ladder (or maaaaybe Mysterium), possibly a lictor.<br /> <br /> But I guess a question we should ask ourselves : What is the goal of our cabal? What's holding us together?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:50:58-07:00","id":1124591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1124559#post1124559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my plan, yeah.<br /> <br /> I am torn on what Order I want my guy to be in. I feel like an Army Veteran might feel naturally drawn to the Arrow, but I also find it interesting to contemplate a Vet who pushes away a military-like organization to pursue membership in a different kind of group, like finding the Mysterium to be a breath of fresh air or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would all depend on his experience with the Army, did he enjoy it or was he out of sorts with it, Why is he out of the service now. I know alot of people that go into the military only to find that they are not aligned with the structure that the military forces upon its members. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1124590#post1124590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently I'm playing with the idea of a Clavicularius mage from the ladder (or maaaaybe Mysterium), possibly a lictor.<br /> <br /> But I guess a question we should ask ourselves : What is the goal of our cabal? What's holding us together?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that the Cabal would be centered around keeping peace between the werewolves and the mages. My character will be investigating supernatural crimes and mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:57:19-07:00","id":1124592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1124534#post1124534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Fast Spells Yantra bonus is not really supported by the rules, but I personally like it. Makes sense for the Artifacts own effects at least. Otherwise it's not very overwhelming in its effects to be honest. Your character is predisposed towards time anyway, making the acceleration effect redundant in the future. And the hex will have issues with withstand on many people. That said I'm just jaded by now, I think it's at least thematically nicely built, though I question why touching the handle makes you faster. Weird effect for a gun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gun safety states that when you are moving with a loaded weapon that you hold in in such a way that it is safe for the innocent bystanders. You should never point a gun in a threatening manner while running or moving fast, That is why you need to hold it like that before casting the Accelerate. As for why the Acceleration it symbolizes that the gun is giving you the quickness of a bullet, speeding you up to match its own deadly pace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 08-04-2017, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T20:00:24-07:00","id":1124595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1124591#post1124591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I was under the impression that the Cabal would be centered around keeping peace between the werewolves and the mages. My character will be investigating supernatural crimes and mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could certainly work for a lictor I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:08:46-07:00","id":1124701,"title":"","content":"Not sure what equipment we are allowed to start with so here is what I have let me know if I need to remove something.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">EQUIPMENT:</span><br /> Colt 45: </b>Holstered on right hip, covered by duster.<br /> <b>Wakizashi: </b>Sheathed on his left hip, covered by duster.<br /> <b>Petrified Wood Police Baton:</b> On belt behind the Wakizashi.\u200b<br /> <b>Duster:</b> Full length Leather Duster.<br /> <b>Tools:</b> These Items are carried in various internal pockets in the Duster. <span style=\"color:#800080\">Path</span> (1871, 20 Dollar Gold Coin, Steel Whisky Flask, Polished Perfected Silver (Cell Phone sized)), <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Order</b></span> (Ski Mask, Jewelers Loop, Mirrored Rose-tinted Sunglasses, Crystal Prism).<br /> <b>Smartphone: </b>Older Model (Samsung Note 4) T-Mobile service, acts as a Hot Spot. (Die Bonus +1, Durability 2, Size 1, Structure 1, Availability \u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Laptop: </b>HP ProBook 675 (Base Model) w/built-in badge reader, and fingerprint scanner. (Die Bonus +1 , Durability 2, Size 3, Structure 2, Availability \u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Lockpicking Kit: </b>Pocket size kit (Die Bonus +1, Durability 1, Size 1, Availability \u2022) Always requires a Dexterity + Larceny roll to use.<br /> <b>Flashlight:</b> Small but Bright penlight/laser pointer (Die Bonus +1, Durability 1, Size 0, Structure 0, Availability \u2022)<br /> <b>Car:</b> 2008 Hyundai Sonada","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 08-04-2017, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:29:43-07:00","id":1124707,"title":"","content":"Added this to the History section.<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> He is an Ex-Police Undercover Detective turned Private Detective after he was accused of murder. His detective agency is in its infancy and not profitable yet. To make ends meet he is a registered Uber driver and will take Body Guard assignments. He is licensed to carry concealed.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">EDIT:</span></b> I have finished with his History and everything else. I am done and ready for a review. If there is anything else that you need from me just let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 08-04-2017, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:04:48-07:00","id":1124905,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\"> <div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><b>Marduk: <span style=\"color:black\">Mastigos, Key-Bearer and Lictor of the Silver Ladder</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 7/7 | <b>Mana:</b> 11/11</div> <br /> <br /> </div> <hr /><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Shadow Name</b>: Marduk<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name</b>: Stephen Jones<br /> <b>Order</b>: Silver Ladder<br /> <b>Path</b>: Mastigos<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Clavicularius<br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Just<br /> <b>Vice</b>: Addictive<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>ATTRIBUTES:</b></span><ul><li><b>Mental</b>:<ul><li>Intelligence: 2</li> <li>Wits: 2</li> <li>Resolve: 4 (Free Dot)</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Physical</b>:<ul><li>Strength: 1</li> <li>Dexterity: 2</li> <li>Stamina: 3</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Social</b>:<ul><li>Presence: 2</li> <li>Manipulation: 3</li> <li>Composure: 3</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>SKILLS:</b></span><br /> * indicates Rote Skills<ul><li><b>Mental: </b>-3 Untrained<ul><li>Academics: 4 (Asset Skill) Specialty (Lex Magica)</li> <li>Computer: 0</li> <li>Crafts: 1</li> <li>Investigation: 1 (Asset Skill)</li> <li>Medicine:</li> <li>Occult: 1 (One Free)</li> <li>Politics: 1</li> <li>Science: 0</li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><b>Physical: </b>-1 Untrained<ul><li>Athletics: 1</li> <li>Brawl: 0</li> <li>Drive: 0</li> <li>Firearms: 0</li> <li>Larceny: 1</li> <li>*Stealth: 1</li> <li>Survival: 1</li> <li>Weaponry: 0</li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><b>Social: </b>-1 Untrained<ul><li>Animal Ken: 0</li> <li>Empathy: 1</li> <li>*Expression: 1</li> <li>Intimidation: 1</li> <li>*Persuasion: 3 Specialty (Negotiations)</li> <li>Socialize: 1</li> <li>Streetwise: 1</li> <li>*Subterfuge: 3 Specialty (Unreadable)</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">ARCANA:</span> </b><ul><li><b>Mind:</b> 3 (Ruling)</li> <li><b>Space:</b> 1 (Ruling)</li> <li><b>Spirit:</b> 3 (Ruling)</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>GNOSIS</b>:</span> 2<ul><li><b>Highest Arcanum:</b> 3</li> <li><b>Other Arcanum:</b> 3</li> <li><b>Combined Spells:</b> 1</li> <li><b>Obsessions:</b> 1</li> <li><b>Mana/Turn:</b> 11/2</li> <li><b>Yantras:</b> 2</li> <li><b>Paradox:</b> 1</li> <li><b>Ritual Interval:</b> 3 hour</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>PRAXES:</b></span><ul><li>Mental Scan</li> <li>Know Spirit</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>ROTES:</b></span><ul><li>Psychic Domination (Subterfuge)</li> <li>Enhance Skill (Academics)</li> <li>Clear Thoughts (Persuasion)</li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">MERITS:</span> </b><ul><li><b>Merit: </b>Status (Silver Ladder) 3 (1 Free)<ul><li>Marduk holds the office of Lictor and profits from the good standing of his former mentors. As such he enjoys the respect of other members of his order.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Merit: </b>High Speech 1 (1 Free)<ul><li>The ability to read and speak High Speech.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Merit: </b>Professional Training (Lictor) 2<ul><li>Two Asset Skills: Academics and Investigation.</li> <li>Networking: Gain two contacts within the field of Investigator (Hunter, Nemesis)</li> <li>Continuing Education: 9-again on Asset Skills.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Merit: </b> Contacts 2 (gained via Professional Training)<ul><li>Dirty Secret: Spirit of transgression. Filthy little thing that revels in everything that bucks the social norm. Knowledge about anything that fits that description and willing to trade that information for a bit of Essence.</li> <li>Hunter: Thyrsus and former Lictor. Knowledgable about the Shadow and all beings that interact with the spirit world. Due to his long work as a lictor has contacts and friends among thearchs all over north america.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Merit: </b>Mentor 3<ul><li>Nemesis: Mastigos thearch from Chicago. Knowledgable in Silver Ladder politics and the summoning, binding and fight against demons wether they be internal, external or supernal. Antimonist, generally hard to get along with but suprisingly dependable and loyal.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Merit: </b> Lex Magica 2<ul><li>When acting in official titled capacity (e.g. as a Lictor) Silver Ladder status is added to his doors to influence his behaviour. Characters cannot spend willpower to enhance dicpools of social or magical actions that are supposed to influence his behaviour. Silver Ladder Status can be used as a Yantra on spells that directly enforce the Lex Magica, the Yantra bonus is half the Status (rounded up)</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>ADVANTAGES:</b></span><ul><li><b>Size:</b> 5</li> <li><b>Speed:</b> 8</li> <li><b>Health:</b> 8</li> <li><b>Willpower:</b> 7</li> <li><b>Wisdom:</b> 7</li> <li><b>Initiative:</b> 5</li> <li><b>Defense:</b> 3</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>YANTRAS:</b></span><br /> <b>Dedicated Tool</b>: stylized key forged from Kassiterum. Usually worn on chain under his shirt, touching his skin.<br /> <br /> <b>Path Tools:</b> Iron, brass, leather, worked materials, Curved sword, whip, cruel weapons<ul><li><b>Coins</b>: custom minted iron coin with imprinted Salomonic seals</li> <li><b>Cups</b>: leather wineskin</li> <li><b>Mirrors</b>: polished plate of brass</li> <li><b>Rods</b>: iron Scepter</li> <li><b>Weapons</b>: pocket knife with blade of iron, leather whip</li> </ul><br /> <b>Order Tools</b>: Symbols of Authority: suits, wrought iron crown<br /> <b>Legacy Tools</b>: Spell is thematically related to a Goetic demon the mage subjugated within the last month (+1), resisting a vice (+2), using the keys of Solomon (+1), utilizin the subjects Virtue or Vice (+2)<br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>NIMBUS:</b></span><br /> <b>Long Term Nimbus:</b> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>'Tempter'</i></span>- Marduks long term Nimbus forces people to confront those things that they desire, but that would damage their life. The husband in the midst of his midlife crisis finds himself hit upon by younger gorgeous coworker, the reformed addict can't stop thinking about getting another hit, just this once.<br /> <br /> <b>Immediate Nimbus</b>: <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>\u2018Binding Pattern\u2019</i></span> - And intricate binding pattern of solomonic keys, runes and symbols appears on Marduks skin. To observant onlookers these bindings seem less like ink tatoos and more like slightly bleeding fine cuts in his skin.<br /> <br /> <b>Signature Nimbus</b>: <i>\u2018<span style=\"color:#B22222\">'Struggle\u2019</span></i> - His signature nimbus is the feeling of fighting with ones own darker impulses.<br /> <br /> <b>Nimbus Tilt</b>: <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>\u2018Gauntlet\u2019</i></span> - Those that witness his Nimbus feel assaulted in their self-control. While this feeling is rather uncomfortable, the subject emerges stronger for the trial it just endured, adding one to its Resolve. <b>Effect:</b> +1 Resolve<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>ASPIRATIONS:</b></span><ul><li><b>Short Term:</b> Catch up with my sister</li> <li><b>Short Term: </b>Summon and subjugate a wraith</li> <li><b>Long Term: </b>Give others a chance to overcome their flaws as I've been given one</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>OBSESSIONS:</b></span><ul><li><b>Long Term:</b> Conquer my own demons completly</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>CONDITIONS:</b></span><ul><li>No Persistent Conditions yet.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>ATTAINMENTS:</b></span><br /> <b>Mind: </b>Counterspell, Mind's Eye, Mage Armor (Mind), Targeted Summoning<br /> <b>Space: </b>Counterspell<br /> <b>Spirit: </b>Counterspell, Spirit Eyes, Mage Armor (Spirit), Targeted Summoning<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>LEGACY:</b></span><br /> Clavicularius<br /> <b>Attainments: </b><ul><li>First Attainment: Goetic Awareness</li> <li>Second Attainment: Goetic Bulwark</li> </ul><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Age/Birthday:</b> 31/May 3, 1986<br /> <b>Gender:</b> Male<br /> <b>Height:</b> 6' 1&quot;<br /> <b>Weight:</b> 180 lbs<br /> <b>Build:</b> lithe<br /> <b>Occupation:</b> Consulting Lawyer, Hobby Psychologist and Lictor<br /> <b>Ethnicity:</b> Caucasian<br /> <b>Nationality:</b> American<br /> <b>Hair Color:</b> Dark Blonde<br /> <b>Eye Color:</b> green-grey<br /> <b>Sexuality:</b> Heterosexual<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Lawyer who rebuilt his life from the ground up after hitting rock bottom. Tests the limits of his own will and that of others. Came to the Denver area relativly recently and is still getting his bearings.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> Marduk<br /> A god king who subjugated the Annunaki to gain his rightful station. Stephen chose this shadow name as it to him resonated with the Clavicularian legend of King Solomon, the Annunaki being the demons both within and without the Mageking has to conquer to rise to his rightful station.<br /> <br /> <b>History:</b> Born as the single child of a happy and nice middle class family living in the chicago suburbs, Stephen was brought up in a sheltered environment. When he hit puberty his life went from nice to boring and lame. Stephen lived it up with alcohol, parties and the occassional joint. By the time he went to UC to study law he had graduated to harsher drugs. For a few years he walked the edge between coke addiction and a somewhat functional life, but eventually he slipped. Half a year later he lay spasming in a ditch, his body succumbing to an overdose. In his last moments, as his consciouness slipped his many demons came alive, tormenting him with his failures. Harrassed by addictions tearing at his flesh, with the laughter of false friends roaring in his ears and the void of never found love devouring his heart Stephen cried out in pain \u2013 and defiance. Confronted with all his failures he saw the potential for what could have been and decided to fight for a second chance. With a strength beyond the physical, with strength borne of will he fought off his demons and carved into their flesh his will to live and to rise beyond his own pettyness. After the last demon retreated, defeated but not conquered, a surge of supernal energy coursed through his body and he awoke leaning against a dumpster<br /> Over the next few days he allmost went insane as Pandemonium bombarded him with his own failings and those of others. He may have turned bitter and went down a left handed path, hadn't a warlock and thearch by the name of Nemesis found him. Nemesis helped Stephen stabilize and cement the discipline he had fought so hard to attain. While Stephen doubled down and finished his degree (to show himself he could), she taught him in the ways of the wise and helped him reforge himself into Marduk. She showed him how to use his gifts to help others earn their own second chances, as he had and initiated him into the ranks of the Silver Ladder. When he showed and interest in Goetia and continued to test his self-discipline Nemesis smiled and unveiled the mysteries of the Clavicularii to him.<br /> Shortly after his initiation into the legacy a scandal rocked the Chicago consilium, as evidence of a Scelestus hiding among the mages of the pentacle surfaced. A Lictor by the name of Hunter was called in to sort out the mess and by the end of the whole ordeal Marduk had impressed Hunter with his methodical analysis of the evidence and social networks within the consilium. As he intended to retire, Hunter offered to train Marduk as a Lictor himself. Uninterested in politicing for a position of power within Ladder and consilum at the time, Marduk gladly accepted. Hunter, a Thyrsus, taught him many ways to approach his new duties that a Mastigos would never have considered and after castigating his own pride, Marduk gladly absorbed every bit of wisdom he could. He had a feeling he might need it. His education complete he has been assigned to the Denver area as the local Deacon wanted a Lictor who would both be wise in the ways of the Shadow and awakened politics for the job. Marduk is afraid he may not be up to the task. Of course such fear is but another battle for enlightenment for a Key-Bearer.<br /> <br /> <b>Important NPC:</b><br /> <b>Nemesis:</b> His original mentor, a respected thearch from Chicago. She helped him bring his life back in order and initiated him into the Arts, Order and her Legacy. To him, she's practically family, perhaps more so than his actual family. During their time together they felt a mutual attraction towards one another, but neither of them choose to act on it. One of the reasons Marduk decided to leave Chicago behind was to prove to himself that he could be self sufficient without his mentor shadow looming over him. Nemesis' personal demons mostly center around feelings of inadequacy, envy and strong desire for vengeance.<br /> <b>Hunter:</b> A former veteran lictor who tired of his duties and trained Marduk as his apprentice. The two of them had their differences, especially when it came to their approach of the job, Hunter preferring direct actions, while Marduk advocates careful observation and deduction. In time they both developed a bond of mutual respect coupled with friendly rivalry. Not wanting to settle down quite yet, Hunter is for now travelling all over the US, visiting friends in various Consilii.<br /> <b>Dirty Secret: </b>A spirit of transgression, allways taking a form that violates societal norms in some fashion.In front of Marduk usually takes the form of a short time college girlfriend that ended up overdosing. It delights in learning the uncomfortable secrets of others and is willing to trade what it knows in exchange. As it only really cares for secrets people are actually ashamed off, it knows suprisingly little about things like organized crime, hufman trafficing or the like, but instead has been known to haunt the halls of politics, the bedrooms of celebrities and the sancti of mages. It has a talent for getting out of sticky situations and is a master in the art of blackmail, often using it's numina to take human form and leverage sleepers into committing more shameful acts, digging themselves deeper and deeper into a deplorable swamp of dirty secrets.<br /> <b>Marshal and Laura Jones: </b>His parents. Boringly average and steadfastly asleep. At first Stephen tried to reconnect with them after his Awakening, but Marduk quickyl saw through the wiles of the demon of family affection steering his mind and castigated those irrational feelings from his mind. The sad truth is that they have nothing to offer to him and he merely keeps up appearances for conviniences sake. Or perhaps because he hasn't fully subjugated his love for his family yet, he himself is not sure and that insecurity is perhaps the only thing that makes Marduk think about them at all.<br /> <b>April Jones: </b>His younger sister recently started college. In an ironic twist of fate she choose to move to Denver to do so rather than staying in Chicago. Her presence makes Marduk a little insecure, as he is suspicious about whether it truly was coincidence (does such a thing even exist? Coincidences are for Sleepers...) that she moved here of all places, before he himself arrived. However he also allways liked her. She is a free spirit, fighteningly unorganized but refreshing. She is now working on an Art degree and Marduk currently considers if and how best to approach her.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>EXPERIENCE:</b></span><br /> <b>Start:</b> 5 Any<br /> <b>Regular Experience:</b> 0, <b>Regular Beats: </b>0/5<br /> <b>Arcane Experience:</b> 0, <b>Arcane Beats:</b> 0/5<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Expenditure:</b><br /> Starting: 1 Legacy (Clavicularius), 4 Arcana (Spirit 3)<br /> <br /> <b>Beats Record</b><br /> <b>(A/M) \u2013 Date; Reason</b></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><i><b>Clavicularius</b></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I didn't want to copy too much out of Legacies the Sublime... thus the empty spaces</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Parentage:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Mastigos, Silver Ladder</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Nickname: </b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Solomonists or Key-Bearers</span><br /> <b>Background</b>:<br /> <b>Appearances:</b> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisites</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: Mind 2, Willpower 5, two dots in one of the following Skills; Academics, Occult, Empathy, Expression or Persuasion</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Initiation</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Organization</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Theory</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ruling Arcanum</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: Spirit</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Yantras</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">: Spell is thematically related to a Goetic demon the mage subjugated within the past month (+1), resisting a vice (+2), using the keys of Solomon (+1), utilizing the subjects Virtue or Vice (+2). </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Oblations</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Rite of Castigation. Meditation on past moments of weakness. Engaging in psychological therapy (either as the therapist or as a patient). Scribing the Keys of Solomon in a durable medium (such as stone, metal or enamel).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>First: Goetic Awareness<br /> Prerequisites: </b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Initiation</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">To master demons of any kind, one needs to be aware of their presence first. Through this attainment the Key-Bearer becomes aware of Spirits in his vicinity. This Attainment emulates &quot;Exorcist's Eyes&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration. If the Solomonists possesses Mind 1, the effects of this Attainment also extend to Goetia.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Optional:</b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\"> Mind 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Solomonists know their demons and those of others. Whenever someone they perceive fulfills his Virtue or Vice the mage can feel the powerful demons of the person stir. This Attainment emulates &quot;Witness&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Second: Goetic Bulwark</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Prerequisites: </b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Spirit 2,</span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Willpower 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">The Clavicularii know that to defeat an overwhelming foe you first have to take away the source of their strength. Thus they learn to ward those things in the phenomenal world that give demons strength by inscribing marking them with the Solomonic seals. This Attainment replicates &quot;Cap the Well&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Optional:</b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\"> Mind 2 </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Solomonists learn to discipline their own minds and tame their own demons. When tempted by his Vice a Key-Bearer may choose to wrestle the Goetic demon of his Vice for control. The player rolls Resolve + Composure and compares the result to the mages Mind dots. If he scored more successes he is overwhelmed by his Goetic demon and thus has to indulge in his vice. Doing so does not replenish a willpower point. If the mages Mind dots equal or exceed the successes of the roll the mage forces his own demon into submission. He does not indulge in the Vice but still regains a willpower point as if he had fulfilled his Vice.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Third: Goetic Shield</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Prerequisites: </b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Spirit 3, the Key-Bearer must </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">increase the other Skill she used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 3, or must attain two dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">The Solomonist rises above and beyond the influence of demons. The powers of spiritual entities fail when faced with the Key-Bearers determination and enlightened soul. This Attainment emulates &quot;Ephemeral Shield&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and to include the physical attacks of Spirits.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Optional:</b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\"> Mind 3<br /> <br /> The benefits of this Attainment extend to Goetia and any affects that target the Solomonists mind, emulating &quot;Mental Shield&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and to include the physical attacks of Goetia.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Fourth: Goetic Subjugation</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Prerequisites: </b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Spirit 4,</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Willpower 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Clavicularius binds demons to his will. By inscribing the Solomonic seals onto an object and then ritually forcing a vanquished spirit into the item he creates a Fetish. This Attainment emulates &quot;Craft Fetish&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration. If the Solomonists has Mind 4, this Attainment may be used on Goetia aswell as on Spirits.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Optional:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Mind 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Key-Bearer learns to call forth his inner demons by the force of his will, forcing them to attend the Solomonists call and take on physical form. This emulates &quot;Goetic Summons&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and to Summoning a Goetia from the mages own Oneiros. By adding in Spirit 2, the Spirit gains the Materialized Condition for the duration of the summons. Subjugating the Goetic demon to the mages will is another matter...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Fifth: Goetic Banishment</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Prerequisites: </b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Spirit 5,</span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">the Key-Bearer must </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">increase the other Skill she used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 4, or must attain three dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements, or two dots in a third Skill from the list.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Clavicularius can ban demons from his presence. With but a gesture invoking one of the Solomonic Keys he can banish the demon from the material plane. This Attainment emulates &quot;Banishment&quot; with Reach assigned to Instand Casting and Sensory Range. If the mage also has Mind 4 this Attainment may be used on Goetia aswell as on Spirits.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Optional: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mind 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">As he can banish spirits without himself, the mage can vanquish his own demons for a short time. Though many Solomonists don't like to admit it, this Attainment can be used to purge the Key-Bearer of Virtue, just as it can battle Vice. This Attainment emulates &quot;Amorality&quot; with Reach assigned to Instant Casting. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#231f20\">New Spell:</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Witness (Mind </b></span><span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><b>\u2022</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Practice: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Unveiling</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Primary Factor: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Empathy, Science, Subterfuge<br /> To the subject people wear their hearts on their sleeves. Whenever someone he perceives acts on his Virtue or Vice the subject becomes aware of this fact.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 08-19-2017, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:08:31-07:00","id":1124909,"title":"","content":"I took the liberty of copying your formatting Hardwire, I hope you do not mind.<br /> <br /> Still need to add more NPCs (have one idea but need to write it up still), Aspirations and Obsessions (have ideas on both but aren't sure which would work the best with the cabal so far), add in tools and write up a 2e conversion for the Clavicularius.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:08:44-07:00","id":1124936,"title":"","content":"Nope I do not mind at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T15:19:49-07:00","id":1124967,"title":"","content":"Added in a conversion for the Clavicularii. Feedback is very welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T19:36:12-07:00","id":1125054,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that the Clavicularius was a left-handed path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T19:41:14-07:00","id":1125057,"title":"","content":"No. They loose members to left handed practices from time to time (primarily those who fail to reign in their own demons) and are generally regarded with a bit of suspicion (and fear) because goetia as a praxis in general is strange and dangerous (even for magical practices). But they're not as a legacy left handed. The members of the legacy are also known for keeping a very close eye upon each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T03:28:47-07:00","id":1125159,"title":"","content":"Looking at the Legacy, you have it as ruling Mind but in the attainments you have Mind as the optional. You should changes the Ruling Arcanum to Spirit.<br /> <br /> First Attainment, second sentence you have &quot;Through this attainment the Key-Bearer <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>the Key-Bearer</b></span> becomes aware of Spirits in his <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>vincinity</b></span>.&quot; you might want to remove the second The Key-bearer, and you misspelled vicinity (remove the &quot;n&quot;). Other then that the attainment in the base and the optional I would change the to Instant casting otherwise it will take a whole scene to cast, with it being an attainment you can cast it as often as needed so duration isn't as important.<br /> <br /> Second Attainment, once again it should be instant casting otherwise the scene that you take to cast the spell, the demon has already devoured the essence. With it as an instant casting then you could stand there all day and as the demon moves towards the essence to feed then you bar it and keep baring it as he move towards it.<br /> <br /> Third Attainment, same it should be instant casting (This is for both the base and the optional), if you take a scene to cast this then the demon has already torn into you for an entire scene.<br /> <br /> Fourth Attainment, both the base and the optional is good.<br /> <br /> Fifth Attainment, Both look good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I know that it is difficult to decide between advanced duration and instant casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:25:06-07:00","id":1125171,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1125159#post1125159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the Legacy, you have it as ruling Mind but in the attainments you have Mind as the optional. You should changes the Ruling Arcanum to Spirit.<br /> First Attainment, second sentence you have &quot;Through this attainment the Key-Bearer <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>the Key-Bearer</b></span> becomes aware of Spirits in his <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>vincinity</b></span>.&quot; you might want to remove the second The Key-bearer, and you misspelled vicinity (remove the &quot;n&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Corrected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other then that the attainment in the base and the optional I would change the to Instant casting otherwise it will take a whole scene to cast, with it being an attainment you can cast it as often as needed so duration isn't as important. </div> </div> </div>It's supposed to be a sense that through keeping up the practices of the legacy and ritual preparation is allways on so to speak. At Arcanum 2 such an attainment would last for a week, at Arcanum 3 for a week, 4 for a month etc. For the spirit Arcanum part I could see instant casting to chance a quick peek (but who wants to be suprised by spirits, you should allways be aware of your surroundings!), but even here advanced duration works better I think. Definitly works out better for the optional effect as you won't know when to look for people indulging their vice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Second Attainment, once again it should be instant casting otherwise the scene that you take to cast the spell, the demon has already devoured the essence. With it as an instant casting then you could stand there all day and as the demon moves towards the essence to feed then you bar it and keep baring it as he move towards it. </div> </div> </div>Same argument basically. If you're in a direct confrontation with a spirit then that spirit taking a turn to feed on some essence is probably not your biggest concern (indeed it's probably an opportunity). The attainment is more meant to close off a feeding ground for some time. Say for example you want to clean up a drug den but there's an intoxication spirit using it's influence to keep the junkies in a spiral of self destruction as he feeds on the resonance of the place. This attainment could close the area off to feeding for a week or month (depending on mastery of the arcana) and thus cause the spirit to search for a different haunt. Alternativly you could weaken a spiritual enemy by closing off their feedings grounds one by one. I don't see this attainment having much effect at all with instant casting on the other hand. That said this feels like one of the weaker attainments to me, if you have a good idea for an alternative I'd be happy to hear it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third Attainment, same it should be instant casting (This is for both the base and the optional), if you take a scene to cast this then the demon has already torn into you for an entire scene. </div> </div> </div>same arguments as before. The attainment is supposed to be maintened through regular uptake, rather than just cast in the heat of the moment. The important factor to keep in mind here is that attainments don't fill up spell control!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:35:16-07:00","id":1125177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1125171#post1125171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the feedback!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Corrected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1125171#post1125171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's supposed to be a sense that through keeping up the practices of the legacy and ritual preparation is allways on so to speak. At Arcanum 2 such an attainment would last for a week, at Arcanum 3 for a week, 4 for a month etc. For the spirit Arcanum part I could see instant casting to chance a quick peek (but who wants to be suprised by spirits, you should allways be aware of your surroundings!), but even here advanced duration works better I think. Definitly works out better for the optional effect as you won't know when to look for people indulging their vice.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I can see keeping it up for a long duration so advanced duration could work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1125171#post1125171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same argument basically. If you're in a direct confrontation with a spirit then that spirit taking a turn to feed on some essence is probably not your biggest concern (indeed it's probably an opportunity). The attainment is more meant to close off a feeding ground for some time. Say for example you want to clean up a drug den but there's an intoxication spirit using it's influence to keep the junkies in a spiral of self destruction as he feeds on the resonance of the place. This attainment could close the area off to feeding for a week or month (depending on mastery of the arcana) and thus cause the spirit to search for a different haunt. Alternativly you could weaken a spiritual enemy by closing off their feedings grounds one by one. I don't see this attainment having much effect at all with instant casting on the other hand. That said this feels like one of the weaker attainments to me, if you have a good idea for an alternative I'd be happy to hear it.</div> </div> </div> </div>With this one you need to choose the essence that you are baring so it takes a casting to select the essence source as the subject of the &quot;Cap the Well&quot; spell. But I see your example and duration in this instance would work best.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1125171#post1125171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">same arguments as before. The attainment is supposed to be maintened through regular uptake, rather than just cast in the heat of the moment. The important factor to keep in mind here is that attainments don't fill up spell control!</div> </div> </div> </div>And this one kept up for a long duration can also work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T15:13:11-07:00","id":1125377,"title":"","content":"Working on reading through some of the older posts and actually creating my own Storyteller-run PC. I think his Shadow Name is going to be Bruiser, and I settled on Arrow for his Order. He left active duty prematurely due to an injury, and his Awakening occurred around the same time during deployment. His world turned upside down, he moved out to Colorado to get some space and try to make sense of what was happening to him, and there learned about the Orders and joined the Arrows. He feels a calling to learn everything he can to master his mind, body, and the arcane arts so he can protect others who might not be able to do so for themselves -- the same he was trained to do in the Army. The nature of war hasn't changed, just the battleground.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> - Thanks for posting the cool format for character sheets! I might steal that too.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> - I had never heard of the Clavicularius but I think it's cool. I'll try to review the actual Legacy mechanics you're proposing and give you more pointed thoughts, but I'm pretty cool with people creating their own homebrew stuff as long as it's not blatantly min/maxing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T15:23:27-07:00","id":1125381,"title":"","content":"There is a detailed write up for the Clavicularius in the first edition book &quot;Legacies the Sublime&quot;. I didn't want to copy too much out of the book, hence why I left some of the fluff spaces empty and just converted the stuff that needed converting. Essentially they're the heirs to the legacy of Solomon (or understand themselves as such) and try to become worthy of their ancestor by conquering their own vices and base impulses. Before you rule others you should rule yourself etc. Quite literally as they delve into goetia extensivly, literally summoning up and fighting down their own demons. The attainments are all built using the standart rules, only thing that doesn't map to a spell clearly and is a bit of a wonky effect is the optional effect of the second attainment.<br /> <br /> So we have two arrows, two guardians and a silver ladder mage now, correct?<br /> Is Bruiser going to try and learn the Mind Arcanum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T04:58:10-07:00","id":1125541,"title":"","content":"BTW <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> did you see <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1010544#post1010544\">this post</a> by 21c Hermit on the attainments of Clavicularius. I find most of his conversions inspired and well thought out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T05:03:53-07:00","id":1125544,"title":"","content":"Guess I should pick a Legacy too. umm...It's a good question. What Legacy would fit Death Wolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T05:23:10-07:00","id":1125551,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> - Haven't decided yet. I try to pick the Arcana I think are the most fun to use. Not sure if I love Mind, although could be cool for him to spend time training in the Astral realm while sleeping to hone his abilities. I haven't picked a Legacy yet. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> - You're not required to pick one. Some characters don't because of specific reasons. But mechanically, it's a cool way to get more mana and Beats, and gives you a third Ruling Arcanum, so most people will take one. There is a list somewhere of the old ones from Mage 1E, I would check that out and see what you think fits your character or sounds cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T05:35:52-07:00","id":1125554,"title":"","content":"The <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">highlighted</span></b> ones below I have 2e conversions for. I did not creat