9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T05:42:31-07:00","id":1125560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1125541#post1125541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> did you see <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1010544#post1010544\">this post</a> by 21c Hermit on the attainments of Clavicularius. I find most of his conversions inspired and well thought out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh I had it somewhere in the back of my head that he had written a conversion for them, but hadn't found them in his thread. Thank you for pointing it out!<br /> <br /> That said it feels a bit shortsighted to limit the entire legacy to just the Vice demon. A mage has plenty of inner demons and to a Clavicularius they all need to be tamed, not just the Vice which is arguably the biggest of them. Also some of the attainments seem a bit dysfunctional (The 'One Mind, Two Thoughts' one for example would require a scene worth of ritual only for you to be able to task your vice demon to think about stuff for a few turns). What I do like however is the option of taking a positive condition instead of willpower when you resist your demon, I think I'll add that in.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> If you want your legacy to be connected to the Werewolves I think there is no legacy that really fits that description. If one was being created it'd probably revolve around the Spirit Arcanum. If you want to go more for a feral theme there are the Devourers of the Flesh (Death/Life based).... but they're decidedly left handed, so that is probably a bad idea. Otherwise I can't think of any legacy that would fit your selection of Arcana and Death Wolfs theme.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> I wondered since you brought up the bit about mastering his mind (and body and arcana). Thas said you don't need mind at all to enter the Astral, so the Arcanum isn't really necessary for awesome Astral hijinks (though it helps to have someone in the cabal with it for utility I suppose).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 08-06-2017, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T11:44:33-07:00","id":1125655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1125560#post1125560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> If you want your legacy to be connected to the Werewolves I think there is no legacy that really fits that description. If one was being created it'd probably revolve around the Spirit Arcanum. If you want to go more for a feral theme there are the Devourers of the Flesh (Death/Life based).... but they're decidedly left handed, so that is probably a bad idea. Otherwise I can't think of any legacy that would fit your selection of Arcana and Death Wolfs theme.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's bad...but Devourers of the Flesh seem so Werewolf, they are pretty much werewolves.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I'd have to make my own Legacy at Essence 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T13:26:41-07:00","id":1125675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1125655#post1125655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it's bad...but Devourers of the Flesh seem so Werewolf, they are pretty much werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it makes sense if the Werewolves he hangs out with are Blood Talons. I think the other Tribes aren't too much into cannibalism... but I may be confusing this with WtA.<br /> <br /> Anyhow it'd be pretty likely to get you killed, members of left handed legacies are usually executed as soon as their doings are discovered. And this legacy turns you into a compulsive cannibal, which isn't all too subtle. Most Devourers of the Flesh band together with other Devourers in cabals and hunt ever stronger targets (which pretty quickly leads to them specifically hunting other mages) to devour them and &quot;gain their strength. The legacy has been &quot;eradicated&quot; a few times but crops up all over again regularily, I think it's been hinted that some &quot;dark entity&quot; (Acamoth? My peronal guess anyway) creates Daimonikums for the legacy now and then and throws it into the path of mages too curious for their own good,<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T19:18:46-07:00","id":1125760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1125675#post1125675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it makes sense if the Werewolves he hangs out with are Blood Talons. I think the other Tribes aren't too much into cannibalism... but I may be confusing this with WtA.<br /> <br /> Anyhow it'd be pretty likely to get you killed, members of left handed legacies are usually executed as soon as their doings are discovered. And this legacy turns you into a compulsive cannibal, which isn't all too subtle. Most Devourers of the Flesh band together with other Devourers in cabals and hunt ever stronger targets (which pretty quickly leads to them specifically hunting other mages) to devour them and &quot;gain their strength. The legacy has been &quot;eradicated&quot; a few times but crops up all over again regularily, I think it's been hinted that some &quot;dark entity&quot; (Acamoth? My peronal guess anyway) creates Daimonikums for the legacy now and then and throws it into the path of mages too curious for their own good,</div> </div> </div> </div>And that gets crossed off my list. No he hangs out around Bone Shadows. What I read had them hunting the enemies of ancient Atlantis and seeking to become like the dragons of Atlantis. Looks like I'm making my own legacy at Gnosis 3... Maybe I should invest in Spirit have one of you all and Mother try to teach me...<br /> <br /> Then make the initiation be someone like having a spirit &quot;Gift&quot; the mage with the first Attainment... Kinda makes me want to shift what I spent my XP on...<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Is it okay if I instead spend that XP on a dot of spirit?<br /> PS: Huh...a Death and forces themed Attainment that slowly turns you into a dragon like being...that might be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 08-06-2017, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T20:37:04-07:00","id":1125779,"title":"","content":"Well I think a dot of Spirit would make a lot of sense for Death Wolf if he is being trained in part by Werewolves, even if it its the Moros' inferior Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T21:36:45-07:00","id":1125790,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> - There are a lot of Legacies out there. I bet you could find one that's interesting for you and a good fit for the character concept you're creating.<br /> <br /> It's worth pointing out that if you don't have a Legacy mentor, you will lose out on one of the extra avenues for gaining bonus Beats (training with your Legacy mentor can earn you an Arcane Beat) until you have your own apprentices. That and the Gnosis requirement means that it will be a while before you can really benefit from creating your own Legacy.<br /> <br /> I do recommend not picking a Left-Handed Legacy. It's not tolerated by the local Consilium, and they will definitely shoot first and ask questions never.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5036-ambersand\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5036\" data-vbnamecard=\"5036\">Ambersand</a> - You have a spot in the game if you're still interested, but you haven't logged onto the forums in several weeks. If I don't hear from you in a few days, your spot will go to someone else waiting to play. Please just confirm whether you're still interested.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12742-doggo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12742_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12742\" data-vbnamecard=\"12742\">Doggo</a> - Are you still interested in playing? Haven't heard from you more about your character in a few weeks. Please post on this thread.<br /> <br /> Everyone: The actual mission or purpose of the cabal is not written in stone. I only described the larger Mysteries and local politics in this area. We as a cabal could do pretty much whatever we found interesting and relevant. I do think that although Bruiser is going to be an Army Veteran and a member of the Adamantine Arrow, he is all for keeping peace and avoiding combat whenever possible. So creating a cabal around the purpose of protecting others from dangerous supernatural creatures (spirits, Uratha, or even other mages) would fit well with his personality and values.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T04:13:27-07:00","id":1125838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1125790#post1125790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone: The actual mission or purpose of the cabal is not written in stone. I only described the larger Mysteries and local politics in this area. We as a cabal could do pretty much whatever we found interesting and relevant. I do think that although Bruiser is going to be an Army Veteran and a member of the Adamantine Arrow, he is all for keeping peace and avoiding combat whenever possible. So creating a cabal around the purpose of protecting others from dangerous supernatural creatures (spirits, Uratha, or even other mages) would fit well with his personality and values.</div> </div> </div> </div>My character would definitly be interested in judical/diplomatic duties for the cabal. As a Lictor it's literally his job to act as judge, jury and excecutioner for mages who break the lex magica*, so keeping an eye out for mages who overstep their boundries? Definitly a thing I can get on board with, which should work well together. And as long as that isn't happening I think trying to act as mediators and helping the victims of the spontaneous Loci could be interesting. I had actually in the back of my head considered that Marduk should help out with the Silver Ladder efforts at psychotherapy for the trauma victims, which I think could also be something Bruiser might be interested in (having suffered from several traumata himself).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *only applicable for mages of the silver ladder and those of other orders wise enough to subject themselves to the judgement of a lictor. But seriously the rights of a lictor in the course of an investigation are kind of insane... to be fair you get your soul ripped out, annihilated and then killed if it turns out you abused your power.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T04:57:37-07:00","id":1126263,"title":"","content":"Alright I think I got it narrowed down to 2<br /> Bokor and Gaolers of Ialdabaoth I have a write up for Bokor but not for Gaolers. And the Wiki entry seemed interesting a group that is interested in keeping out abyssal entities, and who's recruitment is seeing if you stay sane after reading a book with a bunch of them trapped inside. Guess I need to find the 2e work up or write it huh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T05:37:43-07:00","id":1126268,"title":"","content":"Bokor would probably be Death/Mind. I guess it'd be interesting to ask <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> here if he wants to use the houserule that if your legacies primary Arcanum is allready a ruling Arcanum, the optional Arcanum becomes ruling for you, effectivly giving you Mind as a third ruling Arcanum. The Bokor are however steeped deeply in Voodun, not sure how well that works together with Bone Shadows, I'm not a WtF expert.<br /> <br /> The Gaolers are a difficult legacy. To join them at all you have to read a book and then find a very well hidden section of the Temenos. So basically you'll have to be an experienced Astral Traveller, but I think this could be nudged around to say there are actually a few Gaolers around and they recruit now and them (the 1e stuff sounded more like they were basically extinct), using the travel to the Sanctum as Initiation. There is a (shortened) write up for the Gaolers in Grimoire of Grimoires. Their Attainments focus on binding Spirits (and Ghosts). Their philosophy basically says you only should use these Attainments against Abyssal entities, but there is nothing mechanical that keeps you from using it against pretty much anyone. They are Spirit/Death, the Death part mostly just extending the use of their Arcana to Ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T07:13:53-07:00","id":1126291,"title":"","content":"Here is one of the better Bokor that I have seen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><b><span style=\"color:Red\">Bokor</span></b></b></span><br /> <br /> <b><b>Origins</b></b><br /> <b><b>Parentage:</b></b> Moros, Free Council<br /> <b><b>Background:</b></b> The word bokor in Vodoun faiths refer to priests of black magic, and from them the Legacy take its name and motifs. Regarded heretical by many Moros, the Bokor consider death to be painful and not peaceful in nature, and hold souls and ghosts sacrosanct but their corpses unworthy of respect. This perspective results in the popular image of the power-hungry Slave-driver who command armies of the dead, a stereotype not encouraged but neither denied even by the Bokor themselves.<br /> <b><b>Appearances:</b></b> The Bokor are strong in Caribbean nations and anywhere Vodoun has spread, and members often reflect such heritage. However, practical and pragmatic as the Legacy is, they never restrict potential initiates out of cultural trappings, and thus members have a wide variety of backgrounds. While the Bokor share nihilism to some extent, one Bokor may express it as ill-kept clothes and hollow laughs while another might chase luxuries and live to seize the moment before their inevitable death.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Doctrine</b></b><br /> <b><b>Prerequisites:</b></b> Death 2, Occult 2, two dots in one of the following Skills; Intimidation, Persuasion, Medicine, Crafts, Larceny<br /> <b><b>Initiation:</b></b> The Bokor have no formal rites of initiation, preferring to get straight to the point and having little patience for formalities. This means that the most difficult part on the applicant's side often end up being persuading a potential mentor to impart the Legacy, as many Bokor are loath to share power. The actual soul-shaping involves spending time studying corpses and getting rid of the natural repulsion they evoke, along with teaching a respect for the spirits of the dead.<br /> <b><b>Organization:</b></b> The Bokor hold major influence in the Free Council, and this is what keeps them from being branded Left-Handed despite their more questionable practices. This indifference from the larger Awakened society suits the Bokor well, since many members are highly goal-driven and return the indifference in kind. While mentors and pupils are more distant than in other Legacies, this individualism never stops them from marshalling forces when the Legacy's secular power is threatened.<br /> <b><b>Theory:</b></b> The last thing a dying man does is shitting his pants. Death is no peaceful deliverer, and the mountains of bodies it leaves in its wake are no worthy of veneration. Because without the soul, the body is just another pile of materials. No one's using it, so stop your whimpering and put it to good use for the living.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Magic</b></b><br /> <b><b>Ruling Arcanum:</b></b> Death<br /> <b><b>Yantras:</b></b> A graveyard or a memorial site (+1); giving orders to subordinates (+2); ritually processed body parts (+2); straw or cloth effigies of the subject (+1, +2 if the effigy is destroyed as a sacrament)<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Dissection or autopsy; embalming and preserving a body; preparing a body for burial, then stealing it; establishing a chain of command<br /> <br /> <b><b>Attainments</b></b><br /> <b><b>First Attainment:</b></b> Bokor's Gaze<br /> <b><b>Prerequisites:</b></b> Initiation<br /> The first thing Bokor mentors teach to pupils is to assess whether a given body is suitable for use. This Attainment resembles the &quot;Forensic Gaze&quot; spell, but a level of Potency can be used to also determine whether the body's owner left a ghost, or whether it Anchors a ghost. Reach is assigned to instant use.<br /> <b><b>Optional:</b></b> Mind 1<br /> Some lore on zombies say they're actually alive, only subdued into half-death with esoteric means. The Bokor's Mind Sight is augmented so that he can identify such domination and suppression into obedience, as long as it is supernatural in source.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Second Attainment:</b></b> Shroud of the Dead<br /> <b><b>Prerequisites:</b></b> Death 2, Occult 3<br /> Too many people oppose the practice of raising zombies, especially when the body used belonged to someone they knew. So the Slave-driver learns to deflect attention from the bodies she works with, by replicating the &quot;Corpse Mask&quot; spell. Reach is assigned to Advanced Duration and completely changing a corpse's appearance. To do use this Attainment the Bokor paints glyphs over the corpse she wishes to disguise, often with blood or wet flour, which takes a scene's worth of time.<br /> <b><b>Optional:</b></b> Mind 2<br /> They say the dead tell no tales, and the Bokor can shroud even the living with that silence. He emulates the &quot;Emotional Urging&quot; spell on his subject, but projecting only lethargy and apathy to manipulate Doors. Reach is assigned to instant use. The Slave-driver may bypass the Withstand ratings of those he used the Bokor's Mark Attainment on.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Third Attainment:</b></b> Bokor's Mark<br /> <b><b>Prerequisites:</b></b> Death 3, two dots in a second Skill among the initiation Skill list<br /> The Bokor lulls her subject's soul and body into death-like sleep, making him more vulnerable to her sorceries. This Attainment replicates the &quot;Suppress Life&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to instant use and Advanced Duration. Another effect of this Attainment is that the Bokor may affect the marked subject with Death magic that affects corpses.<br /> Additionally, a Slave-driver using the Sympathetic Range Attainment on anyone she's marked with this Attainment may do so without expending Reach. This allows her to use her Legacy Attainments on such subjects if needed.<br /> <b><b>Optional:</b></b> Mind 3<br /> The Mark lulls even the subject's psychic aura, drowning her into the background. The Bokor duplicates the &quot;Incognito Presence&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to instant use and Advanced Duration. He scores automatic successes equal to his Mind dots when a Clash of Wills is provoked by supernatural concentration. If the main effect of this Attainment was already used prior to using this effect, the Slave-driver bypasses the subject's Withstand ratings.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Fourth Attainment:</b></b> Call to Service<br /> <b><b>Prerequisites:</b></b> Death 4, Occult 4<br /> The Slave-driver further refines her mastery over her zombies, making them more lasting and potent. This Attainment emulates the &quot;Quicken Corpse&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and making them suitable for combat. She must paint glyphs on the corpse for a scene, but this can be done together with preparations for Shrouding the Bodies.<br /> Additionally, the Slave-driver may attempt to hijack zombies raised by Supernal magic or other phenomena, represented as a Clash of Wills. This does not work on corpses animated by possession from ephemeral entities. If the Bokor's own zombies are being invaded, including possession by ephemeral entities, she scores automatic successes equal to her Death dots in the defending Clash.<br /> <b><b>Optional:</b></b> Mind 4<br /> Some of the more skilled and callous Slave-drivers can whittle down a living subject's mind so that she becomes pliable and receptive as a zombie is. This effect replicates the &quot;Befuddle&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to instant use. Applying powdered hallucinogens, the so-called zombie powder to the subject allows the Bokor to bypass Withstand ratings.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Fifth Attainment:</b></b> Bokor's Chain<br /> <b><b>Prerequisites:</b></b> Death 5, two dots in a third Skill among the initiation Skill list<br /> The last threshold a Bokor dare not cross is the abuse of ghosts and souls, which are sacrosanct to the Legacy. One exception is binding a ghost to possess its own body, so that it may resolve whatever unfinished business it has. This Attainment resembles the &quot;Revenant&quot; spell, but can only allow a ghost to Manifest on its own corpse. Reach is assigned to instant use and Advanced Duration. Ghosts rarely resist such chances, but if needed the Bokor may bypass its Withstand ratings by raising the corpse as a zombie prior to using this Attainment, be it through standard spells or her Attainments.<br /> Furthermore, the Bokor now scores automatic successes equal to her Death dots even when she's the one attempting to hijack a corpse using Call to Service.<br /> <b><b>Optional:</b></b> Mind 5<br /> The most potent dark magic the Bokor wield is the ability to puppeteer even the living, something that even many cold-hearted Slave-drivers consider a moral compromise in their part. This effect duplicates the &quot;Psychic Domination&quot; spell. Reach is assigned to instant use, sensory range, Advanced Duration, and forcing a task instead of merely implanting an urge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T18:54:01-07:00","id":1126549,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> - I think that is a neat idea. I don't think it's too broken, because it opens up options of what Legacies you might consider without giving up that benefit of getting a new Ruling Arcana that other players would get. I'm cool with giving you the optional Arcana as the Ruling one. <br /> <br /> After reading lots of options, the one that really fits the character concept I'm looking for is the Perfected Adept. Does anyone have a write-up of that conversion handy? I just like the idea of Bruiser really dedicating his soul crafting to the pursuit of perfection and truly mastering his body and mind.<br /> <br /> What would the optional Arcanum be for that, you think? Mind? I don't remember much about it from 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T19:08:39-07:00","id":1126552,"title":"","content":"I did a conversion for the Perfected Adepts (at least the first attainments).... however I houserules legacies alot so it's not completely rules conform. I'll see what I have available. Secondary Arcanum used to be both prime and forces, I made it forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T19:16:48-07:00","id":1126555,"title":"","content":"Parent Path: Obrimos<br /> Parent Order: Adamantine Arrow<br /> Ruling Arcanum: Life<br /> Secondary Arcanum: Forces<br /> Emanation Realm: -<br /> Yantras: Performing a kata (+1), train until exhaustion (+2), upholding duty (+1), exercising<br /> body control (+1)<br /> Oblations: Rigorous martial arts practice,<br /> including sparring with other Perfected Adepts; feats of<br /> endurance, such as long-distance running, holding<br /> weights for long periods and exposure to the elements;<br /> exhibiting humility, such as serving another person for<br /> an hour by seeing to all his needs<br /> Prereq skills would probably involve Brawl, Athletics,...<br /> <br /> <br /> 1 - The Foundation - Initiation<br /> <br /> The initiate starts to focus onto his body to build a solid foundation for his perfection. This<br /> attainment mimics a knowing practice of Life, cast upon the user. With an instant action a<br /> perfected adept can learn everything he needs to know about the state of his own body. It<br /> reveals any conditions and tilts the mage suffers from, wether he is poisoned or ill and how<br /> he is affected by them.<br /> <br /> Optional: Forces 1<br /> <br /> Through rigorous training the monk learn how to move most efficiently. This attainment mimics a<br /> persistent version of the spell Kinetic Efficiency.<br /> <br /> 2 - Body Temple<br /> <br /> This spell mimics a persistent version of the spell Body Control<br /> <br /> Alternative: Forces 2<br /> <br /> Persistent version of kinetic blows<br /> <br /> -----&gt; Persistent here means Advanced Duration. Since the Perfected Adepts train all the time anyway they just reactivate it over and over again, leading to it being basically allways up.<br /> <br /> 3 - Hardened Form<br /> <br /> Activating Life armor looses it's cost, Body Control from Body Temple receives the 1/0 armor<br /> reach<br /> <br /> Alternative Forces 3:<br /> Forces armor looses activation cost. Kinetic blows gets the ability to stun opponents.<br /> <br /> 4 and 5 were rough sketches, but involved spending mana akin to owod blood buffing to increase attributes, enhancing pattern restoration (less mana consumed, healing agg), ideas for the optional arcana involved hitting someone from afar ala telekinetic strike (they had that in 1e iirc) and some variant of turn momentum.<br /> <br /> edit: ups, meant to make that post an edit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T19:52:32-07:00","id":1126563,"title":"","content":"I wrote up the Perfected Adept for my brother in a mage game you are welcome to use it. I did the conversion so if you don't like it change what you don't like.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Franklin Gothic Medium\">Perfected Adept</span></span></b> (2E Fan Conversion) \u2013 Mage: the Awakening 1e, pg. 349<br /> (See the Perfected Adept starting on Page 349 of the Mage: the Awakening 1<sup>st</sup> edition)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>History:</b> (See the Perfected Adept starting on Page 349 of the Mage: the Awakening 1<sup>st</sup> edition)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Franklin Gothic Medium\">Origins </span></span></b><br /> <b>Parent Path or Order:</b> Obrimos or Adamantine Arrow<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Monks<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> (See the Perfected Adept starting on Page 349 of the Mage: the Awakening 1<sup>st</sup> edition)<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> (See the Perfected Adept starting on Page 349 of the Mage: the Awakening 1<sup>st</sup> edition)<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Franklin Gothic Medium\">Doctrine </span></span></b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Life 2, Prime 1, Medicine 2, Brawl 2, Athletics 2, and the Ardent Hand merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation:</b> The perspective adept must display his dedication to perfecting his body and must pass a rigorous fitness test without the use of magic. He must also display his knowledge of at least one fighting style.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> (See the Perfected Adept starting on Page 349 of the Mage: the Awakening 1<sup>st</sup> edition)<br /> <br /> <b>Theory:</b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Franklin Gothic Medium\">Magic </span></span></b><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Life<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras:</b> The weapon of the adepts primary fighting style, A display of martial prowess +1, Analyzing the targets Chi flow +1.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Oblations:</b> Rigorous martial arts practice, including sparring with other Perfected Adepts; feats of endurance, such as long-distance running, holding weights for long periods and exposure to the elements; exhibiting humility, such as serving another person for an hour by seeing to all his needs.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Franklin Gothic Medium\">Attainments </span></span></b><br /> Perfected Adepts must devote themselves to study of the Life Arcanum, along with basic principles from the Prime Arcanum. This dedication allows them to control their bodies and the Chi that flows through it. In addition, their bodies must be physically fit (Athletics 3+) by time they reach the third Attainment. With the fourth attainment and higher, they must also have established competency with the martial arts (Brawl 3+).<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment:</b> Perfected Senses.<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Initiate<br /> The Perfected Adept has learned to hone his senses to be better attuned to his environment, sensing things that others would overlook. By remaining still and concentrating on his surroundings he can sharpen one of his senses for near superhuman levels. This attainment is similarly to casting \u201cHeighten Senses\u201d adding his Life dots to his perception rolls, he may only have one sense enhanced by this ability at a time. To enhance a different sense take another activation and the original enhanced sense drops to normal. Each activation of this attainment takes an instant action and lasts as long as he concentrates.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Prime 1<br /> If the Perfected Adept also has prime 1 then he can see the chi flow within himself and other around him. By remaining still and concentrating on his subject he gains the use of \u201cSupernal Vision\u201d. Each activation of this attainment takes an instant action that lasts as long as he concentrates, although it can only be used to analyze living creatures.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment:</b> Destroy Foreign Bodies.<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Life 2<br /> The Perfected Adept is able to control every aspect of his body and this includes his immune system. Upon obtaining this attainment he is able to purge his body of disease as if casting \u201cPurge Illness\u201d. Subtract his dot in Life from the severity level of the disease and if it is greater than the severity level his body destroys the disease before it can take effect, if it is less than the severity level lower the severity level by the Life dots. This is an instant action.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Forces 2<br /> The perfected Adept learn to push his body to the limits, allowing him to run just a little faster, jump a little higher and exert himself just a little longer. This attainment is similar to \u201cKinetic Efficiency\u201d and the Adept gains a bonus on rolls to resist fatigue equal to Potency. Actions are less strenuous when moving so efficiently. He also Add the caster\u2019s Forces dots to the total distance (in yards) covered on a jump, to the subject\u2019s swimming and running Speed, and to any climbing rolls. Each activation of this attainment takes an instant action and lasts for 2 turns.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment:</b> Body Temple<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 4, Life 3, Athletics 3<br /> At this level the Perfected Adept is able to control the various aspects of his body. By slowing down his breathing, each dot in Life halves the amount of oxygen he needs. Similarly by slowing down his heartrate he affects how fast foreign substances flows through his body, each dot in Life doubles the interval at which toxins affect him. By slowing down his metabolism he is able to sustain himself on less food, each dot in Life halves the amount of food needed and doubles the amount of time between deprivation or fatigue check. Additionally each dot in life halves the amount of time needed for natural to occur and adds +1 to his reflexes. The adept may also eliminate the scent that his body gives off. These effects are similar to \u201cBody Control\u201d and each activation of this attainment takes a scene to use and lasts for 1 day.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Forces 3<br /> With Forces 3 the Perfected Adept can wrap his hands, feet, knees, whatever body part he can use to strike a target (including a head butt) with a kinetic field, this is similar to \u201cKinetic Blow\u201d and adds potency as a weapon damage bonus. This does extend to held weapons held by the adept. Each activation of this attainment takes an instant action and lasts for 2 turns. It has a potency of 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment:</b> Chi Force<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 6, Life 4, Brawl 3<br /> The mage controls the flow of his chi, boosting one specific Physical Attribute, similar to the Life 3 \u201cHoning the Form\u201d spell. When this attainment is gained, the mage must choose a single Attribute (Strength, Dexterity or Stamina) that he wishes to concentrate upon in the perfection of his body. He cannot later choose a different Attribute.<br /> To gain the boost thereafter, the mage performs an instant action to channel his chi, and his Life dots are added to the chosen Attribute. The effect lasts for 1 Day per activation.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Forces 4<br /> If the Perfected Adept also has forces 4 he can use his chi at a distance similarly to a \u201cTelekinetic Strike\u201d. This must be aimed and barriers will stop it. The concussive force of this the target to the ground. This attainment takes an instant action the Perfected Adept to focus his chi and inflict his Forces dots in damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment:</b> Perfect Body<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 8, Life 5<br /> As with Chi Force, above, but the mage can now improves the other two Physical Attribute. He can even use both of these attainments at the same time, as long as he spends separate instant actions to activate the powers.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Forces 5<br /> If the Perfected Adept also has forces 5 his Telekinetic Strike does Lethal damage. Also he is able to slow incoming projectiles (ie bullets, arrows, etc) reducing their damage by his Forces dots. This is similar to the \u201cVelocity Control\u201d but can only be used to slow incoming projectiles. This is an instant action that can be used reflexively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T19:54:26-07:00","id":1126564,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Would Bokor be permissible to you? Acording to the book, it is not a left handed path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T02:34:13-07:00","id":1126632,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> I intend to use the rule to trade in a Praxis to start a Legacy, can I do that before gameplay or do you want me to wait until the game starts and do it first thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T03:59:15-07:00","id":1126645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1126564#post1126564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Would Bokor be permissible to you? Acording to the book, it is not a left handed path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if that's the one you like, sure!<br /> <br /> I think we can primarily use the conversion above, although parts of it seem a little far-reaching. The 3rd attainment in particular seems kind of ridiculous, you can use a Death attainment to both ignore Withstand ratings AND cast sympathetic range spells on the target? That's pretty powerful and I don't think I buy the argument for why it should be allowed. I'll have to think on it as we advance. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> - Thanks for the draft of the conversion. I like a lot of the ideas but it seems like your optional Arcana rules don't seem to follow the same pattern as other conversions I've seen. I might tweak it more to my liking. As for starting with a Legacy, I need to review the rules on them but I'll get back to you. If the rules say you can start with a Legacy at our &quot;level&quot; then I'm cool with you being inducted already. <br /> <br /> Everyone: In case you haven't noticed, I type here in spurts. I'm a working professional and I don't get a lot of consolidated time to play. Once we are up and running it's easier for me to make a post in a short amount of time, but it means I might be a bit slow as we get started. Thanks for your patience. <br /> <br /> You three are clearly posting often and very active here. Our other applicants don't seem to be here, so if I don't hear soon about their plans, I will be changing our party composition and extending invites to people on the wait list. They've got until Friday end of day to pitch a character in more detail and post a rough draft of a character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T04:49:19-07:00","id":1126654,"title":"","content":"The rules for trading in a Praxis are listed on page 199, and quoted below. As you can see it allows you to do this even for the first attainment. the question is can I have already done this by the start of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Awakening page 199</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Praxis Refund: If the mage knew the Legacy Attainment<br /> as a Praxis, she internalizes her understanding. She loses the<br /> Praxis, but receives a \u201crefund\u201d of one Arcane Experience plus<br /> one Arcane Beat. Legacy members often develop Praxes to<br /> train themselves for upcoming Legacy Attainments, including<br /> the first, for pupils who study under a tutor but have yet to<br /> be initiated.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 08-09-2017, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T05:02:52-07:00","id":1126657,"title":"","content":"Sure! No problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T05:10:03-07:00","id":1126660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1126657#post1126657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure! No problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks done so I start with one praxis and the Legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T05:30:04-07:00","id":1126666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1126291#post1126291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><b>Third Attainment:</b></b> Bokor's Mark<br /> <b><b>Prerequisites:</b></b> Death 3, two dots in a second Skill among the initiation Skill list<br /> The Bokor lulls her subject's soul and body into death-like sleep, making him more vulnerable to her sorceries. This Attainment replicates the &quot;Suppress Life&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to instant use and Advanced Duration. Another effect of this Attainment is that the Bokor may affect the marked subject with Death magic that affects corpses.<br /> Additionally, a Slave-driver using the Sympathetic Range Attainment on anyone she's marked with this Attainment may do so without expending Reach. This allows her to use her Legacy Attainments on such subjects if needed.<br /> <b><b>Optional:</b></b> Mind 3<br /> The Mark lulls even the subject's psychic aura, drowning her into the background. The Bokor duplicates the &quot;Incognito Presence&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to instant use and Advanced Duration. He scores automatic successes equal to his Mind dots when a Clash of Wills is provoked by supernatural concentration. If the main effect of this Attainment was already used prior to using this effect, the Slave-driver bypasses the subject's Withstand ratings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading it in detail something that occurs to me: That's not how Supress Life works. It's a veiling spell that veils lifesigns, so a human holding still under this spell will look like a Corpse, one moving around like a Zombie or a Vampire perhaps. But it doesn't put people into comas.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T06:17:47-07:00","id":1126672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1126666#post1126666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reading it in detail something that occurs to me: That's not how Supress Life works. It's a veiling spell that veils lifesigns, so a human holding still under this spell will look like a Corpse, one moving around like a Zombie or a Vampire perhaps. But it doesn't put people into comas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok take that up with the person that wrote the conversion as stared I just copied it here for use if it was wanted. If the ST wishes to change that then more power to him. All legacies are a subjective view point and can be altered as needed to fit each campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T06:25:36-07:00","id":1126674,"title":"","content":"Relax, not trying to attack you personally, just pointing out a slight mistake in the writeup. It's arguably quite possible to create a spell like that using Death 2, it's just not Supress Life and it should probably be withstood by Stamina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T06:56:49-07:00","id":1126683,"title":"","content":"Here is a possible rewrite for Attainment 3<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Bokor bolster\u2019s her servant by applying a their personal mark to a zombie they control. The zombie gains stats as a [dread monstrosity]. A Power, Finesse, and resistance pool all three of these are set to the master\u2019s Death Arcana. The zombie uses these as seen fit for any task. Including interpreting it\u2019s master\u2019s orders, as normal. It also receives up to 3 physical skills from it\u2019s master. These enhanced zombies have different names depending on who taught the Bokor, the most common though is thrall. They are still incapable of advanced enough thought to carry on social activity. They cannot even react to spoken or written words of anyone, other than their master, with the skill of a chat bot. A Bokor cannot control more Thralls than their death arcana. Any thrall made in surplus replaces a previous thrall who turns back into a standard zombie until the number of thralls decreases. Should the Bokor\u2019s death arcana increase the Power, Finesse, and Resistance of all thralls increase as well.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T07:18:27-07:00","id":1126692,"title":"","content":"So the &quot;Thralls&quot; new stats just replace the Zombies old stats or add to it? How long does it take to apply this mark? How long does it last? Ephemeral Entities usually only use Power, Finesse and Resistance for their rolls, they don't use skills at all. Also what does receiving physical skills from its master mean? Get 3 Skills at exactly the same level its master has them at?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T08:22:07-07:00","id":1126720,"title":"","content":"Let's table the discussion on the Bokor level 3 attainment for now. I would like to review it in closer detail when I have time, but it's a moot point because it will be a while before it's even available to the PC due to the Gnosis requirement. As for actually joining the Legacy, I think it's totally cool. Sound good?<br /> <br /> I will try to write up my ideas for Legacies, and review the attainments for all the Legacies our players wish to use (including Bruiser's). But for now, let's all focus on getting basic character stats up first so we can get up and running.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T08:25:24-07:00","id":1126722,"title":"","content":"I am done on all accounts. So I should be good to go unless you find something that needs to be changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T09:49:46-07:00","id":1126745,"title":"","content":"I want to add in one or two more NPC descriptions, but otherwise should be finished aswell. I think what we all should figure out together is what our cabals name is, what our declared purpose is, if we have a &quot;sanctum&quot; (not nec the merit) or something we use together, which rights we uphold, how long we've been established etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T18:16:06-07:00","id":1126909,"title":"","content":"Cabal name ideas:<br /> Wat