> Concept: Emmisary of the Wolves<br /> <br /> Attributes<br /> Intelligence: 2<br /> Wits: 2<br /> Resolve: 3<br /> <br /> Strength: 2<br /> Dexterity: 3<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Presence: 3<br /> Manipulation: 2<br /> Composure: 3<br /> <br /> <br /> Skills<br /> Academics: 1<br /> Computer:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Investigation: 1<br /> Medicine: 1 (Order Skill)<br /> Occult: 2 (Spirits)<br /> Politics:<br /> Science:<br /> <br /> Athletics: 2 (Ranged Spells)(Order Skills)<br /> Brawl: 1<br /> Drive: 0<br /> Firearms: 2<br /> Larceny: 0<br /> Stealth: 1<br /> Survival: 1<br /> Weaponry: 1<br /> <br /> Animal Ken: 2<br /> Empathy: 0<br /> Expression: 2 (Singing)<br /> Intimidation: 2 (Order skill)<br /> Persuasion: 2<br /> Socialize: 2<br /> Streetwise: 0<br /> Subterfuge: 1<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Advantages</b></span><br /> Health: 7<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> Defense: 4<br /> Initiative: 6<br /> Speed: 10<br /> Size: 5<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 2<br /> Wisdom: 7<br /> Max Mana/Per Turn: 11/2<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Merits</b></span><br /> First Tongue 1<br /> Familiar 4 (Ashlyn Aslan - Spirit Sister, Spirit of Dominion)<br /> Mentor (Mother/Pack Shaman - Bone Shadow) 1<br /> Shadow name 2<br /> Hallow 1<br /> Resources 1<br /> Status: Pack 1<br /> Status: Adamant Arrow 1<br /> High Speech 1<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Arcana:</b></span><br /> Death 3<br /> Forces 2<br /> Matter 1<br /> Spirit 1<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Praxes:</span></b><br /> Shadow Crafting<br /> Control Electricy<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Rotes</b></span><br /> Rotting Flesh<br /> Invisability<br /> Remote Control<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dedicated Tool</span></b><br /> Carved Bone Knife<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Nimbus</b></span><br /> Stange breath marks on glass as he passes by as if some great beasts breath were upon it.<br /> <br /> <b>Immediate:</b><br /> a pack of ghostly wolves surround him<br /> <br /> <b>Signature:</b><br /> A skeletal wolf<br /> <br /> <b>Tilt:</b><br /> -1 Resolve as fear that someone dangerous is stalking you.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Aspirations</b></span><br /> <b>Short Term: </b>Hunt a Mystery<br /> <b>Short: </b>Help a Mage Understand The Pack<br /> <b>Long:</b> Work a deal between the Pinnacle and the Pack<br /> <br /> <b>Obsession</b><br /> What effects do the thinner guantlet here have on the underworld?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Equipment</b><br /> Old car<br /> Inexpensive Smart Phone<br /> Suit (+1 Presence)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Pre Awakening<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> He was born into a Werewolf pack. Wolf blooded by nature with a spirit companion as his tell. He grew up a member of the pack, always following around his older sister. When his older sister underwent her first change she became a might Bone Shadow Rahu. He was still her shadow when ever he could, and her arms when she needed him. Many felt he would follow in his mother's footsteps and become a Ithauer. They were wrong...he awakened to become a mage. His spirit friend left him, and he was left confused and helpless<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Post Awakening<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> His mother did her best to help him understand his powers teaching him, and getting spirits to help him. His Praxis are carved into his skin in much the same way werewolf gifts are carved into theirs. The local consilium pulled him out of there and give him a new education trying to build on what his mother taught him. Another student (A Bokor) helped him to understand that power comes with two signs responsibility and privilage. Often time these go hand in hand.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Physical Appearance<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Stuff goes here<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Familiar<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Name:</b> Ashlyn Aslan <b>Nickname:</b> Spirit Sister, Controlling Bitch(derogatory by other spirits)<br /> Wolf Spirit of Domination<br /> <b>Ban</b> Loses all willpower if forced to follow the order of an inferior <b>Bane</b> The blood of a slave keeper<br /> <b>Power</b> 6 <b>Finesse</b> 4 <b>Resistance</b> 4<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Wolves 1 Loyalty 1<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Twilight Form, Image, Materialize (Familiar)<br /> Numia: Dement, Drain, Hallucination, Mortal Mask, Regenerate<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 08-13-2017, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T03:58:33-07:00","id":1127551,"title":"","content":"If you were Wolfblooded you keep your Tell. If you want to keep things balanced, its just a 3 dot Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T09:09:28-07:00","id":1127677,"title":"","content":"If we're the Watch Dogs, what do we watch? Do we keep an eye on the &quot;naturally&quot; occuring Irisis, trying to make sure sleepers don't walk in, spirits don't walk out and if possible close them up?<br /> <br /> I'll be away for a week btw and thus won't be able to read/post during that time starting tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T10:28:36-07:00","id":1128085,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> - Thanks for the update, no worries. <br /> <br /> I finally have some down time this weekend and will be working a lot on my to-do list to get the game up and running, which includes making my own character, reviewing Legacy conversions, and reviewing character sheets. <br /> <br /> I had a few questions for you all. Just wanted to really make sure you are ok with me running my own character. My plan is to treat my PC using the same rules as all other characters, and I will be extra mindful of not meta-gaming. I just have spent over a year trying to find a Mage game to join as a player, and it hasn't worked out, so I would like to have a chance to play. <br /> <br /> I was thinking about taking the Retainer merit to have my pet dog, who would represent an important NPC serving my character. I'm thinking a 2- or 3-dot merit would be right to reflect a professionally trained military working dog. Does that sound about right? Looking to use the &quot;trained guard dog&quot; stats on p.121 of the CoD core book. I would like feedback on whether that seems fair. <br /> <br /> As far as Obsessions go, I want to remind people that these should essentially be long-term magic-related aspirations. You earn Arcane Beats when you make significant progress towards specific goals. So &quot;Learn how and why the Loci are forming in Denver&quot; is acceptable, but &quot;Spirits&quot; is too vague and &quot;Meet a rank 3 Spirit&quot; is more of a short-term aspiration rather than an Obsession.<br /> <br /> Finally, I think I would like to make a few changes to character creation. We are still starting with 5 bonus XP and a cap of Gnosis 2, but I'm giving everyone Gnosis 2 for free. So for most of you, this means you'll get more Merit dots back at character creation. Also, as far as starting equipment goes, you can start with any number of items with Availability equal to your Resources Merit dots, and one or two items with an item rating one dot higher than your Resources. I like using Merits to flesh out characters and give more story hooks for NPCs, to reward players who truly invest in their relationships with NPCs using merits like Mentor or Allies, and to add more background nuance and customization to players.<br /> <br /> Let me know if anyone has any problems with these details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T11:04:31-07:00","id":1128089,"title":"","content":"As for the dog a 2 point merit would be more than enough, seriously wouldn't even go with 2 point unless he was highly trained and effective. Three dot retainers are for professionals that can assist you in their field of expertise. So 2 for a trained military dog.<br /> <br /> My look at Obsessions is that they are magical goals. There can be a short term or long term. If long term you can earn beats along the way and short term is a one shot. If you want to do away with the one shot I am fine with that and I will re-examine my Obsession.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the 2 Gnosis and I will gladly take additional merits as I was trying to balance the merits with effectiveness and I fell short on merit points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T11:09:07-07:00","id":1128095,"title":"","content":"Also, I am going to officially adopt the house rule that if the ruling Arcanum for your Legacy is already one of your ruling Arcana, you get the optional Arcanum for your Legacy as a new ruling Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T11:12:40-07:00","id":1128096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1128089#post1128089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the dog a 2 point merit would be more than enough, seriously wouldn't even go with 2 point unless he was highly trained and effective. Three dot retainers are for professionals that can assist you in their field of expertise. So 2 for a trained military dog.<br /> <br /> My look at Obsessions is that they are magical goals. There can be a short term or long term. If long term you can earn beats along the way and short term is a one shot. If you want to do away with the one shot I am fine with that and I will re-examine my Obsession.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the 2 Gnosis and I will gladly take additional merits as I was trying to balance the merits with effectiveness and I fell short on merit points.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am taking my point of view based on this description of Obsessions in the character creation section of the core book:<br /> <br /> &quot;Obsessions are like long-term Aspirations, but grant Arcane Beats and Mana when you resolve and make major progress toward them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T12:02:38-07:00","id":1128117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1128096#post1128096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am taking my point of view based on this description of Obsessions in the character creation section of the core book:<br /> <br /> &quot;Obsessions are like long-term Aspirations, but grant Arcane Beats and Mana when you resolve and make major progress toward them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well I have removed the Obsession that I had and will give a new long term Obsession some thought. <br /> <br /> I have added some new merits as follows (Resources 2, increased Professional Training to 2, Safe place 1, and Trained Observer 1) That is another 5 points of merits. I have added the stats for the equipment that I have listed. The only thing that I couldn't find an availability for was the Car, you will need to tell me its availability and if I can afford it.<br /> <br /> The character sheet is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1124051#post1124051\">here</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T13:36:44-07:00","id":1128566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1128085#post1128085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Finally, I think I would like to make a few changes to character creation. We are still starting with 5 bonus XP and a cap of Gnosis 2, but I'm giving everyone Gnosis 2 for free. So for most of you, this means you'll get more Merit dots back at character creation. Also, as far as starting equipment goes, you can start with any number of items with Availability equal to your Resources Merit dots, and one or two items with an item rating one dot higher than your Resources. I like using Merits to flesh out characters and give more story hooks for NPCs, to reward players who truly invest in their relationships with NPCs using merits like Mentor or Allies, and to add more background nuance and customization to players.<br /> <br /> Let me know if anyone has any problems with these details.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem here...that just means I might pick up a familiar representing my old familiar when I was wolf blooded, as well as status with the local pack.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> That said...I would like to ask some questions about the Pack? You know so I know more about that part of my character's life. So I can write his physical description. Can you get back to me on that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T16:10:11-07:00","id":1128607,"title":"","content":"Due to a lack of activity on their part in the past month and for not responding to PMs or posts, I have decided to remove Ambersand from the group and invite <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13009_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13009\" data-vbnamecard=\"13009\">BurritoMage</a> to the group from our waiting list!<br /> <br /> Burrito, please post a character concept here and start working on a character. We are using the standard rules for character creation with the following exceptions: start with Gnosis 2 for free (cannot start higher); use 5 bonus XP; and you can start with any number of items with item availability rating equal to your Resource merit in dots, and a select few items at Resources +1.<br /> <br /> You're not required to play the character idea you briefly mentioned earlier in this thread (a Thyrsus street artist), but feel free to if that still sounds fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T16:53:43-07:00","id":1128616,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:red\">BRUISER</span></b></span><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> None | <b>Spells:</b> None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 11/11</div> <hr /><br /> <b>Character Sheet</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Shadow Name</b>: Bruiser<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name</b>: John Anthony<br /> <b>Order</b>: Adamantine Arrow<br /> <b>Path</b>: Thyrsus<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Perfected Adept<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Loyal<br /> <b>Vice</b>: Vindictive<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><b>ATTRIBUTES:</b></span><br /> <b>Mental</b>: Intelligence 1, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical</b>: Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social</b>: Presence 2, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><b>SKILLS:</b></span><br /> * = Rote Skill, ** = Asset Skill<br /> <b>Mental</b>: Investigation 1, Medicine* 2, Occult (Spirits) 2<br /> <b>Physical</b>: Athletics* 3, Brawl** 3, Firearms (Handguns) 3, Survival 1, Weaponry 1<br /> <b>Social</b>: Animal Ken** (Dogs) 3, Empathy 1, Intimidation* 2, Persuasion 1<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><b>MERITS:</b></span><br /> High Speech<br /> Order Status (Adamantine Arrow) 1<br /> Adamant Hand (Brawl) 2<br /> Quick Draw (Firearms) 1<br /> Professional Training (Army dog handler: Animal Ken, Brawl) 2<ul><li>Networking: Contacts (Army Veterans, Animal Enthusiasts) 2</li> <li>Continuing Education: 9-again on Asset Skills</li> </ul><br /> Resources 1<br /> Firefight 1 [Style]<br /> Retainer (&quot;Zeus&quot;) 2<br /> Mentor 1<br /> <br /> <b>Retainer: &quot;Zeus&quot;, retired military working dog, labrador retriever</b><br /> <u>Attributes:</u><br /> Intelligence 1, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> Presence 3, Manipulation 0, Composure 1<br /> <br /> General Dice Pools: Born Survivor 7, Marathon Runner 7, Aggressive Growl 5<br /> Combat Dice Pools: Bite 6 (+0L), Tackle 6 (B)<br /> <br /> Initiative Modifier: +5<br /> Defense: 7<br /> Health: OOOOOOO<br /> Willpower: 0<br /> Size: 4<br /> Speed: 12<br /> <br /> <b>Mentor:</b> Alexandros, Obrimos Arrow and Legacy mentor<br /> Gnosis 3<br /> Forces 2, Life 3, Prime 4<br /> <u>Benefits:</u> Academics, Politics, Survival<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><b>ADVANTAGES:</b></span><br /> Size: 5<br /> Speed: 11<br /> Initiative: +6<br /> Defense: 6<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><b>MAGIC:</b></span><br /> Gnosis 2<br /> Wisdom 7<br /> Life 3, Prime 1, Spirit 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><b>ATTAINMENTS:</b></span><br /> Counterspell (Life, Prime, Spirit)<br /> Mage Armor (Life, Spirit)<br /> Targeted Summoning (Life, Spirit)<br /> Life: Improved Pattern Restoration<br /> Spirit: Spirit Eyes<br /> Legacy: Perfected Senses<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><b>PRAXES:</b></span><br /> Analyze Life (Life 1)<br /> Speak with Beasts (Life 1)<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><b>ROTES:</b></span><br /> Dispel Magic (Prime 1, Athletics)<br /> Knit (Life 3, Medicine)<br /> Spirit Summons (Spirit 3, Occult)<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><b>TOOLS:</b></span><ul><li><b>Dedicated Tool</b>: John's set of Army dog tags, worn on a chain around his neck</li> <li><b>Path Tools</b>: Wood, copper, stone, natural materials; axe, sling, hunting weapons<ul><li><b>Coins</b>: An old lucky penny from John's childhood coin collection</li> <li><b>Cups</b>: John's military flask; a small glass made from polished stone</li> <li><b>Mirrors</b>: A small pocket-sized mirror with a copper frame</li> <li><b>Rods</b>: A wooden walking staff with intricately carved runes</li> <li><b>Weapons</b>: A stone arrowhead; a military-issue combat knife</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Order Tools</b>: Martial tools to symbolize conflict.<ul><li>Used bullet casings; individual first aid kit</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><b>NIMBUS:</b></span><br /> <b>Long-term</b>: People around Bruiser start to either attract or repel wildlife. Some might find that bugs and pests constantly show up in their homes. Others might notice that household pets are on edge around them, or conversely, find cats and dogs eager for their attention.<br /> <br /> <b>Immediate</b>: Bruiser emits a feral scent that evokes a rush of adrenaline in observers, making them feel on edge.<br /> <br /> <b>Signature</b>: Locations bearing Bruiser\u2019s Signature Nimbus evoke a sense of excitement and a physical sensation of warmth. Objects feel powerful or carry an inherent sense of purpose.<br /> <br /> <b>Tilt</b>: -1 Composure<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b><span style=\"color:red\">ASPIRATIONS:</span></b></span><ul><li><b>Short Term</b>: Meditate in the wilderness</li> <li><b>Short Term</b>: Escort another mage into the Shadow</li> <li><b>Long Term</b>: Improve his reputation and rank within the Adamantine Arrow</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b><span style=\"color:red\">OBSESSIONS:</span></b></span><ul><li>Study and catalog diferent types of spirits and Resonance</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><b>CONDITIONS:</b></span><br /> No Persistent Conditions currently.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"color:red\">EQUIPMENT:</span></span></b><br /> <b>Staff</b>: +1 Damage, -1 Initiative, Strength 2, Size 4, Availability 1; Knockdown, Reach, Two-Handed<br /> <b>Glock 17</b>: +1 Damage, Long Range, Medium Capacity, 0 Initiative, Strength 2, Size 1, Availability 2<br /> <b>Small knife</b>: +0 Damage, 0 Initiative, Strength 1, Size 1, Availability 1; Thrown (A)<br /> <b>Military-issue combat knife</b>: +1 Damage, -1 Initiative, Strength 1, Size 2, Availability 2; Enhance: Crafts or Survival<br /> <b>Brass knuckles</b>: +0 Damage, 0 Initiative, Strength 1, Size 1, Availability 1; Brawl<br /> <b>Reinforced Clothing</b>: 1/0 rating, Strength 1, Defense 0, Speed 0, Availability 1; Coverage: Torso, arms, legs<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://freebeacon.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/tedd-1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Age:</b> 32<br /> <b>Gender:</b> Male<br /> <b>Height:</b> 5\u2019 11\u201d<br /> <b>Weight:</b> 190 lbs.<br /> <b>Build:</b> Muscular<br /> <b>Occupation:</b> Currently unemployed, on disability<br /> <b>Ethnicity:</b> Mixed Western European heritage<br /> <b>Nationality:</b> American<br /> <b>Hair Color:</b> Brown<br /> <b>Eye Color:</b> Green<br /> <b>Sexuality:</b> Heterosexual<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> U.S. Army Veteran on a journey of personal and spiritual discovery<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> Bruiser<br /> John carried a reputation in his U.S. Army unit for being hot-headed but incredibly loyal. He always had his friend\u2019s back, and he never gave up or ran away from a fight. After his injury, John battled with pain and withdrew from the world around him, but his Awakening filled him with a new sense of awe and determination. His Shadow Name is a warning to any who might harm him or his allies: You swing hard, I\u2019ll swing harder.<br /> <br /> <b>Pre-Awakening:</b><br /> John was born in the Chicago suburbs, but he didn't live there for long. Because his father actively served in the U.S. Air Force and had several permanent changes of station, their family was relocated multiple times; John remembers living in Illinois, Ohio, Colorado, and even Alaska. John struggled with these transitions, and their moves always caused tension between John's parents, ultimately leading to divorce. He and his mother moved back to Chicago when he was in middle school, and they stayed there until he graduated.<br /> <br /> John remained in close contact with his father and admired his dedication to the military, and he joined the Army to help with college tuition. Because he enjoyed working with animals, he decided to pursue a military career as a dog handler. John was deployed twice to Iraq, where his partner Zeus, a smart labrador retriever trained to identify explosives, identified several IEDs before they were activated and saved the lives of dozens of soldiers, including John.<br /> <br /> A few months before his second tour was scheduled to end, however, John was injured by an IED and had to be medically evaucated. He suffered a traumatic brain injury and multiple fractures in his arms, neck, and shoulder, requiring extensive surgery and rehabilitation and forcing him into medical retirement from the Army. Zeus similarly became more agitated and skittish after this incident and was retired from service, and John was able to adopt his partner, but he didn't know how to cope with the chronic back and shoulder pain that threatened to envelop his life. John quickly reached a point when he was heavily prescribed narcotics but couldn't find lasting relief.<br /> <br /> <b>The Awakening:</b><br /> One day, John's father, who had ultimately settled in the Denver area near the local Air Force base, contacted him and told him that he heard from another airman about a &quot;spiritual healer&quot; who might be able to help John recover. John was immediately skeptical, but every other medical treatment he had tried -- surgery, medications, physical therapy -- hadn't worked. Out of desperation and fighting despair, he flew out to Denver to meet this holistic healer, but something about the rural area and the rugged wilderness began to evoke a change in him that he didn't fully understand. John met with this healer, who claimed that he was injured not just physically but spiritually, and he agreed to a ritualistic &quot;cleansing&quot; that supposedly would help him find &quot;inner peace.&quot;<br /> <br /> What happened next for John in that private, incense-filled room was his first true spiritual experience, an Astral journey to the Primal Wild. John's eyes were opened by the Moon to both the reflection of Life and the Shadow it casts upon the world. No longer bound by worldly knowledge, arguing with medical professionals about the &quot;mind-body link&quot; rather than the true duality of Life and Spirit, John broke the chains forged around his body and shattered them, and he uttered a Primal roar that formed rune-shaped cracks in the dirt where he stood.<br /> <br /> The &quot;holistic healer&quot;, who was actually just a guy looking for an easy scam target and equipped with some nice incense and cheap weed, was stunned when John emerged from the cramped shack with a radically different take on life. And at first, John did still experience pain; his Awakening hadn't changed that. But once he had experienced and survived the Ecstatic rush of the Primal Wild, pain was just another sensation that proved he was alive.<br /> <br /> <b>Post-Awakening:</b><br /> Unknown to the &quot;spiritual healer&quot; or John, a mage had been closely following and investigating the patients of the &quot;spiritual healer&quot; looking for telltale signs of Awakening, and he quickly found John and introduced him into the Dever Consilium. With his new awarenes of Supernal magic and appreciation for the greater context of his existence, John embarked on a journey of personal transformation and development. He found himself drawn to the doctrine of the Adamantine Arrow, sought training and entrance, and successfully passed his training and testing requirements to earn his way into the Order. Taking the Shadow Name of &quot;Bruiser&quot;, he continued with his journal of soul-searching and was initiated into the Legacy of the Perfected Adepts. As a Monk, Bruiser dedicates his waking hours to honing his physical and magical abilities, protecting his cabal and Consilium from danger, and studying the unique oddities of the Shadow in the Denver region.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Experience</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>EXPERIENCE:</b></span><br /> <b>Beats: </b>0/5, <b>Experience:</b> 0<br /> <b>Arcane Beats:</b> 0/5, <b>Arcane Experience:</b> 0<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Expenditure:</b><br /> Starting: Life 3 (4 XP), Legacy Attainment (1 XP)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Perfected Adept Legacy</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>DOCTRINE:</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Life 2, Athletics 2, and one of the following additional Skills at 2 dots or higher: Medicine, Brawl, or Survival.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation:</b> The perspective adept must display his dedication to perfecting his body and must pass a rigorous fitness test without the use of magic. He must also display his knowledge of at least one fighting style.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:red\">MAGIC:</span></b><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Life<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum: </b>Prime<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras:</b> The weapon of the adepts primary fighting style, A display of martial prowess +1, Analyzing the target\u2019s chi flow +1.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Oblations:</b> Rigorous martial arts practice, including sparring with other Perfected Adepts; feats of endurance, such as long-distance running, holding weights for long periods and exposure to the elements; exhibiting humility, such as serving another person for an hour by seeing to all his needs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:RED\">ATTAINMENTS:</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>First Attainment:</u></b><u> Perfected Senses</u><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Initiation<br /> <br /> As the \u201cHeightened Senses\u201d spell, this Attainment add the Perfected Adept\u2019s Life dots to his perception rolls. Each activation of this attainment takes an instant action and remains in effect for as long as the mage sustains concentrations on the Attainment.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Prime 1<br /> As \u201cSupernal Vision\u201d, but can only be used to examine a living person. Requires an instant activation to use.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Second Attainment:</u></b><u> Destroy Foreign Bodies</u><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Life 2, Athletics 3<br /> <br /> As the \u201cPurge Illness\u201d spell. Take an instant action to subtract the Perfected Adept\u2019s dots in Life Arcanum from the severity of any disease in his body. If Potency is less than the illness\u2019 rating, reduce it by the difference, and if greater, the spell eliminates the illness from the subject entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Prime 2<br /> As the \u201cWards and Signs\u201d spell. When the subject is the target of a spell, that spell is Withstood with the Potency of this attainment. Each activation of this attainment requires one scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Third Attainment:</u></b><u> Body Temple</u><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Life 3, Athletics 3. In addition, he must either have 3 dots in the second Skill used to meet the requirements of the Legacy, or 2 dots in a second Skill from the list of possible requirements.<br /> <br /> As the \u201cBody Control\u201d spell, this Attainment grants bonuses based on the Perfected Adept\u2019s dots in Life, including slower breathing and heartbeat, reduced metabolism, faster reflexes, and eliminating body odors. The subject\u2019s bashing wounds also heal faster, and he gains 1/0 armor for the duration of the Attainment effect. Activating this Attainment requires one scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Prime 3<br /> As \u201cDispel Magic\u201d, but can only affect spells directly targeting this subject and requires at least one dot in each Arcanum involved in the spell. The Attainment requires an instant action to activate and has a lasting effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Fourth Attainment:</u></b><u> Chi Force</u><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Life 4, Athletics 4, and the other Skill requirements of the previous Attainment.<br /> <br /> As the \u201cKnit\u201d spell, the subject can channel his chi into his wounds to rapidly restore damage to the body, including lethal damage. The Perfected Adept may only use this Attainment on his own wounds. Each activation requires an instant action and heals a number of wounds equal to his Life dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Prime 4<br /> As the \u201cChannel Mana\u201d spell. The Perfected Adept can manipulate the body\u2019s chi force to shift or relocate mana between the subject and any other living person he touches, equal to the Potency of the Attainment. He can ignore his Gnosis-derived mana per turn limit. Each activation requires an instant action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Fifth Attainment:</u></b><u> Perfect Body</u><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Life 5, Athletics 4. In addition, he must either have 4 dots in the second Skill used to meet the requirements of the Legacy; 3 dots in a second Skill from the list of possible requirements; or 2 dots in a third Skill from the list of possible requirements.<br /> <br /> As the \u201cHoning the Form\u201d spell, this Attainment allows the Perfected Adept to improve any combination of his physical Attributes. Gain his Life dots in Potency and assign them between the Perfected Adept\u2019s physical Attributes as extra dots. The affected Attributes cannot be raised above<br /> the subject\u2019s maximum Attribute dots (5 for normal human beings). Each activation requires one scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Prime 5<br /> As the \u201cSupernal Dispellation\u201d spell, this attainment allows the Perfected Adept to shrug off the effects of any undesirable spell that specifically targets him or includes him as a subject, with no need to possess the specific arcana involved in the spell. Each activation takes an instant action and has an advanced duration.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 09-19-2017, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T17:26:26-07:00","id":1128632,"title":"","content":"A draft of my character sheet is up, still working on adding some details (including the backstory and Legacy info). Unfortunately I'm not sure I will have much time tonight to actually work on this like I thought I would, having some personal issues come up and I can't spend much time on the computer. Sorry guys. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T23:23:05-07:00","id":1129125,"title":"","content":"I'll have my guy up tomorrow, what's the code or whatever for putting up a spoiler?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T01:27:40-07:00","id":1129145,"title":"","content":"[spoiler stuff you want hidden [/spoiler]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T03:16:57-07:00","id":1129725,"title":"","content":"Wow, ok, so BurritoMage has apparently been banned due to inflammatory language here on the forums. So he's out.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> - You're next on the wait list. If you are still interested, you are welcome to join us again with Dr. Luck. Please go back and revise your character sheet to fit our modified character creation rules. You get Gnosis 2 for free, but it is capped at that level, and you get 5 additional XP to spend on whatever you want. Please let us know if you have questions or if you have changed your mind about playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T08:22:31-07:00","id":1129796,"title":"","content":"Thank you, I'm in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T08:35:17-07:00","id":1129803,"title":"","content":"Cool! One thing to remember, because your Gnosis will be 2 instead of 3, make sure to limit yourself to 2 Praxes and 1 Obsession. You also will need to add a bunch of Merits, since you had previously put all of those into Gnosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T11:54:15-07:00","id":1129910,"title":"","content":"I have updated my character. Please give feedback. Is there a chance of encountering other supernaturals or is that a still no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T03:13:56-07:00","id":1130195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wtaylorjr2001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1129910#post1129910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have updated my character. Please give feedback. Is there a chance of encountering other supernaturals or is that a still no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Character sheet looks good, thanks for updating! I do have a few thoughts for you:<br /> <br /> 1) Resources: Your background says that Dr. Luck is pretty broke, but now you've added Resources 2, suggesting that he has some decent expendable income. So you could say that he's recently inherited some money, maybe had his first breakthrough with a book, or that lotto ticket he found actually won him some money. You also could then feasibly own a nicer car, an actual working cell phone, and so forth. But if you like the idea of him being a &quot;starving artist&quot;, you could cut the Resources merit and put that into something else.<br /> <br /> 2) Legacy: If interested, you could start with your character inducted into a Legacy. If you aren't familiar with these, I would review that section of the core Mage 2E book. It's a way to give yourself another Ruling arcanum and access to some additional supernatural abilities. I am using a house rule that if your Legacy's primary arcanum is already a Ruling arcanum for your character (so if you pick one that has Fate or Time as its Ruling arcanum), then you get its optional arcanum as a Ruling arcanum instead.<br /> <br /> 3) Yes, there will always be a possibility of encountering other supernatural creatures, including vampires, ghosts, goetia, or something else. However, werewolves will be the most likely to encounter because of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T11:18:05-07:00","id":1130361,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback. I would like to start with Shadow name and get the safe place, hallow, sanctum, and resources in the first few gaming sessions. I would like to have my Luck grant me the opportunity to get these things in play. I want to finish a book that I was writing and get resources first then safe place hallow and sanctum.<br /> <br /> I would like a Legacy that would grant me Space as a Ruling Arcanum but I don't know of any. I will see if I can get anything good from google.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","user":"wtaylorjr2001","date":". 08-17-2017, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T21:38:40-07:00","id":1131117,"title":"","content":"Updated my sheet. Turned Nemesis into a three dot mentor. She's not from Denver, so the political assist she can render is limited (but with order status 3, I should be fine on my own when it comes to dealing with the ladder... and that was kind of the point in moving away from chicago anyway). Given the rules for mentors in the corebook she should have gnosis 4 and 13 total dots in arcana, probably focussed on spirit and mind (Spirit 4, Mind 4, Space 3, Prime 1, Death 1 would be my personal suggestion. Think she'd be a second degree adept in her main arcana, space 3 for utility is too good to pass up for any mastigos long term, prime 1 is crucial for dealing with mages and death 1 unlocks the last kind of ephemeral entity to her perception). The three skills she could help with.... uhhh Occult for her knowlegde about Goetia/Spirits/Demons, Intimidation for her rather direct and forceful nature and empathy for her insight into human nature could work. As for what she wants out of marduk... I'll leave it up to you wether she has ulterior motives, but so far their relationship is best described as challenging each other with romantic undertones.<br /> <br /> The freed up contact spot I replaced with a spirit of transgression.<br /> <br /> I put another point into professional training and would like to use the last dot if you'll allow it to buy my second legacy attainment.<br /> <br /> Also added a bunch of npcs to it. Feel free to do weird things with his sister if you feel like it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a><br /> Reading through your chars writeup I think that your nimbus sounds to me more like it'd cause an increase in wits/composure from the adrenaline rush rather than a decrease in composure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":".  gnosis 4 not 3 08-25-2017, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T08:52:57-07:00","id":1132639,"title":"","content":"A questions: How long has our cabal been established. Only just now, everyone is still new to each other? Just wondering how much we know about each others capabilities, personalities (and beware perhaps even personal lives), etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 08-22-2017, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:52:12-07:00","id":1133897,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> - You might be interested in the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Reality_Stalker\" target=\"_blank\">Reality Stalkers</a>, <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Tellurians\" target=\"_blank\">Tellurians</a>, or <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Walker_in_Mists\" target=\"_blank\">Walkers in Mists</a>. You would qualify for the first two due to your membership in the Mysterium, and the third due to both your Path and Order. I would argue that the Walkers in Mists are probably more popular in the Denver area due to the rural environment outside of the city. If you want to pick one of these, let me know and we can work on creating the core doctrine of the Legacy and its first Attainment or two. It cost 1 XP to unlock the first Attainment, which is the only formal XP cost to join the Legacy prior to the game restarting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> - Thanks for all of your hard work with fleshing out your character background and making everything so detailed. I think your suggestions for the Mentor merit sound very appropriate. You can buy the second Attainment, yes.<br /> <br /> For my character, I was going for the idea that when we are in our &quot;fight or flight&quot; mode, we get hyped up and are more likely to react quickly and strongly to a threat. So the -1 Composure is supposed to reflect the idea that the &quot;adrenaline&quot;-like rush that his Nimbus evokes makes someone have a harder time appearing or staying calm. I think increased Resolve or Wits would make sense as well, but the Composure part reflects the fact that most people just don't appear as calm and graceful when they're under pressure.<br /> <br /> Doggo hasn't logged into the forums or replied to my PM from a few weeks ago, so at this point I'm going to be removing him from the roster as well.<br /> <br /> Other than Dr. Luck finalizing his Legacy and my own need to finalize my general character details, does anyone else have any issues they need resolved or anything else that they're waiting on from me before we can finally get the ball rolling?<br /> <br /> On a related note: I'm really sorry for the delay in getting things up and running. I've been swamped at work, and I've been busy with personal stuff as well. My wife is a teacher, so during the school year I often take more time to work on PbP games because she goes to bed earlier, so I expect to have increased availability in the near future. I also just found a way to get around a Gmail firewall at work and be able to type out posts and email them to my phone using a different web-based email browser. Hopefully that means my post rate will increase a fair bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T13:07:00-07:00","id":1133918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1133897#post1133897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> - You might be interested in the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Reality_Stalker\" target=\"_blank\">Reality Stalkers</a>, <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Tellurians\" target=\"_blank\">Tellurians</a>, or <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Walker_in_Mists\" target=\"_blank\">Walkers in Mists</a>. You would qualify for the first two due to your membership in the Mysterium, and the third due to both your Path and Order. I would argue that the Walkers in Mists are probably more popular in the Denver area due to the rural environment outside of the city. If you want to pick one of these, let me know and we can work on creating the core doctrine of the Legacy and its first Attainment or two. It cost 1 XP to unlock the first Attainment, which is the only formal XP cost to join the Legacy prior to the game restarting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the rules RAW you need 2 dots in the legacies primary Arcanum. Unless you want to homerule it down to 1 (which I'd be fine with personally, the first Attainment only uses level 1 Arcana afterall, but there are arguments against it aswell) he'd need to pick up a 2nd dot of space before Dr. Luck can join a Space based legacy (could of course just move one dot from the other Arcana over to Space).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> - Thanks for all of your hard work with fleshing out your character background and making everything so detailed. I think your suggestions for the Mentor merit sound very appropriate. You can buy the second Attainment, yes. </div> </div> </div>Awesome. His nightly ritual of getting a line of coke ready and then cleaning it up without taking it now serves for more than just self discipline!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For my character, I was going for the idea that when we are in our &quot;fight or flight&quot; mode, we get hyped up and are more likely to react quickly and strongly to a threat. So the -1 Composure is supposed to reflect the idea that the &quot;adrenaline&quot;-like rush that his Nimbus evokes makes someone have a harder time appearing or staying calm. I think increased Resolve or Wits would make sense as well, but the Composure part reflects the fact that most people just don't appear as calm and graceful when they're under pressure. </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. Maybe the other effects will come into play at higher gnosis, should the nimbus tilt not change completly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doggo hasn't logged into the forums or replied to my PM from a few weeks ago, so at this point I'm going to be removing him from the roster as well.<br /> <br /> Other than Dr. Luck finalizing his Legacy and my own need to finalize my general character details, does anyone else have any issues they need resolved or anything else that they're waiting on from me before we can finally get the ball rolling? </div> </div> </div>As asked above: Any word of god on how long this cabal's been together? Otherwise no not really, I'm ready and eager to start personally <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a related note: I'm really sorry for the delay in getting things up and running. I've been swamped at work, and I've been busy with personal stuff as well. My wife is a teacher, so during the school year I often take more time to work on PbP games because she goes to bed earlier, so I expect to have increased availability in the near future. I also just found a way to get around a Gmail firewall at work and be able to type out posts and email them to my phone using a different web-based email browser. Hopefully that means my post rate will increase a fair bit. </div> </div> </div>It takes as much time as it takes. Pbp games were never fast paced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T13:20:31-07:00","id":1133922,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, forgot about his Arcana and didn't see that. Good catch. I think we stick to RAW for that. <br /> <br /> With granting 5 XP post-character creation, i think it makes sense for all the characters to have been in the cabal for several months. Not an incredibly long time, but long enough to become initiated into Orders, indoctrinated into Legacies, learn the fundamentals of Supernal lore and magic, and carve out names for themselves in whichever way they want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T13:47:56-07:00","id":1133933,"title":"","content":"Well Cabal and being Awakened are not necessarily the same thing. So I take it we should only have been awakened for a few months? I guess I should adapt my background then. To be fair working as a Lictor while with a Cabal would probably have been stressful either way. Could just be a normal Factotum.<br /> <br /> If we've got an established cabal we should probably think about which of the rights we want to follow and if we want to use any of the cabal positions (hearthtender etc) and who to fill them with. That is if you guys want to use all that stuff from Sanctum and Sigil at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T03:54:34-07:00","id":1134106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1133933#post1133933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Cabal and being Awakened are not necessarily the same thing. So I take it we should only have been awakened for a few months? I guess I should adapt my background then. To be fair working as a Lictor while with a Cabal would probably have been stressful either way. Could just be a normal Factotum.<br /> <br /> If we've got an established cabal we should probably think about which of the rights we want to follow and if we want to use any of the cabal positions (hearthtender etc) and who to fill them with. That is if you guys want to use all that stuff from Sanctum and Sigil at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point, if you want your character to have been Awakened for more than a few months, I'm fine with that. I'm not saying there is a hard limit or something here, just trying to make a recommendation based on my best judgment of what seems to make sense to me. <br /> <br /> I have Sanctum and Sigil but I haven't looked through it in a long time. Anything in particular I should review that relates to cabals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T04:54:06-07:00","id":1134114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1134106#post1134106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good point, if you want your character to have been Awakened for more than a few months, I'm fine with that. I'm not saying there is a hard limit or something here, just trying to make a recommendation based on my best judgment of what seems to make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Lictorial training usually takes about a year and you wouldn't do it with a complete rookie either way. My char would just have spent more time refining his skills after awakening and dealing with personal issues than the other pcs perhaps. Or he is a late bloomer or something.<br /> <br /> The real question I suppose is wether you want to have a PC even be a Lictor. They're forbidden from taking apprentices or holding any sort of other official office, as they can be called in to arbitrate at the drop of a hat. So essentially he could get called in to work a state and a half away on the drop of a hat. Personally I think that'd make for a neat storyhook, but IC it means his cabal would need to be aware that he may leave suddenly now and then and it's rather unconditional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have Sanctum and Sigil but I haven't looked through it in a long time. Anything in particular I should review that relates to cabals? </div> </div> </div><br /> Cabal positions (p. 20) - basically just classical ways for the cabal to organize itself, not really necessary imo but could add some fluff (and as a thearch I guess my char should push for them to be established, they have hard on for all kinds of well established organization afterall).<br /> <br /> Protocols (p. 25) - basically another form of inter cabal organization. Essentially the cabal works out what they stand for and swear an oath (can be but is usually not a binding oath via the fate arcanum) to uphold these guidelines, turning the whole thing into an iron law. Can be especially important for thearchs who don't want to screw over their cabal. (SL usually doesn't ask thearchs to activly works against their cabal, but pumps them for information about them. They won't ask them to break the law to do so however....Not widely known outside the order though)<br /> <br /> as part of the Protocols - the great Rights (p. 26) - This is arguably the most important sections. Details the 5 great rights of cabals (which are golden laws, so trump any other regulations that have been established by a consilium or something of the like). The cabal has to choose which of these rights they want to upholds. It entails a right of crossing (establishes a way of crossing the cabals territory for other mages), the right of Emeritus (those that have earned the cabals respect are expected get it in return - the most often disregarded right I think, since it kind of gives the cabal a responsibility to act in certain way to people deserving respect... its actually quite complex, best read it for yourself), RIght of Hospitality (the duty to grant hospitality to those who ask it), Right of Nemesis (basically the awakened war option), RIght of Sanctuary (Sancta are involatile and should not be violated).<br /> <br /> Cabals can choose not to uphold certain of the rights, but those who choose to ignore more than one, maybe two are usually regarded poorly. You also can't expect people to respect the sanctity of your own sanctum if your creed doesn't involve respecting theirs....<br /> <br /> Sigils (p. 34) - not super important, mostly fluff a cabal has a Sigil (or sigils even), mostly fluff","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 08-26-2017, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T16:37:23-07:00","id":1134297,"title":"","content":"I will choose a Legacy later, after I reach space 2. I changed my arcana to time three and dropped spirit 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","user":"wtaylorjr2001","date":". 08-26-2017, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T21:50:20-07:00","id":1135348,"title":"","content":"Ok, I think we are almost all about wrapped up with getting things ready. I had a lot of down time tonight to work on my character. I think the only thing I have left to do is my equipment.<br /> <br /> I haven't purchased the CoD: Hurt Locker book yet, but I did find an old pre-printed version of the equipment appendix that was sampled in a blog post, and it looks like they changed the Glock 17 to a 2-dot availability rating. Does anyone have the book and have access to the new stats they included for firearms?<br /> <br /> Last thing we need to do realy is just confirm the cabal rules, and discuss <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a>'s question about whether his character should be a Lictor. I'll try to review that stuff this weekend or sometime this week if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T02:18:13-07:00","id":1135375,"title":"","content":"I do and yes the Glock 17 is availability 2.<br /> <br /> As for the Cabal stuff I find that part of the game boring so if we must lets get it out of the way. As for him being a Lictor, that is up to him, just realize that a cabal has its ways of dealing with those that betray them even if it was demanded by their order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 08-30-2017, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T09:08:04-07:00","id":1135471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1135375#post1135375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Cabal stuff I find that part of the game boring so if we must lets get it out of the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally we don't have to deal with the positions and rights if that's not something that'll be important for the chronicle. But we should lay low some kind of code on how our cabal will operate/what obligations are to each other. I guess my inerest here specifically boils down to : I'm playing a lawyer :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for him being a Lictor, that is up to him, just realize that a cabal has its ways of dealing with those that betray them even if it was demanded by their order. </div> </div> </div>It's mostly a question of wether <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> thinks he can use this for fun storyhooks. It would give us an easy in on investigative stories within the mage community. Fluff wise I can do the same &quot;magic lawyer&quot; thing as a normal factotum. As for the latter part: That's more a problem with the Silver Ladder in general, but easily circumvented by taking secrecy or cabal support oaths (normals ones, not the magical ones), essentially making it law. The SL doesn't ask it's members to go against the law. Only thing you shouldn't do around him is break the Lex Magica in some definite way and expect him to be quiet about it. The punishment for corrupt Lictors is torture, followed up by execution and destruction of their soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T13:25:54-07:00","id":1135573,"title":"","content":"That is all and well and can be as simple as implied that we do it and with a wave of the had it is done. I games that I have played we have done all of the puff and pomp and it was for not because it never came up. The concillium has the rules already in place, to have to write them out again is ridiculous. Yes the fluff can be nice but to spend even more time before the game start just to hammer back and forth on this and that is not an attractive proposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T09:07:38-07:00","id":1136604,"title":"","content":"Quoted from the Supernal Suburbia OOC thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1136562#post1136562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From here on out, ephemeral entities only use Rank + Influence (if relevant) to their CoW dice pool. For contested rolls, such as for Numina, they will use Rank + whichever trait is most relevant (often Power or Resistance).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a short note from my experience on spirit clashes: If you want Spirits (and I think Werewolves use similar clash rules) to be scary and possibly relevant oponents for this campaing you may want to think about homeruling the clash rules for them. Otherwise a starting mage character can pretty simply shield himself from them. Keep in mind that a mage can very easily acquire +5 dice on a clash of wills (for improvised spells more like ~ +3 but that's still alot). So Marduk for example could just give the whole Cabal a Spirit shield that will protect them from Numina or physical attacks by spirits or Werewolves with a Clash dicepool of 10. Meanwhile a Spirit (think the same for Werwolves) would oppose that with a roll of.... 1-5 dice, usually 1-2, maybe 3 as high ranking entities are rare. In my own experience making spirits roll Rank + an appropriate attribute makes them more competitive, they're still at a huge disadvantage because they can't keep up with mages changing the rules or simply learning and manipulating their banes, or a myriad of other things, but at least a rank 5 entity using the blast numen on you is actually very scary instead of a nonissue now when it happens.<br /> <br /> Edit: Werewolves apparently commonly use Primal Urge + Renown, which isn't quite that bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 09-03-2017, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T16:14:05-07:00","id":1138739,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Has this game died before it even got started? If so just let us know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T22:35:12-07:00","id":1138808,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> - No, I'm still here and planning to run the game. My problem is that I've been crazy busy and have had severely limited availability to finalize everything before I'm ready to reboot the IC thread, due to work and personal obligations. <br /> <br /> There are a few specific things I need to complete before I can start up the game again. It looks like all of you are pretty much ready to go, but I need about an hour or two to sit down and sift through my old notes about the story, update NPC info, and integrate those so I can make a cohesive story for the new chapter. But I haven't been able to find that time in the past few weeks, either at home or at work.<br /> <br /> As long as you all are willing to wait it out a bit longer, I hope to have it up and running soon. I actually tried to stay up late a few nights ago and get things done, but I fell asleep early accidentally. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T05:39:35-07:00","id":1138860,"title":"","content":"No problem, I just hadn't heard anything and was just seeing if I was wasting time by checking the boards. I understand the pressures of work and I also have alot of work to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T05:57:04-07:00","id":1138863,"title":"","content":"I can definitely say that my gaming pace will be slower than some games. I will probably be able to post about every 3 days, and would like players to post at least once per week. I'll do everything I can to post more frequently than that, but I can't promise it based on how everything has been going for me lately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T14:30:50-07:00","id":1139000,"title":"","content":"I think it'd be good if we got started soonish, since too much time passing between char creation and actual play can cause players (and storytellers) to loose their investment into the game. That said don't stress yourself, it's fine if the pace isn't the quickest <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T18:08:54-07:00","id":1139595,"title":"","content":"Good news: I had some downtime this weekend to sit and do some planning about the story, so I have some cool ideas of how to create some conflict to keep everything interesting. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> - I reviewed the Silver Ladder book, and you can be a Lictor if you like. If it becomes a problem from a story perspective or causes too many issues, we can find fair workarounds.<br /> <br /> The last thing that needs to happen before we can get IC up and running is for me to review your NPC info that everyone mentioned in your backstories (if relevant) and update the NPC info as it relates to the initial chapter. I will try to do that this week, sooner rather than later!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T14:48:50-07:00","id":1139774,"title":"","content":"I'll keep the Lictorial status around then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The NPCs should be up to date. One thing I don't think is on his sheet is that I'd like for him to get involved with the Silver Ladder efforts to help sleepers deal with their accidential visits to the shadow. This is something I'd like to come to be in play however, not part of his background as of yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T20:48:20-07:00","id":1140075,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> - Hey everyone! I'm excited to say that I have finally been able to put the rest of the work into getting our game up and running! Thank you all SO much for being patient with me this past month.<br /> <br /> There are some posting and dice rolling conventions that I use in my PbP games that I'd like us all to use:<br /> <br /> <b>IC posts: </b>When you make in-character posts, please include a header at the top of each post with your character's status (e.g., current HP and Willpower, active spells under your control, conditions). Please make sure to update this header with each new post you make. Your HP, WP, mana, etc. in each post should reflect your status at the time of that post. So for example, if you roll to contain Paradox and take bashing damage, your HP in that header should capture your new HP with that bashing damage. For any OOC information like rolls, questions, etc., please include that in your post using the [spoiler] bbcode tag.<br /> <br /> <b>Spellcasting: </b>This is especially important for creative thaumaturgy, but in general, please make sure to clearly state your spell factors, assigned reach, etc. when describing your spells and including rolls. Keep this in the [spoiler] tag. See <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1129781#post1129781\">here</a> for an example of how this looks; you can choose your own formatting, please just include these details in some way.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice rolls:</b> Whenever you need to roll dice, please include a link in your post to an online dice roller that archives previous rolls with permanent links, preferably <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/?action=roll\" target=\"_blank\">Orokos</a>. It can elegantly roll for d10 dice games, with most rolls using a template of &quot;Xd10h8&quot;, where X = number of dice in your pool and &quot;h8&quot; means that you get successes on 8 or higher. By default, this rolling code will use the 10-again quality, so make sure to roll using &quot;Xd10o9h8&quot; for 9-again, &quot;Xd10o8h8&quot; for 8-again, etc. Chance die pools use Xd10h10. In some cases, I will make rolls for you to save posting time; these will usually include Clash of Wills and Initiative.<br /> <br /> <b>Action pacing: </b>When we are not in a formal initiative count, time is fluid; you can take non-reflexive actions in your posts without needing to track things like exact casting time (so feel free to use multiple Yantra for the same spell to cast with a higher dice pool, like High Speech chanting and a Path tool, even if your spellcasting would extend more than a round or two). You can even include a few actions in the same post, if relevant, but try not to overdo it.<br /> <br /> <b>Post pacing:</b> I use pretty relaxed posting expectations. Please try to respond to IC posts that involve you within a week of time in real life. I try to reply to all posts as the Storyteller within 3 days of your post, when ST action or response is required. If you expect to have limited availability for an extended period of time, please let me know. If everyone is pretty active and posting more frequently, then I'll try to pick up my ST post pace accordingly.<br /> <br /> <b>Consecutive rolls: </b>If you're in a tense or time-limited situation, you can make consecutive attempts on a mundane or spellcasting roll but at -1 penalty for each consecutive attempt. However, you don't get penalized for rolls that are free of time pressure.<br /> <br /> If the spell is instant cast and does not risk Paradox, and the dice pool is above 0, I'd like you to at least roll it on the dice roller once. If it fails, you can choose to <b>&quot;take 1&quot;</b> -- basically assume you eventually cast it with 1 success, or keep rerolling if preferred. If the spell is cast as a ritual, I'd like you to roll each time; you'll take -1 consecutive rolls on the ritual because it takes up time, so there's time pressure and implications of failing the roll. For spells that risk Paradox, I'd like you to roll each attempt because of the cumulative bonuses to the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> Spells that fit multiple categories above use both sets of rules. So for example, instant-cast spells that risk Paradox will have the additional +1 Paradox per roll, but no cumulative -1 penalty to the roll itself. Ritual-cast spells that risk Paradox will have cumulative -1 penalty to the spell casting roll and +1 Paradox.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage armor and dodging:</b> To save time for posting, whenever you are attacked and take damage and have the option to activate Mage Armor reflexively (i.e., you still have at least 1 mana left and haven't reached your max mana use per turn), you can choose to active Mage Armor retroactively and apply it to the attack that was already rolled. Similarly, if you haven't taken your turn in a combat situation and are attacked, you can choose to dodge reflexively and make your roll retroactively. Mage Armor that adds to your defense applies <b>before</b> doubling for dodging rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Modifying rolls: </b>When you make a roll, if you are unsure of the correct adjustment for penalties/bonuses, make your roll without them and I will modify accordingly. If I need to subtract dice, I will take them off your roll results in backwards order. If I need to add to your dice pool, I'll roll additional dice and add the successes to your previous total.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think that's everything for now! Please post here if you have questions/concerns. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Now that the thread is up and running, I hope to be able to keep things moving at a faster clip. Sorry again for the delay in starting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 09-13-2017, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T12:56:56-07:00","id":1140290,"title":"","content":"I'm excited to start! Anything I should know about Victory?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1140075#post1140075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[<br /> I will make rolls for you to save posting time; these will usually include Clash of Wills and Initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate that, as it's kind of annoying when the game gets suspended for a week just so everyone slowly makes a post in which they only roll their initiative. Just keep in mind that clashes of wills can be bolstered by wp, so players might want to do that retroactivly if you roll the CoW for them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T05:56:35-07:00","id":1141034,"title":"","content":"Doctor Luck wasn't lucky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T06:02:46-07:00","id":1141036,"title":"","content":"Indeed. I think you may have messed the timescale in your post, the cabal was supposed to be meeting at 10am iirc, so as it stands Dr. Luck would be late by multiple hours.<br /> <br /> (Also can you exceed the gnosis derived yantra limit when doing ritual casting?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T06:58:21-07:00","id":1141053,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> - There are a few errors in your post. <br /> <br /> You made your spell rolls as if you still have Gnosis 3, back with your original character before we rebooted the game. At Gnosis 2, your ritual casting time interval is 3 hours and you only can use up to 2 Yantras. So you only have time for about one ritual spell before the group leaves.<br /> <br /> In addition, even if you had enough time to cast multiple ritual spell attempts, per our game rules and conventions above, you would suffer a consecutive -1 on each roll.<br /> <br /> Because you have 2 free reach, and you only used one, I recommend you just use another for an instant cast spell and use the &quot;take 1&quot; rule as needed.<br /> <br /> In regards to your actual spell, I might have missed this, but please clarify which boon you are selecting. Are you granting yourself a certain number of 9-again rolls? Bonus to your dice pools? Or some combination?<br /> <br /> Finally, I still need a perception roll from you (Wits + Composure).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T08:27:23-07:00","id":1141073,"title":"","content":"I corrected several of these issues. Doctor Luck gets up at 4 in the morning to practice spell casting and to write. His writing was cut short and he left to meet up with the cabal at 10 am. He uses ritual casting and failed twice. He succeeded with the instant casting. I added the wits + composure roll also. I reread the post and corrected it this morning fixing almost all of the problems. I used 2 Yantras, Shadow name and a dedicated tool, my silver walking stick.I missed the -1 per extra roll so I will redo it. The spell itself is two conditions and 3 +5 to mundane rolls. Got to go to mass fix when I get back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T09:26:59-07:00","id":1141089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wtaylorjr2001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1141073#post1141073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I corrected several of these issues. Doctor Luck gets up at 4 in the morning to practice spell casting and to write. His writing was cut short and he left to meet up with the cabal at 10 am. He uses ritual casting and failed twice. He succeeded with the instant casting. I added the wits + composure roll also. I reread the post and corrected it this morning fixing almost all of the problems. I used 2 Yantras, Shadow name and a dedicated tool, my silver walking stick.I missed the -1 per extra roll so I will redo it. The spell itself is two conditions and 3 +5 to mundane rolls. Got to go to mass fix when I get back.</div> </div> </div> </div>High Speech is also a Yantra.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Gnosis (2) + Fate (3) + Shadow Name (3) + Dedicated Tool (1) + High Speech (2) - Spell Factors (6) = 5 Dice<br /> <br /> Also you must name the skill that you are getting the =5 to<br /> <br /> Grant a dice bonus equal to Potency on certain actions<br /> (<b>usually a single Skill</b>) for a number of rolls equal to the<br /> Potency of the spell during its Duration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T11:51:03-07:00","id":1141144,"title":"","content":"&quot;Also you must name the skill that you are getting the =5 to&quot;<br /> <br /> The subject\u2019s player chooses which<br /> of his rolls are affected by this boon before rolling the dice.<br /> I can choose which skills to use it on before I roll the dice.<br /> <br /> New dice rolls<br /> <br /> Gnosis (2) + Fate (3) + Shadow Name (+3) + High Speech (2) - Spell Factors (-6) = 4 Dice<br /> <br /> I forgot High Speech was a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Reach = Advanced Duration and Instant Casting.<br /> I would like to use the take 1 rule.<br /> <br /> Thank you all for your comments.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T11:54:53-07:00","id":1141150,"title":"","content":"What that means is that the Boon doesn't get spent the first (x) times you use the Skill in a roll, you decide if you use it or not before rolling. You still need to choose the Skill at the moment of casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T12:05:48-07:00","id":1141156,"title":"","content":"I stand corrected, thanks. Brawl, Occult, and Expression (writing) are the skills I choose to make lucky heh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T02:07:06-07:00","id":1141690,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to add some clarification here because this came up a while ago in my other game. You almost have it right, but not quite there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The wording is complicated, but when using Exceptional Luck, you need to treat Potency of the <b>spell</b> and Potency of the <b>boon/hex</b> as two related but separate stats. Anything that references spell potency is based on the full potency, which can be allocated to different bonuses such that the total potency of the boons equals the spell's potency.<br /> <br /> Your total spell Potency is 5, with Duration of 1 day. That means you can &quot;mix and match&quot; up to 5 boon effects: 9-again on any 1 mundane roll (which does not need to be specified until you choose to use it), +1 bonus to a specific skill for a number of rolls equal to the <i>spell</i> Potency, or 1 condition.<br /> <br /> You chose Charmed and Steadfast, and split the remaining 3 boon Potency between 3 skills. So you will get <b>+1</b> (not +5) on each of 5 Brawl, Occult, and Expression rolls. You can choose when to apply the bonuses, but must decide before any roll, and they only last until the end of the day.<br /> <br /> If you prefer, you could also pick a single skill (say, Occult for example) and make it a +3 boon, which will apply on any 5 Occult rolls of your choosing before the spell ends. You would still have your Charmed and Steadfast conditions.<br /> <br /> Does that make more sense?<br /> <br /> I messaged <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> to see if he is still with us, I'm hoping he remains interested despite the delay in the game starting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T02:18:08-07:00","id":1141692,"title":"","content":"If that is how you play it then that is how it will be played, but that isn't how it is stated in the book. And no I am not trying to debate the issue as I said that it how you play it then that is how it will be played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T03:16:40-07:00","id":1141697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1141692#post1141692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that is how you play it then that is how it will be played, but that isn't how it is stated in the book. And no I am not trying to debate the issue as I said that it how you play it then that is how it will be played.</div> </div> </div> </div>My intention is to play it per RAW, and I thought that I correctly referenced and clarified the rules from the core book. Can you explain why you think I'm wrong, and maybe give an example or reference of how it should work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T03:38:02-07:00","id":1141702,"title":"","content":"I understand the confusion, the definition of Boons and Hexes is poorly worded. I do read it as rwknoll, where you have the overall Potency of the spell (say, 5) wich determines certain aspects of the Hex or Boon (Penalty in the case of Hex, Number of rolls affected in the case of Boon) while the Potency you asign to each of the effects determines the rest of the variables (Number of rolls affected for Hexes, Bonus to the rolls of a single Skill for Boons) while the dice tricks (9-again or 8-again) and Tilts just need a flat 1 Potency asign to them to work.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You can tell, because the sidebar at the begining of Fate describing how Boons and Hexes work mentions Potency of the Spell and Potency of the Hex/Boon as different things in the same paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 09-19-2017, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T13:15:39-07:00","id":1141867,"title":"","content":"What is the primary spell factor of the hex/boon? Do we get this ...the player may<br /> move the primary factor up its chart a number of steps equal to<br /> the character\u2019s rating in the spell\u2019s highest Arcanum minus one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T14:07:30-07:00","id":1141889,"title":"","content":"For Exceptional Luck, it is Potency, so you have a base Potency equal to your Fate dots even before applying penalties to increase it further. That mean, though, that the spell only lasts a meager turn before running out unless you take penalties or add Reach to increase the Duration factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T14:43:37-07:00","id":1141904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wtaylorjr2001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1141867#post1141867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the primary spell factor of the hex/boon? Do we get this ...the player may<br /> move the primary factor up its chart a number of steps equal to<br /> the character\u2019s rating in the spell\u2019s highest Arcanum minus one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, the boon/hex itself does not have a primary spell factor. That pertains only to the spell itself that creates the boon. <br /> <br /> So just to reiterate: The Potency of your Exceptional Luck spell is increased by your Arcana dots per normal rules, and Duration of the spell is 1 turn by default unless you make it longer. When your spell succeeds, you can mix and match the following to &quot;spend&quot; your spell Potency. <br /> <br /> For each 1 boon Potency, gain the following:<br /> - A beneficial condition<br /> - A use of 9-again (or 8-again with reach)<br /> - +1 for a specific skill for a number of rolls equal to the spell's total Potency<br /> <br /> All bonuses end when resolved or used, or when the spell itself expires, whichever comes first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T15:00:11-07:00","id":1141911,"title":"","content":"OK then I would like to make it +3 to occult for 3 rolls please. Thanks for clearing this up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T01:18:37-07:00","id":1142067,"title":"","content":"Grant a dice bonus equal to <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Potency</b></span> (Potency 5 so +5) on certain actions<br /> (usually a single Skill) for a number of rolls equal to the<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Potency</b></span> (Potency 5 so 5 rolls) of the spell during its Duration. Multiple boons<br /> cannot grant their bonus to the same action; only the<br /> highest bonus counts. The subject\u2019s player chooses which<br /> of his rolls are affected by this boon before rolling the dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> No where in there does it say that the potency (5 in the example) is divided among the number of rolls equal to potency, it specifically states that you get potency for a number of rolls equal to potency. Like I said I am not here to debate the rule you have made your choice and we will need to live with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T02:51:33-07:00","id":1142079,"title":"","content":"Well personally I'd say that it's reasonable to substract the potency spent on conditions or dicetricks, so I'd personally read/handle it as &quot;+3 to 3 rolls of one ability or +3 to 2 of one ability and +3 to one of another etc&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a><br /> <br /> My character has activated a Space 1 spell that lets him see through any obstacles. Is there anything of note inside the house he would notice at a quick glance? If there are any people inside he'd also quickly flash his magesight on them.<br /> <br /> Also I recently wrote a Spirit based investigation spell for another mage game and would like to hear if you think that one would be ok to use. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1138248#post1138248\">Here</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 09-20-2017, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T19:32:43-07:00","id":1142785,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> - So Thorbes' point/example illustrates exactly what I was trying to explain. On p. 134 for example, it says that &quot;The mage may also mix and match the above effects using Potency. So, a Potency 4 hex allows the mage to levy a penalty on the subject\u2019s next two actions, as well as apply the Blinded and Leg Wrack Tilts.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Potency 4 hex could do any of the following:<br /> (1) Apply -4 penalty to all mundane actions for a total of 4 rolls<br /> (2) Apply 4 negative tilts (either existing ones in the book, or custom tilts)<br /> <br /> Notice that in the example above, when you mix and match, the Potency of the hex affects the number of actions affected: a Potency 2 hex levies a penalty on the subject's next <b>two</b> actions, and another Potency 2 hex applies <b>two</b> tilts. A spell with total Potency 4 can create both of these effects.<br /> <br /> Similarly, a Potency 4 boon could do any of the following:<br /> (1) Grant 9-again on 4 mundane dice rolls<br /> (2) Grant +4 bonus on number of dice rolls equal to <b>spell potency</b> (i.e., 4) for a single action<br /> (3) Grant 4 beneficial conditions<br /> <br /> When you mix and match, you split up the spell's total Potency into multiple boons, each with their own Potency rating. So a spell with total Potency 4 could allow you to gain a Potency 2 boon that grants 9-again on <b>2</b> dice rolls, as well as a separate Potency 2 boon that grants a <b>+2</b> bonus on <b>4</b> dice rolls for a single action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> - I totally misread what that spell does, sorry. I thought of it as giving you an &quot;aerial&quot; kind of vision, but didn't realize that it lets you see inside the house, too. I'll edit my post with more info for you.<br /> <br /> Regarding that spell you are asking about. I like the idea, but I want to make sure I understand exactly what it does. I'm sure it's clearly written already, I'm just kind of tired at the minute. So say you cast it on a forest fire, which is Resonant for fire Essence. Would that allow you to inherently know that, for example, a lazy camper flicked his cigarette butt into the grass, or that someone poured an accelerant on the flame to make it grow faster?<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a spell that lets you understand what actions led to the Resonance developing. However, I don't know if I like either Reach option you listed. A Death spell could reveal the presence of the Anchor condition, for example, but I don't think it can tell you which ghosts have received Essence from that Anchor or know their ban/bane just by studying the Anchor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T19:58:36-07:00","id":1142790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=1142785#post1142785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;12802&quot;]<br /> <br /> Regarding that spell you are asking about. I like the idea, but I want to make sure I understand exactly what it does. I'm sure it's clearly written already, I'm just kind of tired at the minute. So say you cast it on a forest fire, which is Resonant for fire Essence. Would that allow you to inherently know that, for example, a lazy camper flicked his cigarette butt into the grass, or that someone poured an accelerant on the flame to make it grow faster?<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a spell that lets you understand what actions led to the Resonance developing. However, I don't know if I like either Reach option you listed. A Death spell could reveal the presence of the Anchor condition, for example, but I don't think it can tell you which ghosts have received Essence from that Anchor or know their ban/bane just by studying the Anchor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't particularily mind you not liking the reach effects. They were just something that occured to me could make sense, but I see that they can be problematic. Most important to me is the base effect.<br /> <br /> Now as to that effect: It shows you what caused the resonance in a particular area, but I think your example is a tricky one. If someone caused a fire in a forest by accident that is an act that does not cast a particularily strong &quot;shadow&quot; and thus creates essence. The fire resulting from it of course produces alot of fire essence, so targetting said fire essence would mostly reveal... well lots of forest fire. A deliberatly caused forest fire however could have a resonance linked to greed, hate, perverse fixiation or whatever motivation caused the arsonist to lay the fire. If an intrepid shaman notices this subtle difference (the ratio of fire to emotion could easily make it hard to notice in this case, probably forcing some sort of perception roll) then he could investigate the emotional context with the spell, potentially seeing the act of arson (however of course through the lens of the shadow, so the arsonist looks more like a spiritual relfection of his actions than his actual self, leading to further complications...).<br /> <br /> A bit of an easier example may be a dead woman found in an apartment, her corpse resonant with death and decay, the area resonant with violence, rage, fear and regret. With this spell each of those resonances could be probed to their source, giving flashes of a heated argument (rage) between a man with red, steaming skin and a women with the tongue of a serpent and green ichor drooling from her mouth bound together by silken bonds, the man striking the woman down with a gigantic larger than life trophy trailing fire (violence/death), the man, shrunken and bluegree in colour, with bulging eyes and shaking, blood staining his hands and tears his eyes standing over the corpse, choked by the bonds that bound them together (regret/fear).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T02:15:37-07:00","id":1143180,"title":"","content":"My apologies I have had an unusually hectic week at work and I will try to get something up in the IC today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T19:22:57-07:00","id":1145951,"title":"","content":"Posting to see what's going on with everyone.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> - Still looking to see if you have anything you wanted to add or post in the IC thread.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> - Feel free to post again or respond to the other information other players have posted since your most recent entry.<br /> <br /> I believe we have lost <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> unfortunately, at least for the meantime, as he hasn't logged in for over a month. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Is there anything that anyone is waiting on input from me as the Storyteller before you're posting? Just want to make sure I'm not missing something on my end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theony